{"id": "adr-001", "question": "Can I still start a new project using the CQRS-with-Hasura approach from ADR0001?", "lang": "en", "category": "yes-no", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0001_cqrs_with_hasura.md"], "expected_keywords": ["Deprecated", "2025-06-01", "Hasura"], "expected_answer": "No. ADR0001 is deprecated as of 2025-06-01: Hasura is no longer part of the company-approved technology stack for new developments, so the ADR must not be adopted for new projects.", "notes": "Status section", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "adr-002", "question": "Nell'approccio CQRS descritto in ADR0001, come sono strutturate le Annotation Tables e con quale vincolo di scrittura?", "lang": "it", "category": "definition", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0001_cqrs_with_hasura.md"], "expected_keywords": ["commands", "responses", "Timescale"], "expected_answer": "Ogni comando (o famiglia di comandi) è rappresentato da due Annotation Tables in PostgreSQL, `commands` e `responses`, che sono INSERT ONLY e partizionate per tempo (ad esempio con Timescale) per garantire prestazioni I/O lineari.", "notes": "Decision + Notes/Implementation > Annotation Tables", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "adr-003", "question": "What are the data store service tiers defined in ADR0002 and what does each one guarantee?", "lang": "en", "category": "list", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0002_data_store_tiers.md"], "expected_keywords": ["Tier 3", "Source of Truth", "Volatile Cache"], "expected_answer": "ADR0002 defines five tiers: Tier 3 Business Critical (data must always be available), Tier 4 Source of Truth (data must not be lost), Tier 5 Expensive Cache (data should be restored), Tier 6 Commercial Cache (data can be reconstructed) and Tier 7 Volatile Cache (data can be lost). The ADR itself is marked deprecated / no longer relevant.", "notes": "Decision section", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "adr-004", "question": "How long can a rebuild outage last for a cheap-to-rebuild cache versus a throwaway volatile cache before it counts as business discontinuity, according to the data store tiers ADR?", "lang": "en", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0002_data_store_tiers.md"], "expected_keywords": ["24h", "7d"], "expected_answer": "For Tier 6 (data can be reconstructed, not expensive to rebuild) an important downtime while rebuilding of up to 24h must not cause business discontinuity; for Tier 7 (volatile cache, data can be lost) the window is up to 7d.", "notes": "Notes/Implementation > Tier 6 and Tier 7 requirements", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "adr-005", "question": "Sotto quale chiave JWT vengono salvati gli scoped claims dell'Enveloped Access Token di OnePlatform, e questa ADR è ancora valida?", "lang": "it", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0003_application_token_envelope.md"], "expected_keywords": ["https://teamsystem.com/one-platform/jwt/claims", "2025-04-14"], "expected_answer": "Gli scoped claims sono memorizzati sotto la chiave `https://teamsystem.com/one-platform/jwt/claims`. ADR0003 è però deprecata dal 2025-04-14 perché si riferisce alla vecchia login app, ormai deprecata.", "notes": "Status + Notes/Implementation", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "adr-006", "question": "Which programming languages have official CloudEvents SDKs, per the Cloud Events adoption ADR?", "lang": "en", "category": "list", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0004_use_of_cloud_events.md"], "expected_keywords": ["PowerShell", "Rust", "Ruby"], "expected_answer": "CloudEvents provides SDKs for Go, JavaScript, Java, C#, Ruby, PHP, PowerShell, Rust and Python. ADR0004 (accepted) adopts CloudEvents for the events that transit through Hermes.", "notes": "Decision section", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "adr-007", "question": "Nel vecchio formato log JSON di ADR0005, quali valori può assumere il campo retention.period e cosa significano?", "lang": "it", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0005_well_known_log_type.md"], "expected_keywords": ["keep forever", "10 years", "retention.period"], "expected_answer": "retention.period è una keyword con valori a = keep forever, b = six months, c = 1 year, d = 10 years; è obbligatorio quando retention.status è true. ADR0005 è comunque outdated dal 2025-02-08 e rimanda ad ADR0011.", "notes": "Decision table, last rows", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "adr-008", "question": "How should I name a virtual machine on Azure North Europe for the demo environment following the old cloud naming convention (ADR0006)?", "lang": "en", "category": "procedural", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0006_cloud_naming_tag_convention.md"], "expected_keywords": ["vm-ts010-az-ne-demo-0027", "incremental from 0000"], "expected_answer": "The pattern is vm-[app name code]-[cloud provider aws|az]-[dev|test|demo|prod]-[2-letter location, e.g. ne for North Europe]-[incremental number from 0000], for example vm-ts010-az-ne-demo-0027 for Alyante. Note that ADR0006 is outdated as of 2022-06-28 and ADR0018 holds the current tagging convention.", "notes": "Naming convention > VM", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "adr-009", "question": "What naming convention did ADR0007 prescribe for M2M authenticated-only tokens, and is that ADR still in force?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0007_m2m_authenticated_only_tokens.md"], "expected_keywords": ["UUIDv4", "ADR0010", "2025-05-21"], "expected_answer": "Token names were a UUIDv4 (also the token uid) concatenated with a brief human-readable service name suffix, e.g. b67edc97-44f8-4b6a-886f-f57eaaa91af1-ACCOUNTING-ASYNC-SCHEDULER, and each calling service should own exactly one token. ADR0007 is deprecated as of 2025-05-21; ADR0010 is the current M2M/client credentials approach.", "notes": "Status + Decision", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "adr-010", "question": "Why did TeamSystem pick Kappa over Lambda architecture for Hermes?", "lang": "en", "category": "comparison", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0008_hermes_architecture.md"], "expected_keywords": ["Kappa", "Lambda", "single stream processing pipeline"], "expected_answer": "Lambda keeps separate batch and stream pipelines, which adds complexity, latency, operational overhead and inconsistency risk; Kappa processes everything as a single continuous stream (a single stream processing pipeline), giving real-time processing, horizontal scalability, easier reprocessing by replaying the event log and better adaptability. ADR0008 is accepted.", "notes": "Issue + Considered Alternatives", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "adr-011", "question": "Con l'architettura Kappa di Hermes dobbiamo conservare tutto lo storico dei dati dentro Kafka?", "lang": "it", "category": "yes-no", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0008_hermes_architecture.md"], "expected_keywords": ["persistence window", "data lake"], "expected_answer": "No. Nel nostro contesto la Kappa Architecture non implica mantenere l'intero dataset storico in Kafka: si mantiene una persistence window sufficientemente ampia e, se serve un reprocessing, i dati possono essere ricaricati dal data lake senza trasformazioni.", "notes": "Key Concepts > Data reprocessing and backfill", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "adr-012", "question": "When should an API return 401 versus 403 in the client credentials model of ADR0010?", "lang": "en", "category": "comparison", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0010_client_credentials.md"], "expected_keywords": ["401 Unauthorized", "403 Forbidden"], "expected_answer": "401 Unauthorized is returned when the token is invalid, missing or expired (authentication failure at the PEP), optionally with a WWW-Authenticate challenge; 403 Forbidden is returned when the token is valid but the central Policy Authorizer (PDP) denies the request for insufficient permissions.", "notes": "Perspective of the Called Service > Error Handling", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "adr-013", "question": "Quali controlli deve fare un servizio chiamato per validare un JWT emesso da TSID prima di passare all'autorizzazione?", "lang": "it", "category": "list", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0010_client_credentials.md"], "expected_keywords": ["JWKS", "RFC 7519", "aud"], "expected_answer": "Secondo ADR0010 il servizio (PEP) valida il JWT secondo RFC 7519 e OAuth 2.0: verifica la firma con le chiavi pubbliche TSID ottenute dall'endpoint JWKS (e messe in cache), il claim iss (issuer TSID), il claim aud (deve includere l'identificativo del servizio), la scadenza exp e opzionalmente nbf. Se la validazione fallisce risponde 401 senza procedere all'autorizzazione.", "notes": "Perspective of the Called Service > Token Validation", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "adr-014", "question": "Is ADR0011 on the well-known JSON log format still the standard to follow?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0011_well_known_log_type.md"], "expected_keywords": ["2026-05-22", "ADR0020"], "expected_answer": "No. ADR0011 is deprecated as of 2026-05-22 and superseded by ADR0020 (OpenTelemetry Semantic Attributes for Platform Context); it is kept only as historical documentation for services still emitting the legacy JSON log schema during migration.", "notes": "Status section", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "adr-015", "question": "Quali protezioni sono obbligatorie per una funzione serverless esposta su internet?", "lang": "it", "category": "list", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0012_serverless_protection_guidelines.md"], "expected_keywords": ["WAF", "Rate Limiting", "concurrency"], "expected_answer": "ADR0012 impone tre controlli: un limite massimo di concurrency (o un meccanismo equivalente di cap sui costi) allineato al picco legittimo più un buffer, il rate limiting a livello di API Gateway, load balancer o servizio, e la protezione dietro un WAF capace di mitigare attacchi come SQLi, XSS e HTTP flood.", "notes": "Decision section", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "adr-016", "question": "Which npm registry should our projects point their .npmrc to now that the namespace-specific registries are being retired?", "lang": "en", "category": "procedural", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0013_centralized_npm_repository.md"], "expected_keywords": ["ts-platform-npm", "https://npm.ts-platform.com/", ".npmrc"], "expected_answer": "ADR0013 adopts a single unified registry, ts-platform-npm, reachable at https://npm.ts-platform.com/; every repository's .npmrc must reference only it and drop namespace-specific entries (e.g. @1f, @fortawesome). Legacy registries are decommissioned three months after full adoption.", "notes": "Decision + Implications", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "adr-017", "question": "For a new Business Capability API, what is the default pagination style and which standard must PATCH requests follow?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0014_business_capability_standardization.md"], "expected_keywords": ["cursor-based", "JSON Merge Patch", "RFC 7396"], "expected_answer": "Pagination must be cursor-based by default (offset-based only in specific non-critical cases), and partial updates use PATCH with JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7396), while PUT is used for full replacement.", "notes": "Decision > MUST > API style", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "adr-018", "question": "Qual è lo stato di ADR0014 sulla standardizzazione delle Business Capability?", "lang": "it", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0014_business_capability_standardization.md"], "expected_keywords": ["Jun 1st, 2026"], "expected_answer": "ADR0014 è marcata come 'To be re-evaluated after Jun 1st, 2026'. Funge da indice della baseline MUST/SHOULD per le Business Capability, rimandando alle ADR dedicate (ADR0004, ADR0011, ADR0015, ADR0016).", "notes": "Status + Notes", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "adr-019", "question": "Are we allowed to version a new REST API with a query parameter like ?api-version=2?", "lang": "en", "category": "yes-no", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0015_rest_api_versioning.md"], "expected_keywords": ["MUST NOT", "api-version", "legacy"], "expected_answer": "No. ADR0015 says query-string versioning is strongly discouraged and MUST NOT be used for new APIs; existing APIs using it are legacy and should migrate to path-based versioning (/{capability}/v{major}/...), which is the platform standard. Header versioning (X-Api-Version) is allowed only in justified cases with architecture approval.", "notes": "Versioning Models > 3. Version in query string", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "adr-020", "question": "Quando rilasciamo una nuova major di un'API, quanto dura la finestra di transizione tipica e cosa deve rispondere la vecchia versione dopo la data di Sunset?", "lang": "it", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0015_rest_api_versioning.md"], "expected_keywords": ["12 months", "3 months", "410 Gone"], "expected_answer": "ADR0015 prevede un parallel run di 12 months, comunicazione 3 months prima del Sunset e un grace period di 1 month dopo il Sunset per le emergenze. Le risposte della vecchia versione portano gli header Deprecation e Sunset e, dopo la data di Sunset, l'API deve rispondere 410 Gone (es. codice API_VERSION_EOL).", "notes": "Lifecycle Communication + Typical Transition Window", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "adr-021", "question": "What content type and mandatory fields must every 4xx/5xx error response of a platform API have?", "lang": "en", "category": "definition", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0016_error_handling_RFC_9457.md"], "expected_keywords": ["application/problem+json", "RFC 9457"], "expected_answer": "Per ADR0016 all 4xx/5xx responses must use Content-Type application/problem+json (Problem Details, RFC 9457) and always include the core fields type, title, status and detail, plus instance preferably as an absolute URI; the JSON status must mirror the HTTP status code.", "notes": "Decision > MUST", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "adr-022", "question": "In a validation error payload, how should each entry in errors[] point to the offending field?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0016_error_handling_RFC_9457.md"], "expected_keywords": ["JSON Pointer", "RFC 6901"], "expected_answer": "Each errors[] entry should include at least path, code and message, where path is a JSON Pointer (RFC 6901) to the failing property, e.g. /items/0/quantity, code is a stable string such as required, min, format or unique, and message is human-readable.", "notes": "Decision > SHOULD; Contract for errors[]", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "adr-023", "question": "How do our old correlationId and requestId map onto the W3C traceparent header?", "lang": "en", "category": "comparison", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0017_trace-context.md"], "expected_keywords": ["trace-id", "parent-id", "correlationId"], "expected_answer": "correlationId (generated once by the client and shared across services) corresponds to the traceparent trace-id, representing the whole end-to-end transaction; requestId (generated by each service for downstream calls) corresponds to parent-id, a single span regenerated at each hop.", "notes": "Logical Mapping table", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "adr-024", "question": "Da dove deve partire il rollout della migrazione da X-Correlation-Id/X-Request-Id agli header W3C Trace Context?", "lang": "it", "category": "procedural", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0017_trace-context.md"], "expected_keywords": ["edge components", "API gateways", "traceparent"], "expected_answer": "Secondo ADR0017 il rollout deve partire dagli edge components (API gateways, ingress point) che generano e propagano traceparent; i servizi downstream vengono aggiornati progressivamente per consumare e propagare i nuovi header, supportando entrambi i tipi di header (legacy e W3C) fino al termine della migrazione, dopo cui gli header legacy vengono deprecati.", "notes": "Migration Strategy > 3. Gradual Service Adoption", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "adr-025", "question": "Where do I find the valid values for the business_capability cloud tag, and what is the component tag for?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0018_cloud_tagging_business_capability.md"], "expected_keywords": ["Development Portal Catalog", "business_capability", "component"], "expected_answer": "The business_capability value must match one of the names in the Name column of the Development Portal Catalog (https://development.teamsystem.com/catalog) and is the primary key for allocating cloud costs. component is an optional free-form label chosen by the owning development team to subdivide costs within a single Business Capability.", "notes": "Decision > Updated mandatory tags", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "adr-026", "question": "What trace sampling strategy does the OpenTelemetry adoption ADR mandate, and where is it applied?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0019_opentelemetry_adoption.md"], "expected_keywords": ["tail-based", "Collector", "head-based"], "expected_answer": "ADR0019 adopts tail-based sampling at the company-managed OpenTelemetry Collector as the default, with policies retaining error, slow and critical-flow traces (100% of error traces and traces above latency thresholds); head-based sampling in SDKs may be used only as an additional cost-control mechanism where justified.", "notes": "Decision + Sampling Strategy", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "adr-027", "question": "Quali attributi sono obbligatori sulla telemetria OpenTelemetry inviata al collector di piattaforma?", "lang": "it", "category": "list", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0019_opentelemetry_adoption.md"], "expected_keywords": ["deployment.environment", "service.name"], "expected_answer": "ADR0019 richiede team (identificativo del team proprietario, usato come tenancy key per visibilità e controllo accessi), deployment.environment (dev | test | prod) e service.name (nome logico del servizio). Opzionali: service.namespace, service.instance.id e correlation_id legacy.", "notes": "Required Attributes", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "adr-028", "question": "Under ADR0020, from which sources should user.id, workspace.id and item.id be populated on spans and logs?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0020_opentelemetry_semantic_attributes.md"], "expected_keywords": ["X-Workspace-ID", "X-Item-ID", "sub"], "expected_answer": "user.id comes from the sub claim of the authenticated TSID JWT (never emit the token itself), workspace.id from the X-Workspace-ID HTTP header and item.id from the X-Item-ID header; header-derived values should be validated before being treated as authoritative, values are strings and are required when available.", "notes": "Decision table + SHOULD", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "adr-029", "question": "In quali casi un data product può fare a meno dell'output port su Hermes?", "lang": "it", "category": "list", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0021_hermes_as_the_default_output_port_for_data_products.md"], "expected_keywords": ["corporate data", "consumer-aligned", "Optional"], "expected_answer": "Secondo ADR0021 l'output port su Hermes è obbligatorio per ogni data product tranne quando il data product riguarda corporate data (es. finance e sales interni, non integrati in OnePlatform) oppure è consumer-aligned (es. ML/insights che calcolano KPI, pensati per accessi OLAP): in questi casi è Optional.", "notes": "Decision + summary table", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "adr-030", "question": "Why does ADR0022 steer Invoice Trading toward Hermes but Customer Hub toward Databricks, even though both consumers are applications?", "lang": "en", "category": "comparison", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0022_data_product_consumption_guidelines.md"], "expected_keywords": ["ITR", "Customer Hub", "Databricks"], "expected_answer": "ITR consumes invoice-level data enriched with eligibility calculations that is reusable by other capabilities and it wants decoupling from schema changes, so Hermes is preferred. Customer Hub consumes pre-aggregated customer data for a single dashboard with OLAP-style access and no other expected subscribers, so Databricks fits better. The ADR concludes consumer type alone is not sufficient; the criteria (decoupling, integration complexity, read performance, reusability) must be applied together.", "notes": "Positions section", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "adr-031", "question": "If an app gets a clientId and clientSecret through Runtime Enrollment, does that already give it access to protected resources?", "lang": "en", "category": "yes-no", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0023_runtime_enrollment_client_credentials.md"], "expected_keywords": ["add-permission", "Policy Manager", "Digital Technical Keys"], "expected_answer": "No. Runtime Enrollment only creates a technical identity; neither the clientSecret nor the access token grants permissions. Access depends exclusively on policies associated with the clientId in Policy Manager via the Identity Profile add-permission APIs, and assigning them requires an identity with administrative permissions on the company (Item), such as Digital Technical Keys.", "notes": "Decision + Constraints", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "adr-032", "question": "Come vengono comunicate ai team R&D le decisioni ufficiali dei comitati di piattaforma e in che ordine di canali?", "lang": "it", "category": "procedural", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["adr:repo-oneplatform-adrs-platform-cascading-official-decisions"], "expected_keywords": ["Development Portal", "Teams", "read-only"], "expected_answer": "L'ADR (in stato Proposed dal 2026-01-23) prevede: 1) una pagina per decisione sul Development Portal come single source of truth, 2) un annuncio breve su un canale Teams ufficiale R&D-wide read-only con link alla pagina, 3) cascata alle persone tramite PO ed Engineering Manager, più opzionalmente una newsletter mensile di piattaforma e una email mirata a PO/EM per gli item urgenti.", "notes": "Positions > Cascade channels", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "adr-033", "question": "What are the workflow states an ADR goes through in the Biosphere ADR repository?", "lang": "en", "category": "list", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["adr:repo-oneplatform-adrs-readme"], "expected_keywords": ["In Core Review", "In Extended Review", "Superseded"], "expected_answer": "The states are Draft, In Core Review, In Extended Review, Approved, Superseded and Deprecated. In both the top-down (Core Architects) and bottom-up (teams via their Engineering Manager opening a merge request) workflows the ADR passes Core Architects review, is published to Confluence and the Developer Portal, goes to the Extended Architects review, and is finally presented in the Architecture Review meeting for visibility only.", "notes": "ADR Workflows section", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "adr-034", "question": "Which log fields did the updated well-known log format (ADR0011) add compared with the original ADR0005 schema?", "lang": "en", "category": "multi-hop", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0005_well_known_log_type.md", "gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0011_well_known_log_type.md"], "expected_keywords": ["client.name", "request.id", "event.action"], "expected_answer": "ADR0011 kept the ADR0005 fields and added client.name, client.version, customer.workspace_id, customer.item_id, customer.manager_id, request.id, event.action, http.request.user_agent and error.code, each with a source (e.g. http header x-workspace-id, x-request-id, JWT sub). ADR0005 is outdated as of 2025-02-08 in favour of ADR0011, which in turn is deprecated (2026-05-22) in favour of ADR0020.", "notes": "Compare Decision tables of ADR0005 and ADR0011 (bold fields are new)", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "adr-035", "question": "Un client creato via Runtime Enrollment deve seguire regole di autorizzazione diverse rispetto ai client M2M classici registrati su TSID?", "lang": "it", "category": "multi-hop", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0010_client_credentials.md", "gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0023_runtime_enrollment_client_credentials.md"], "expected_keywords": ["Runtime Enrollment", "Policy Manager", "client_credentials"], "expected_answer": "No. ADR0023 è un'estensione di ADR0010 e non introduce un nuovo modello: l'identità ottenuta con Runtime Enrollment si autentica con OAuth2 client_credentials su TSID esattamente come ogni altro client M2M, il servizio chiamato agisce da PEP validando il JWT e interrogando il Policy Authorizer (PDP), e l'autorizzazione dipende solo dalle policy assegnate al clientId nel Policy Manager (401 se il token non è valido, 403 se manca l'autorizzazione).", "notes": "ADR0023 Notes + ADR0010 Called Service perspective", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "adr-036", "question": "Which of the original cloud resource tags were dropped by the business capability tagging update, and which ones still apply?", "lang": "en", "category": "multi-hop", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0006_cloud_naming_tag_convention.md", "gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0018_cloud_tagging_business_capability.md"], "expected_keywords": ["business_capability", "tfmanaged", "ref_po"], "expected_answer": "ADR0018 removes the domain and service tags from ADR0006 and replaces them with business_capability (mandatory, matching the Development Portal Catalog) and component (optional). The other ADR0006 tags (env, ref_po, ref_tech, tfmanaged, app_name, technology) and the naming conventions remain valid; ADR0018 supersedes only that tag subset.", "notes": "ADR0006 Decision > Tags; ADR0018 Decision + Notes", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "adr-037", "question": "How does the OpenTelemetry adoption relate to the earlier decision to replace X-Request-Id and X-Correlation-Id?", "lang": "en", "category": "multi-hop", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0017_trace-context.md", "gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0019_opentelemetry_adoption.md"], "expected_keywords": ["default propagator", "traceparent", "OpenTelemetry"], "expected_answer": "ADR0017 replaces the custom X-Request-Id/X-Correlation-Id headers with W3C Trace Context (traceparent mandatory, tracestate optional) through a gradual dual-header migration. ADR0019 builds on it: OpenTelemetry uses W3C Trace Context as its default propagator, so adopting OTel SDKs with OTLP and the company Collector is consistent with ADR0017, which remains the reference for header propagation rules; legacy headers must still be supported during the transition.", "notes": "ADR0017 Decision; ADR0019 Argument > Context Propagation and Notes", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "adr-038", "question": "Perché i data product devono pubblicare di default su Hermes, e che ruolo ha Hermes nell'architettura dati aziendale?", "lang": "it", "category": "multi-hop", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0008_hermes_architecture.md", "gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0021_hermes_as_the_default_output_port_for_data_products.md"], "expected_keywords": ["Kappa", "output port", "Hermes"], "expected_answer": "ADR0008 definisce Hermes come hub Kafka di una Kappa Architecture: un commit log immutabile e single source of truth usato sia per l'integrazione operativa tra applicazioni sia per alimentare i data product analitici. Coerentemente ADR0021 rende obbligatorio un output port su Hermes per ogni data product (eccetto corporate data e consumer-aligned), raccomandando che la tabella OLAP su Databricks legga dal topic Hermes stesso, così da riusare un unico flusso di offloading e favorire l'adozione di OnePlatform e le integrazioni asincrone.", "notes": "ADR0008 Key Concepts; ADR0021 Decision + Assumptions", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "mc-001", "question": "Which commercial identity product is TS ID v3 built on top of?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "manually-curated", "expected_source_ids": ["manually-curated:manually-curated-oneplatform-glossary-full"], "expected_keywords": ["Duende IdentityServer", "Auth0"], "expected_answer": "TS ID v3 is built on Duende IdentityServer (v6), the commercial OIDC/OAuth2 product. Auth0 was only the PoC alternative, not Duende.", "notes": "Canonical Register > Identity & Access", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "mc-002", "question": "How does the on-prem to cloud integration bus differ from Hermes, and what proxy does it use?", "lang": "en", "category": "comparison", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "manually-curated", "expected_source_ids": ["manually-curated:manually-curated-oneplatform-glossary-full"], "expected_keywords": ["Integration Hub", "Girino", "point-to-point"], "expected_answer": "The Integration Hub is a separate point-to-point on-prem to cloud integration bus that goes through the Girino proxy. It is not a Hermes version: Hermes 2 is the Kafka/Confluent CloudEvents streaming platform and Hermes 1 the legacy Azure Service Bus streaming.", "notes": "Canonical Register > Streaming & Integration; Confusables > Generation pairs", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "mc-003", "question": "Se un utente scrive semplicemente 'CIC', posso espanderlo automaticamente in Cassa in Cloud?", "lang": "it", "category": "yes-no", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "manually-curated", "expected_source_ids": ["manually-curated:manually-curated-oneplatform-glossary-full"], "expected_keywords": ["CIC", "Contabilità in Cloud", "Commercialisti in Cloud"], "expected_answer": "No. CIC è ambiguo e non va mai auto-espanso: i claimant sono Cassa in Cloud (contesto POS), Contabilità in Cloud (contesto contabile, con la variante legacy CiC Reviso), Commercialisti in Cloud (studi) e il fittizio Coffee In Cloud degli esempi ICE. Va disambiguato dal contesto; solo FIC, DIC e COMIC hanno espansioni sicure.", "notes": "Resolution Index > Abbreviations & acronyms", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "mc-004", "question": "What are the three signature levels offered by TeamSystem Signature and what do the acronyms stand for?", "lang": "en", "category": "list", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "manually-curated", "expected_source_ids": ["manually-curated:manually-curated-oneplatform-glossary-full"], "expected_keywords": ["FEQ", "Firma Elettronica Qualificata", "FES"], "expected_answer": "TeamSystem Signature has three ascending tiers of one product: FES (Firma Elettronica Semplice, simple), FEA (Firma Elettronica Avanzata, advanced) and FEQ (Firma Elettronica Qualificata, qualified, with 1Shot / Triennale / Automatica variants and eIDAS legal value equivalent to a handwritten signature).", "notes": "Confusables > Construction & Trust Services acronyms", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "mc-005", "question": "Is DWH the same thing as the Warehouse capability in the OnePlatform vocabulary?", "lang": "en", "category": "comparison", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "manually-curated", "expected_source_ids": ["manually-curated:manually-curated-oneplatform-glossary-full"], "expected_keywords": ["Data Warehouse", "WMS", "L7 Data"], "expected_answer": "No. DWH means Data Warehouse (analytics/BI, part of the L7 Data capability), whereas Warehouse / WMS is physical SCM warehousing. Same root word, opposite domains, never merge them.", "notes": "Definition never-merge cues; Resolution Index; Common Misconceptions", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "mc-006", "question": "In the Contratto Unico, if the General Terms, the Order, the MDPA and the Supplementary Terms conflict, which document wins over which?", "lang": "en", "category": "list", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "manually-curated", "expected_source_ids": ["manually-curated:manually-curated-oneplatform-glossary-full"], "expected_keywords": ["MDPA", "Supplementary Terms", "Order"], "expected_answer": "The internal order of prevalence is: (i) the MDPA, (ii) the Order, (iii) the Supplementary Terms (Condizioni Integrative), (iv) the General Terms (Condizioni Generali). The Order also prevails over the General and Supplementary Terms per its own definition.", "notes": "Commercial / Legal Register > Condizioni Generali Definizioni, entry 12 'Contratto' (CG Art. 1 par. 1.2)", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "mc-007", "question": "How much advance notice must TeamSystem give a customer when it withdraws a product from the market, and what is the notice called?", "lang": "en", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "manually-curated", "expected_source_ids": ["manually-curated:manually-curated-oneplatform-glossary-full"], "expected_keywords": ["six months", "Comunicazione di Ritiro", "Replacement Service"], "expected_answer": "The Comunicazione di Ritiro (Withdrawal Notice) is a written notice, also by email, with at least six months' notice, by which TeamSystem informs the Customer it intends to withdraw one or more Products/Services from the market; it must describe any Replacement Service that will replace each Obsolete Service.", "notes": "Commercial / Legal Register > Condizioni Generali Definizioni, entry 9", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "mc-008", "question": "Prosystem è ancora un prodotto a sé oppure è cambiato nome? Di che tipo di suite si tratta?", "lang": "it", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "manually-curated", "expected_source_ids": ["manually-curated:manually-curated-oneplatform-glossary-full"], "expected_keywords": ["Giada", "Prosystem", "CAF"], "expected_answer": "Prosystem è il nome precedente di Giada (CAF Giada): è un alias, non un prodotto distinto. Giada è la suite fiscale per i CAF (730, REDDITI, 770, ISEE, IMU).", "notes": "Confusables > Products - the catalog families ('Giada (formerly Prosystem)'); Generation pairs 'CAF suite'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "mc-009", "question": "The acronym SFA shows up both in TSE Industry 4.0 material and in CRM material — does it mean the same thing in both?", "lang": "en", "category": "comparison", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "manually-curated", "expected_source_ids": ["manually-curated:manually-curated-oneplatform-glossary-full"], "expected_keywords": ["Shop Floor Analytics", "Sales Force Automation", "SFA"], "expected_answer": "No. SFA is context-dependent and must never be auto-expanded: in the manufacturing / TSE Industry 4.0 context it means Shop Floor Analytics (official brochure), in a CRM context it means Sales Force Automation (maintainer ruling).", "notes": "Confusables > Acronym collisions; Common Misconceptions", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "mc-010", "question": "Under the contract definition of Assistenza, can TeamSystem support staff intervene directly on the customer's own IT systems?", "lang": "en", "category": "yes-no", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "manually-curated", "expected_source_ids": ["manually-curated:manually-curated-oneplatform-glossary-full"], "expected_keywords": ["Assistenza", "expressly excluded", "Assistance"], "expected_answer": "No. Assistenza (rendered Assistance, never bare 'Support') is the technical-support service that suggests to the Customer, on request and where possible, technical solutions for correct use of the Services; any direct intervention on the IT systems of the Customer, Subsidiaries or Third-Party Beneficiaries is expressly excluded.", "notes": "Commercial / Legal Register > Condizioni Generali Definizioni, entry 4", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "mc-011", "question": "Onto which cloud target do the legacy Alyante, Active and ACG ERPs converge in TeamSystem's internal adoption register?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "manually-curated", "expected_source_ids": ["manually-curated:manually-curated-teamsystem-product-catalog"], "expected_keywords": ["TSE V12 Cloud", "Alyante", "ACG"], "expected_answer": "The Alyante / Active / ACG ERPs, all marked Legacy (L), converge onto TSE V12 Cloud, marked Target (T), in the internal Area register's Legacy to Target line.", "notes": "Internal Area register (Legacy -> Target)", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "mc-012", "question": "How many engineering Areas does TeamSystem's internal adoption register use to group the product portfolio, and what lifecycle flags does it assign to each module?", "lang": "en", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "manually-curated", "expected_source_ids": ["manually-curated:manually-curated-teamsystem-product-catalog"], "expected_keywords": ["Micro ERP", "Trust & Cybersecurity", "Business Capability (BC)"], "expected_answer": "The register groups the portfolio into 15 engineering Areas (Architecture & Engineering, CAF, Construction, Data, Digital Finance, E-Procurement, Enterprise, Extended CRM, HRS, Legal, Micro ERP, Micro Vertical, Platform, Professionals, Trust & Cybersecurity) and marks each module Legacy (L), Target (T) or Business Capability (BC).", "notes": "Internal Area register (Legacy -> Target)", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "mc-013", "question": "Be Amazing è un software TeamSystem per commercialisti?", "lang": "it", "category": "yes-no", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "manually-curated", "expected_source_ids": ["manually-curated:manually-curated-teamsystem-product-catalog"], "expected_keywords": ["Be Amazing", "partnership program", "Commercialisti"], "expected_answer": "No. Be Amazing compare nel verticale Commercialisti (tax studios) del catalogo ma è un partnership program, non un prodotto software, a differenza di TeamSystem Studio Cloud, Studio AI, ViaLibera, Digital Box e Studio HR.", "notes": "Portfolio by market vertical > Commercialisti", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "mc-014", "question": "Are TeamSystem Waste and TeamSystem Waste 360 the same product, and who is each aimed at?", "lang": "en", "category": "comparison", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "manually-curated", "expected_source_ids": ["manually-curated:manually-curated-teamsystem-product-catalog"], "expected_keywords": ["RENTRI", "ARERA", "Utilities"], "expected_answer": "No, they are two distinct products (maintainer decision of 2026-07-23, superseding the earlier 'one product' ruling). TeamSystem Waste is special-waste compliance (RENTRI/FIR/MUD, formerly named AIC) for waste producers, transporters, intermediaries and consultants; TeamSystem Waste 360 is ARERA-compliant integrated environmental-service management for the Utilities market.", "notes": "Naming & confusables > 'TeamSystem Waste vs. TeamSystem Waste 360'. NB: the high-level glossary still states 'Waste 360 = Waste, one product' (stale).", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "mc-015", "question": "A quale Area e a quale target del registro interno vengono ricondotti gli strumenti LogicalSoft come Termolog e Travilog?", "lang": "it", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "manually-curated", "expected_source_ids": ["manually-curated:manually-curated-teamsystem-product-catalog"], "expected_keywords": ["Termolog", "Architecture & Engineering", "LogicalSoft"], "expected_answer": "Gli strumenti di ingegneria LogicalSoft (Termolog / Schedulog / Travilog), tutti marcati Legacy (L), sono mappati sui target Business Capability (BC) dell'Area Architecture & Engineering.", "notes": "Internal Area register (Legacy -> Target)", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "mc-016", "question": "What does TeamSystem mean by treating OnePlatform as 'Platform as a Product', and what is the platform's standard acronym?", "lang": "en", "category": "multi-hop", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "manually-curated", "expected_source_ids": ["manually-curated:manually-curated-oneplatform-manifesto", "manually-curated:manually-curated-oneplatform-glossary-high-level"], "expected_keywords": ["Platform as a Product", "1P", "non-functional requirements"], "expected_answer": "'Platform as a Product' means the platform is TeamSystem's first and foremost product, serving all others in the portfolio, built to achieve economies of scale and guarantee non-functional requirements, and developed with the concentration and care each product deserves. The platform's standard acronym is 1P (as in 1P Audit Log), and bare 'TS Digital' is its legal/contract name.", "notes": "Manifesto intro + Essential Glossary 'OnePlatform (1P)' entry", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "mc-017", "question": "Quale principio del Manifesto OnePlatform parla di pratiche di green software engineering e di riduzione del debito tecnico?", "lang": "it", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "manually-curated", "expected_source_ids": ["manually-curated:manually-curated-oneplatform-manifesto"], "expected_keywords": ["Sustainable", "green software", "technical debt"], "expected_answer": "Il principio 4, 'Sustainable': la sostenibilità tecnica e operativa serve a ridurre il debito tecnico, mantenere l'efficienza, abbassare costi e consumi, e promuove pratiche di green software engineering per minimizzare l'impatto ambientale.", "notes": "Manifesto > 4. Sustainable", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "mc-018", "question": "Secondo il manifesto della piattaforma, come si riduce la necessità di assistenza tecnica diretta agli utenti?", "lang": "it", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "manually-curated", "expected_source_ids": ["manually-curated:manually-curated-oneplatform-manifesto"], "expected_keywords": ["Self Service", "self-service support", "documentation"], "expected_answer": "Con il principio 'Self Service': gli utenti devono poter configurare e usare i servizi senza dipendere da interventi esterni; tramite documentazione dettagliata e supporto self-service si riduce il bisogno di assistenza tecnica diretta, guidando gli utenti con regole chiare e best practice.", "notes": "Manifesto > 5. Self Service", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "mc-019", "question": "Which OnePlatform manifesto principle relies on Continuous Discovery, and what is it meant to achieve?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "manually-curated", "expected_source_ids": ["manually-curated:manually-curated-oneplatform-manifesto"], "expected_keywords": ["Future-proof", "Continuous Discovery", "consolidated technologies"], "expected_answer": "The 'Future-proof' principle: the platform adopts modern but consolidated technologies for solid long-term foundations and uses Continuous Discovery practices to anticipate market trends and user needs, so it stays relevant and keeps creating value over time.", "notes": "Manifesto > 3. Future-proof", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "mc-020", "question": "What do OnePlatform services get automatically from Biosphere?", "lang": "en", "category": "list", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "manually-curated", "expected_source_ids": ["manually-curated:manually-curated-oneplatform-design-principles"], "expected_keywords": ["Biosphere", "Static code analysis", "secret manager"], "expected_answer": "Through Biosphere, 1P services automatically benefit from static code analysis, infrastructure-as-code, a centralized secret manager and an infrastructure policy manager, as part of the 'Cybersecurity and Privacy by Design' principle.", "notes": "R&D Principles > 2. Cybersecurity and Privacy by Design", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "mc-021", "question": "Nei principi R&D di OnePlatform, chi gestisce i penetration test e come viene certificato il retest?", "lang": "it", "category": "procedural", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "manually-curated", "expected_source_ids": ["manually-curated:manually-curated-oneplatform-design-principles"], "expected_keywords": ["WAPT", "Security Engineering", "external entity"], "expected_answer": "I processi di penetration testing (WAPT) sono gestiti da Security Engineering, con una doppia certificazione WAPT (retest) effettuata tramite un ente esterno; l'integrazione avviene solo tramite canali autorizzati (API Gateway, Integration Hub) e firewall governato da policy, con formazione OWASP continua per gli sviluppatori.", "notes": "R&D Principles > 2. Cybersecurity and Privacy by Design > Security Engineering", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "mc-022", "question": "How many R&D principles govern how OnePlatform is built, and into which two groups are they split?", "lang": "en", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "manually-curated", "expected_source_ids": ["manually-curated:manually-curated-oneplatform-design-principles"], "expected_keywords": ["eight", "Technical Principles", "Functional Principles"], "expected_answer": "There are eight principles, grouped into Technical Principles (how the platform is engineered: Once only, Cybersecurity and Privacy by Design, Collaborative platforms talking through APIs, Native SaaS/Multitenant/Multicloud/Mobile enabled) and Functional Principles (how it serves customers and the business: Digital first / AI embedded, Design to cost/onboard/retain/maintain, Engagement in SW, Enhance collaboration between stakeholders).", "notes": "R&D Principles intro and section headings", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "mc-023", "question": "Quali servizi core della piattaforma sono obbligatori per ogni applicazione e in quale layer della CityMap si trovano?", "lang": "it", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "manually-curated", "expected_source_ids": ["manually-curated:manually-curated-oneplatform-glossary-high-level"], "expected_keywords": ["TS ID", "Workspace", "mandatory"], "expected_answer": "TS ID e Workspace sono obbligatori per ogni applicazione. Fanno parte del gruppo Foundation dei Core Services, che si trovano al Layer 3 (L3) della CityMap a otto layer.", "notes": "Essential Glossary > Core Services (Layer 3); CityMap at a Glance", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "mc-024", "question": "Into which groups are the Layer 3 Core Services organized, and what sits in the Monetization group?", "lang": "en", "category": "list", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "manually-curated", "expected_source_ids": ["manually-curated:manually-curated-oneplatform-glossary-high-level"], "expected_keywords": ["six groups", "TouchX", "Licensing"], "expected_answer": "Core Services are organized in six groups: Foundation, Experience, TouchX, Monetization, AI and Support. The Monetization group holds Provisioning, Trial, User Telemetry, Metering, Licensing and Engagement in SW.", "notes": "Essential Glossary > Core Services (Layer 3); Layer 3 table", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-001", "question": "In the OnePlatform Reference Implementation, how do the two business capabilities talk to each other and what does the second one do when it gets a message?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:CTO:1079836744"], "expected_keywords": ["Hermes", "running total", "BC2"], "expected_answer": "BC1 reacts to an explicit user action (e.g. a button click) and publishes a domain event through Hermes, which is the only communication mechanism between the two capabilities. BC2 is fully decoupled and only reacts to events: on receipt it updates a persistent running total saved in a database and exposes it via an API consumed by the frontend.", "notes": "Requirements section", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-002", "question": "Which core services does the Enablement team walk through during the First Blood meeting of a new onboarding?", "lang": "en", "category": "list", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:CTO:594313417"], "expected_keywords": ["Company Registry", "IntegrationHUB", "Policy Manager"], "expected_answer": "The core services walkthrough covers Company Registry, Workspace, Connection Service, IAM TeamSystemID, IAM Policy Manager, NCS, IntegrationHUB, Hermes and API Gateway.", "notes": "First Blood phase, item 2.5", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-003", "question": "What data-sharing problems were identified for Cassa in Cloud when adopting the Workspace model, and which one is the shared virtual wallet about?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:CTO:646807813"], "expected_keywords": ["wallet", "Franchisor"], "expected_answer": "Three potential issues: sharing data between workspaces of different companies with a single owner and multiple readers (a franchisor sharing article definitions with franchisees); sharing data between workspaces of different companies in read and write mode, which is the wallet use case where an end customer has a shared virtual wallet usable in stores of different companies; and segregating data for users of the same company based on the store they belong to (store managers not seeing each other's customers and suppliers).", "notes": "Potential Issues in Workspace adoption", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-004", "question": "Quali servizi di piattaforma sono obbligatori quando si integra un prodotto esistente con approccio low effort secondo il manifesto delle Business Capability?", "lang": "it", "category": "list", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:CTO:657950007"], "expected_keywords": ["1Front", "Policy Manager", "Metering"], "expected_answer": "L'integrazione low effort deve almeno usare i servizi obbligatori della piattaforma: TSID, Workspace / Registry, 1Front, Hermes, Metering e Policy Manager. Il modello dati e di processo originale viene adattato senza stravolgerlo e sono accettabili compromessi sulla UX.", "notes": "Use Cases in Capability Realization, case 2 Low Effort Integration", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-005", "question": "Is a Business Capability allowed to depend directly on another Business Capability?", "lang": "en", "category": "yes-no", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:CTO:657950007"], "expected_keywords": ["Platform Capabilities", "Hermes"], "expected_answer": "No. Business Capabilities must not have direct dependencies on other Business Capabilities; the only allowed dependencies are towards Platform Capabilities (integration, identity, data services). Any interaction between capabilities must be mediated by the platform's integration components such as Hermes pub/sub, point-to-point integrations (iHub, HoReCa, Mesh) and the internal ServiceRegistry/NamingService.", "notes": "Common Characteristics of Capabilities", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-006", "question": "What are the three kinds of rules or profiles that live inside the Policy Manager, according to the From Product to Capability deck?", "lang": "en", "category": "list", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:CTO:647498120"], "expected_keywords": ["System Rules", "Domain Rules", "User Profiles"], "expected_answer": "The Policy Manager distinguishes System Rules (centrally defined platform-wide policies, e.g. checking a feature is licensed or that a firm can manage a company's data via connections), Domain Rules (defined by each Business Capability owner for its own service, e.g. the PO defining the Timesheet reporting access rule) and User Profiles (rules assigned directly by users, BC owners or sysadmins via self-service tools).", "notes": "Business Capabilities Authorization - Policy", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-007", "question": "Quali pattern sono stati usati per scomporre il monolite di Fatture in Cloud (FiC) in capability?", "lang": "it", "category": "list", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:CTO:647498120"], "expected_keywords": ["Bounded Context", "Strangler Fig", "Canary Releases"], "expected_answer": "Il monolite FiC (tradeitems, invoicing, warehouse, csl) è stato suddiviso applicando il principio del Bounded Context per identificare contesti autonomi, poi migrato gradualmente con lo Strangler Fig Pattern, in cui le nuove capability (Tradeitems, Warehouse, Pricelist...) sostituiscono progressivamente le funzionalità del monolite reindirizzando il traffico, in combinazione con Canary Releases che introducono ogni capability a una piccola percentuale di clienti.", "notes": "An example: FiC use case", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-008", "question": "Can an existing commercial offer be modified after release, for example to add a feature to it?", "lang": "en", "category": "yes-no", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:CTO:918487120"], "expected_keywords": ["immutable", "a new offer"], "expected_answer": "No. Commercial offers are immutable: if something changes, a new offer is created and the existing one is not modified; the license is then upgraded on the clients who should receive (or lose) the new feature. Each offer is defined by a YAML manifest, the list of BCs via URN and a commercial configuration such as COMIC2025/COMIC2026.", "notes": "1.3 Commercial Offers", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-009", "question": "Nella proposta di release management, qual è il modello di rilascio previsto per una Business Capability e quando è ammessa una versione congelata?", "lang": "it", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:CTO:918487120"], "expected_keywords": ["Rolling Release", "Release Candidate", "frozen"], "expected_answer": "Il modello è il Rolling Release (default e fortemente raccomandato), con una sola versione Stable e una Release Candidate (RC) che servono solo come punto di controllo verso le offerte commerciali. Una versione frozen è ammessa solo come eccezione controllata ed esclusivamente nel perimetro applicativo: la piattaforma non supporta migrazioni dati né garantisce consistenza se la migrazione ha impatti cross-capability. Il versioning delle BC è scoraggiato.", "notes": "1.2 Business Capability (BC)", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-010", "question": "How many layers does the current TeamSystem CityMap have, and is it the same as the version shown in the September 2025 strategy deck?", "lang": "en", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:manually-curated-citymap-teamsystem-authoritative"], "expected_keywords": ["eight bands", "7-band"], "expected_answer": "The authoritative 2026-07 CityMap has eight bands, numbered L8 (Commercial Offering, top) down to L1 (SW Lifecycle, bottom): Commercial Offering, Business Capabilities, AI Agents, Integration, Data, Core Services, Infrastructure and SW Lifecycle. It supersedes the condensed 7-band rendering used in slide 7 of the 2025-09-10 From Product to Capability deck.", "notes": "Provenance note + The eight bands", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-011", "question": "How do I compute the user id to send to Gainsight PX in the identify call?", "lang": "en", "category": "procedural", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:confluence-gp-gp-644284658-gainsight-px-integration-guidelines"], "expected_keywords": ["SHA-256", "TSID"], "expected_answer": "The user id must be the SHA-256 hash of the TSID user code, converted to lowercase and trimmed before hashing (e.g. echo -n \"<tsid>\" | sha256sum). If users do not log in with TSID, another stable unique id must be hashed, for example <userId>_tsx for TSX users, so that it cannot collide with ids from other apps.", "notes": "2.2.2.1 User ID Calculation", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-012", "question": "Se lo stesso utente lavora su due aziende diverse, Gainsight PX tiene traccia di entrambi gli account? Come va gestito il caso?", "lang": "it", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:confluence-gp-gp-644284658-gainsight-px-integration-guidelines"], "expected_keywords": ["Gainsight PX", "custom property", "last account"], "expected_answer": "No: in Gainsight PX le informazioni di account vengono sovrascritte, quindi se lo stesso utente opera per due aziende viene conservato solo l'ultimo account associato alla sua attività. Per distinguere le azioni sulle diverse aziende bisogna aggiungere a ogni evento una custom property che identifichi il contesto aziendale.", "notes": "Important Disclaimer on Gainsight PX Behavior", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-013", "question": "In the One Back Office user profiling model, what is a permission set and what happens when a user holds two permission sets of the same category?", "lang": "en", "category": "definition", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:OBO:1044119755"], "expected_keywords": ["permission set", "highest-level"], "expected_answer": "A permission set is a collection of one or more policies (each policy belongs to only one permission set), characterized by a mandatory level and an optional category. A user can have several permission sets, even from different categories, but for each category only the highest-level permission set assigned is active: if a user with level 2 receives level 3, level 2 is superseded. Higher levels inherit the permissions of lower levels.", "notes": "3. Entity - PERMISSION SET / LEVELS AND CATEGORIES", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-014", "question": "Today, how is a user recognized as enabled for the OnePlatform backoffice, and which rego function should my module's policies call to check it instead of re-implementing the logic?", "lang": "en", "category": "multi-hop", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:OBO:1440841863", "confluence:OBO:1044119755"], "expected_keywords": ["BACKOFFICE:ADMIN", "is_backoffice_operator"], "expected_answer": "AS-IS a user is enabled for the backoffice if they have the registry role BACKOFFICE:ADMIN; the TO-BE is a dedicated Policy Manager attribute (PM-side implementation still to do). Integrating modules should not replicate profiling logic but use the general rego policy function data.platform.backoffice.v1.is_backoffice_operator to verify whether the user is a Backoffice operator.", "notes": "ICE guideline Step 2.1 Access gate; Profiling module section 7", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-015", "question": "Come devo nominare e modellare le policy del mio modulo ICE per il backoffice, e cosa deve fare il BFF se il Policy Manager non risponde?", "lang": "it", "category": "procedural", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:OBO:1440841863"], "expected_keywords": ["billing.invoice.view", "fail-closed"], "expected_answer": "Vale la regola una azione → una policy, modellata con Identity/Action/Resource/Context (I-A-R-C) e registrata nel catalogo del Policy Manager nel perimetro del modulo, con convenzione <domain>.<feature>.<action> (es. billing.invoice.view, billing.invoice.manage) e metadati per la discoverability. A runtime il BFF/back-end invoca il Policy Manager Authorizer per ogni azione protetta con fallback fail-closed: in caso di errore del PM (503) l'accesso viene negato. L'enforcement resta server-side, il FE si limita a mostrare/nascondere componenti.", "notes": "Step 2.2 e 2.3", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-016", "question": "Cos'è la Family nel Metering e in che formato va scritto il suo nome?", "lang": "it", "category": "definition", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:confluence-mpdd-mpdd-1587380572-1-1-i-tre-attori-bc-family-bbs"], "expected_keywords": ["Family", "BBS"], "expected_answer": "La Family è il nome tecnico dell'offerta commerciale nel Metering: è il ponte tra BBS e Metering, perché BBS inserisce quel nome nel pacchetto e Metering lo legge per sapere quali feature attivare e con quali limiti. Il formato è UPPERCASE_WITH_UNDERSCORE, ad esempio FATTURAZIONE_PRO. In M3 evolverà nel concetto di Commercial Offer componibile tramite Capability Catalog.", "notes": "The Family: the technical name of your offer", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-017", "question": "In the M3 Capability Catalog, which conditions must a business capability satisfy before it can be included in a commercial offer?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:confluence-mpdd-mpdd-1586561282-1-2-una-capability-tante-feature"], "expected_keywords": ["published", "monetization_ready", "Capability Catalog"], "expected_answer": "Only capabilities with status published and monetization_ready: true can enter commercial offers. In M3 every BC has an identity card in the Capability Catalog with its features, limitable dimensions and usage events, and the enrollment process becomes formal and governed (today BCs are registered informally with no centralized catalog).", "notes": "M3 Direction box", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-018", "question": "Devo creare un pacchetto FIC attivato a livello di workspace per la family FIC_PREMIUM_PLUS: quale versione della Subscription API uso e cosa metto nel campo name?", "lang": "it", "category": "multi-hop", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:confluence-mpdd-mpdd-1217429956-creazione-pacchetti-fic-api-subscription", "confluence:confluence-mpdd-mpdd-1586987315-1-3-i-due-canali-bbs-e-store-fic"], "expected_keywords": ["V3", "FICPREMIUMPLUS", "underscore"], "expected_answer": "Per l'attivazione su WorkspaceID si usa la Subscription V3 dell'agyo-subscription-api (la V2 usa l'ItemID). Nel body il campo name va popolato senza underscore anche se la family lo prevede: per FIC_PREMIUM_PLUS il name è FICPREMIUMPLUS, mentre il campo family mantiene l'underscore.", "notes": "FIC package creation page: V2 vs V3 + mapping Family → Name; 1.3 channel comparison (Workspace Flow = Subscription V3, name without underscores)", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-019", "question": "What is the difference between synchronous and asynchronous consumption counting in Metering, and when should each be used?", "lang": "en", "category": "comparison", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:confluence-mpdd-mpdd-1587216639-1-4-i-cicli-di-vita-commerciale-e-a-consumo"], "expected_keywords": ["Slot-based", "Queued", "COOLDOWN"], "expected_answer": "Synchronous (slot-based) counting means the BC asks Metering before acting: a slot is LOCKED, the BC executes, then confirms (USED) or cancels (FREE); slots go to COOLDOWN and return FREE after 6 months. It is for small numbers and critical actions that must never exceed the limit (signature certificates, user enablement, company management). Asynchronous (queued) counting means the BC acts first and notifies Metering afterwards via message bus, aggregated into daily buckets without real-time blocking; it is for massive volumes such as invoices issued, electronic submissions, API calls and documents.", "notes": "The two counting modes", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-020", "question": "Quando un cliente raggiunge la soglia del constraint, che differenza c'è tra il comportamento readonly e l'overage lato webhook e stato del pacchetto?", "lang": "it", "category": "comparison", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:confluence-mpdd-mpdd-1587216639-1-4-i-cicli-di-vita-commerciale-e-a-consumo"], "expected_keywords": ["overage", "READONLY", "No webhook"], "expected_answer": "Con il comportamento Block/Readonly Metering invia alla BC il webhook ENABLE_READONLY_SUBSCRIPTION e il pacchetto passa nello stato READONLY_CONSTRAINT_LIMIT_REACHED; è la BC a decidere se bloccare totalmente o mostrare i dati in sola lettura. Con l'overage invece il consumo continua oltre soglia, viene fatturato a fine periodo da BBS, non viene inviato alcun webhook e il pacchetto resta ACTIVE. Lo stesso webhook ENABLE_READONLY_SUBSCRIPTION è usato anche per la scadenza soft comunicata da BBS.", "notes": "What happens when the threshold is reached", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-021", "question": "How are AI credits charged in OnePlatform: is there one wallet per product, and what weights can an operation have?", "lang": "en", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:confluence-mpdd-mpdd-1665630222-1-5-il-flusso-ai-e-il-wallet-ai"], "expected_keywords": ["AI Wallet", "10 credits", "overage"], "expected_answer": "No: the AI Wallet is unique per company and shared by all products (credits from several AI Editions add up in the same wallet). Based on the price list Metering applies a weight of 0 credits (free), 1 credit (light), 5 credits (medium) or 10 credits (heavy operation, e.g. complex reconciliation) and deducts it from the company's wallet. AI never blocks: when credits run out it goes into overage billed by BBS, and the Product ID keeps consumption traceable per product.", "notes": "How consumption works step 3 and AI Wallet characteristics", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-022", "question": "Do I need to request the M2M token that Metering uses to call my webhook, and what should I check on it?", "lang": "en", "category": "yes-no", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:confluence-mpdd-mpdd-1589149784-2-2-guida-per-tech-lead-e-dev-wip"], "expected_keywords": ["SERVICES_SUBSCRIPTION_WEBHOOK:WRITE", "JWK"], "expected_answer": "No. The token used by Metering for the config flow (Metering → Product) is managed by the Metering team and you must not request it yourself. Your responsibility is only to validate it on arrival by checking the JWK signature and the presence of the action SERVICES_SUBSCRIPTION_WEBHOOK:WRITE. The token for the consumption flow (Product → Metering) is instead requested by the product team, per environment.", "notes": "Your responsibilities point 6; M2M authentication - the two flows", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-023", "question": "When a customer changes plan, is the upgrade applied at the same time as a downgrade would be?", "lang": "en", "category": "comparison", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:confluence-mpdd-mpdd-1590362117-2-3-guida-per-go-to-market"], "expected_keywords": ["Upgrade is immediate", "downgrade is planned", "expiry"], "expected_answer": "No. The upgrade is immediate and replaces the old package right away, while the downgrade is planned: it is scheduled and applied at the expiry of the current package.", "notes": "The base rules you must know", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-024", "question": "How is a product's OnePlatform scenario classified before a Metering integration, and what must a Hybrid product do first?", "lang": "en", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:confluence-mpdd-mpdd-1590362125-3-1-identifica-il-tuo-percorso-di-integrazione"], "expected_keywords": ["Scenario 2", "Integration Questionnaire v1.6", "Giovanni Colasurdo"], "expected_answer": "Four yes/no questions (TsID as identity, Registry/Workspace, itemId/ownerId/workspaceId, standard JWT authentication) give a score: 4 Yes = Scenario 1 Native (low complexity, standard Company or Workspace Flow), 1-3 Yes = Scenario 2 Hybrid (medium), 0 Yes = Scenario 3 No integration (high, Metering integration postponed). A Scenario 2 or 3 product must first complete the Integration Questionnaire v1.6 with the OnePlatform team (Giovanni Colasurdo), because identity, tenancy and workspace must be aligned before Metering.", "notes": "1 — Classify your OnePlatform scenario", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-025", "question": "Se il mio webhook risponde con un errore a Metering, dopo quanto tempo viene ritentata la chiamata e cosa succede se continua a fallire?", "lang": "it", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:confluence-mpdd-mpdd-1590951983-4-1-le-4-action-del-webhook"], "expected_keywords": ["300 seconds", "dead-letter"], "expected_answer": "Metering pianifica un retry dopo 300 secondi. Se il webhook continua a fallire, l'evento finisce in dead-letter e richiede un intervento manuale del team Metering; per questo il webhook deve essere idempotente perché lo stesso payload può arrivare più volte.", "notes": "Behavior in case of a webhook error", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-026", "question": "Which API do I call to find out which packages are currently active for a company, and what is the test base URL?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:confluence-mpdd-mpdd-1591279656-4-2-api-di-lettura-metering-package-read"], "expected_keywords": ["/api/v1/company/{itemId}/packages", "metering-package-read"], "expected_answer": "Use the Metering read API (metering-package-read), not BBS: GET /api/v1/company/{itemId}/packages returns all active packages for a company (GET /api/v1/company/{itemId}/families/services returns the active Family and services). The test base URL is https://metering-package-read-test.ts-paas.com, with Swagger UI at /swaggerui/index.html. In M1 the source of truth is the WORKSPACES_SERVICE table for the Workspace Flow and COMPANIES_SERVICE for the Company Flow.", "notes": "Base endpoint / Available endpoints", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-027", "question": "Quale chiave di idempotenza devo usare nel webhook Metering, dato che la stessa chiamata può arrivare più volte?", "lang": "it", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:confluence-mpdd-mpdd-1593213145-4-3-anti-pattern-e-errori-comuni"], "expected_keywords": ["action + serviceId + itemId", "idempotency key"], "expected_answer": "Metering può inviare la stessa chiamata più volte a causa dei retry, quindi il webhook deve essere idempotente usando come idempotency key la combinazione action + serviceId + itemId (o workspaceId). Per il caso multi-licenza la chiave unica è invece serviceId + itemId/workspaceId.", "notes": "Anti-pattern: Non-idempotent webhook", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-028", "question": "Il Metering calcola da solo il consumo eccedente rispetto alla soglia acquistata?", "lang": "it", "category": "yes-no", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:confluence-mpdd-mpdd-1590951974-5-4-faq"], "expected_keywords": ["BBS", "700", "200 invoices"], "expected_answer": "No. Metering non calcola l'extra consumo: invia solo il consumo totale registrato ed è BBS che lo confronta con la soglia del pacchetto acquistato, determina l'overage e genera la fatturazione. Esempio: pacchetto da 500 fatture, consumo effettivo 700, Metering invia 700 e BBS calcola 200 fatture di eccedenza.", "notes": "FAQ: Does Metering automatically calculate the extra consumption", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-029", "question": "When a subscription is renewed, does the consumption counter go back to zero?", "lang": "en", "category": "comparison", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:confluence-mpdd-mpdd-1590951974-5-4-faq"], "expected_keywords": ["Synchronous consumption", "Asynchronous consumption", "resynchronization"], "expected_answer": "It depends on the consumption type. For synchronous (slot) consumption no reset is performed: on renewal a new Enable Subscription is issued but occupied slots and counters stay unchanged. For asynchronous consumption a resynchronization of the consumption is performed.", "notes": "FAQ: Is consumption reset to zero on renewal", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-030", "question": "How do I open a request to the Metering team and which ticket types are available?", "lang": "en", "category": "procedural", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:confluence-mpdd-mpdd-1590886422-5-3-come-fare-una-richiesta-al-team-metering"], "expected_keywords": ["Monetization Enablement", "1327", "separate ticket"], "expected_answer": "Open a ticket on Service Desk → Monetization Enablement / Metering (portal 1327) choosing one of three types: Questions / General support, Change to the integration with Metering (modify an existing Family, indicating its exact name, the change and the impact on active customers) or New integration with Metering (create a new Family, after following the Quick Guide). If you have several needs, open a separate ticket for each request.", "notes": "whole page", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-031", "question": "Nel ticket per un token tecnico M2M legacy che serve a chiamare i webhook remoti di enable/disable di una feature, quale service identifier va indicato e chi sono i contatti tecnico e funzionale da riportare?", "lang": "it", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:confluence-mpdd-mpdd-1505984707-quick-guides-token-tecnici-m2m-legacy-e-apertura-ticket-mete"], "expected_keywords": ["ts-services-subscription-webhook-invoker", "Giorgio Ratti", "enableDisable"], "expected_answer": "Nel caso webhook il service identifier in cui verrà installato il token è ts-services-subscription-webhook-invoker, con claim del tipo <nome_feature>:enableDisable confermato dall'owner dell'API. Come Technical Contact e platform engineer va indicato Alessandro Mulé (o lo sviluppatore di riferimento), come Functional Contact Giorgio Ratti (o il PO di riferimento). Il token è per ambiente: serve un ticket separato per DEV, TEST e PROD.", "notes": "Flow A, Case 2 – Calls to remote enable/disable webhooks", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-032", "question": "Cosa cambia tecnicamente tra Company Flow e Workspace Flow e cosa chiede il team Metering prima di procedere con un cambio di tipo di flusso?", "lang": "it", "category": "comparison", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:confluence-mpdd-mpdd-1631649803-quick-guide-cambio-tipo-di-flusso-company-workspace"], "expected_keywords": ["COMPANIES_SERVICE", "WORKSPACES_SERVICE", "migration plan"], "expected_answer": "Il Company Flow usa l'itemId (UUID azienda), attiva l'intera organizzazione, usa la Subscription API V2 e la tabella COMPANIES_SERVICE; il Workspace Flow usa il workspaceId, attiva il singolo workspace, usa la API V3 e la tabella WORKSPACES_SERVICE. Il cambio è l'operazione più delicata: richiede la migrazione di tutte le subscription attive e l'aggiornamento del webhook. Il team Metering non procede senza migration plan documentato, stima delle subscription attive, conferma che il webhook lato prodotto è aggiornato (o una timeline) e una finestra temporale concordata.", "notes": "What changes technically / What happens if information is missing", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-033", "question": "Voglio aggiungere un limite di consumo a una Family che oggi non ne ha: quali informazioni sono indispensabili nel ticket perché il team Metering proceda?", "lang": "it", "category": "list", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:confluence-mpdd-mpdd-1631584265-quick-guide-nuovo-constraint"], "expected_keywords": ["SINCRONO", "ASINCRONO", "effective date"], "expected_answer": "Il team Metering non procede finché non sono definiti: il tipo di conteggio (SINCRONO a slot con blocco in tempo reale, o ASINCRONO queued via message bus), la soglia e il comportamento a soglia (blocco totale / read-only / overage) e la gestione della base clienti attiva con la data di efficacia (effective date) del constraint. Nel ticket vanno anche Family target, nome del constraint, cosa si misura, overage, upgradable, periodo e tipo di scadenza.", "notes": "Mandatory information / What happens if information is missing", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-034", "question": "What does the ENABLED_TO_CONNECT flag mean when registering a feature in Metering, and what is the related maximum-connections setting?", "lang": "en", "category": "definition", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:confluence-mpdd-mpdd-1625391264-quick-guide-all-attivazione-e-gestione-del-metering-per-prod"], "expected_keywords": ["ENABLED_TO_CONNECT", "shared with other items"], "expected_answer": "ENABLED_TO_CONNECT (true/false) indicates whether the package can be shared with other items, e.g. linked companies (studio-company connections). If it is true, MAX_ACTIVE_CONNECTIONS sets the maximum number of items with which the package can be shared (e.g. 5). Related feature flags are HIDDEN, NOTIFY_STATUS_CHANGE and AUTO_CONNECT (default false).", "notes": "8. Information about the Feature table", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-035", "question": "Which four domains make up the target architecture of Metering M3 and what does each one do?", "lang": "en", "category": "list", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamMeteri:1203601614"], "expected_keywords": ["Smartmeter", "Subscription Manager", "Wallet Manager"], "expected_answer": "The M3 target model has four domains: Smartmeter records consumption, Subscription Manager manages rights and rules (entitlement), Service Manager activates/deactivates services, and Wallet Manager manages credit.", "notes": "Target Conceptual Architecture", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-036", "question": "Nell'integrazione con Metering chi fa cosa: quali sono le responsabilità del team di prodotto e quali del team Metering?", "lang": "it", "category": "list", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:confluence-mpdd-teammeteri-1231224903-quick-start-integrazione-con-metering-oneplatform"], "expected_keywords": ["RACI", "test payloads", "serviceId"], "expected_answer": "Secondo la RACI il team di prodotto fornisce le informazioni della guida e le porta alla call, espone il webhook, implementa tutte e 4 le action, garantisce l'idempotenza, gestisce il multi-licenza, testa con curl prima della call, sceglie il serviceId univoco, verifica che le BC siano registrate su OnePlatform e documenta i gap (sezione A6). Il team Metering valida il caso d'uso col modello M3, definisce/aggiorna Family, Services e Constraints, registra il serviceId, invia i test payloads negli ambienti di staging, supporta il debugging, definisce i next step e valuta e prioritizza i gap segnalati.", "notes": "C3 — RACI — Who Does What (the standalone 5.2 RACI page is empty)", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-037", "question": "Which data products does the monetization system emit, in what format, and how do I consume them?", "lang": "en", "category": "list", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:confluence-mpdd-mpdd-1665695748-4-5-data-products-subscription-manager-e-m1"], "expected_keywords": ["CloudEvent", "Witboost", "Hermes"], "expected_answer": "Three data products: Families (from M1 Metering, emitted by metering-package-debouncer: snapshot of active packages per client, used by My Personal Area, support and billing), Subscriptions (from Subscription Manager: constraints, current consumption, state, sharing) and Consumptions (from Subscription Manager: every consumption event). They are CloudEvent JSON events, not APIs: consumers subscribe to the corresponding Hermes topic or read the data lake, and the schema definitions are hosted on Witboost.", "notes": "Overview: which data products exist", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-a-038", "question": "A chi mi rivolgo per definire l'offerta commerciale e gli articoli, per configurare Family e constraint nel Metering e per i prerequisiti OnePlatform come TsID e Workspace?", "lang": "it", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:confluence-mpdd-mpdd-1588822184-2-1-guida-per-product-owner"], "expected_keywords": ["Luca Faccone", "Giorgio Ratti", "Giovanni Colasurdo"], "expected_answer": "Per offerta commerciale, articoli e listino il riferimento è BBS (Luca Faccone, o il referente Store FIC); per la configurazione di Family, Service e Constraint nel Metering il Metering Team (Giorgio Ratti); per i prerequisiti OnePlatform (TsID, Workspace, Registry) il team OnePlatform (Giovanni Colasurdo).", "notes": "Who to turn to", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-b-001", "question": "My batch service needs to call another capability. Should I use client credentials or a delegation token, and is the old M2M token still an option?", "lang": "en", "category": "comparison", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1286537244"], "expected_keywords": ["client credential", "delegation token", "deprecated"], "expected_answer": "If the operation must be attributable to a real user, use the delegation token (U2M); if it cannot be associated with a user, use the client credential flow. The old M2M token (manually generated JWTs validated by the legacy B2B Auth Service) is deprecated and replaced by client credentials.", "notes": "Sections 'Client Credential vs Delegation token U2M: which one to use?' and 'Context and objective'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-b-002", "question": "Qual è la durata massima del refresh token in una delega U2M e quanto dura l'access token delegato?", "lang": "it", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1325400251"], "expected_keywords": ["30 days", "absolute expiration"], "expected_answer": "Il refresh token ha una durata massima di 30 giorni ed è limitato da una scadenza assoluta (absolute expiration) per delega, approvata dalla policy. L'access token delegato è corto, tra 5 e 15 minuti.", "notes": "Section 7) Security rules of the U2M functional/technical specification", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-b-003", "question": "In the token exchange call to TSID for a delegation, what does the duration parameter control and what happens if I pass a value above the client's configured limits?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1325400251"], "expected_keywords": ["delegation_payload", "default lifetime", "positive integer"], "expected_answer": "duration is a positive integer in seconds giving the desired lifetime of the delegated access token and refresh token; it must be lower than the client's configured access/refresh token lifetime limits, otherwise the client's default lifetime is used. It is sent together with client_id, grant_type, subject_token (the original user token) and delegation_payload (the opaque result of the Delegation Manager API).", "notes": "Section 8) API implementation details - Token exchange (ExtService -> TSID)", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-b-004", "question": "How can a downstream authorizer tell that the JWT it received is a delegation token, and where are the delegated details stored in it?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1325400251"], "expected_keywords": ["token_type=delegation", "authorization_details"], "expected_answer": "The claim token_type=delegation identifies a delegation token, and the claim authorization_details contains the JSON value that was provided in the delegation_payload parameter of the token exchange.", "notes": "Section 8) Response - Sample delegation token; also mentioned in security rules of the OPC-7313 page", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-b-005", "question": "What changes for the Delegation Manager between the T1 and T2 releases of the delegation token flow?", "lang": "en", "category": "comparison", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1283686531"], "expected_keywords": ["DelegationManager", "delegation_id", "getDelegation"], "expected_answer": "In T1 the DelegationManager stays stateless (mapping only) and the new logic is in PolicyAuth, which recognizes delegation tokens and checks delegated permissions at runtime. In T2 the DelegationManager gains persistence and authorization logic, becoming the source of truth: it checks that the user may delegate the requested permissions, the delegation_payload becomes an opaque delegation_id, and TSID calls getDelegation on the DM during the token exchange instead of trusting the payload from the ExtService.", "notes": "Sections 'T1 - Minimum version for production', 'T2 - DelegationManager with persistence' and '5) Evolutionary summary'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-b-006", "question": "Nella fase T1 del delegation token un utente potrebbe inserire nel payload permessi che non possiede? Perché il rischio è stato accettato?", "lang": "it", "category": "yes-no", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1283686531"], "expected_keywords": ["opaque", "Authorizer", "T2"], "expected_answer": "Sì, in T1 il DelegationManager non verifica la coerenza con il profilo, quindi tecnicamente è possibile. Il rischio (R1) è accettato perché il payload è opaco e non ha significato fuori dall'Authorizer, l'Authorizer finale nega comunque i permessi non legittimi al momento dell'autorizzazione, e la mitigazione completa arriva in T2 con la logica autorizzativa nel DelegationManager.", "notes": "Section 'T1 - Security consideration' and table 'Relevant risks and decisions' (R1)", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-b-007", "question": "What do I need to set up before my service can start requesting delegation tokens from TSID?", "lang": "en", "category": "procedural", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1325400251"], "expected_keywords": ["1P Technical Support", "token exchange", "ticket"], "expected_answer": "Two pre-conditions: the client's delegation permissions must be enabled through a ticketing process (identifying the delegable service, the delegable policies and the maximum authorizable duration), and both the External Service and the External Async Service must be registered as clients in TSID, requesting client credentials with scope token exchange by opening a ticket to 1P Technical Support.", "notes": "Section 3) Pre-conditions", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-b-008", "question": "In the full delegation token model, which JWT claims carry the delegator and the delegate identities?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1031962729"], "expected_keywords": ["act.sub", "ABAC"], "expected_answer": "The sub claim identifies the delegator and act.sub identifies the delegate; downstream services and the Policy Manager validate the token and apply ABAC rules on these claims plus scopes and duration, and every operation is recorded for audit.", "notes": "Section 'Use of the Delegation Token'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-b-009", "question": "Perché è nato il meccanismo del Delegation Token? Quale problema risolve rispetto alle chiamate M2M tra Business Capability?", "lang": "it", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1282539740"], "expected_keywords": ["F24", "GovHub", "Orchestrator"], "expected_answer": "L'obiettivo è eliminare le credenziali machine-to-machine (chiavi M2M, service account generici) tra BC propagando l'identità dell'utente in modo sicuro e verificabile. Alcune BC come F24, Orchestrator e GovHub accettano solo chiamate attribuibili ad account personali e rifiutano i service account generici; con il Delegation Token la BC destinataria sa quale utente ha originato l'azione e ne verifica i permessi prima di eseguire.", "notes": "Section 1. General Objectives and Requirements", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-b-010", "question": "What happens to an active delegation if the delegating user's account gets deactivated, or if some of their permissions are removed before the nightly job runs?", "lang": "en", "category": "multi-hop", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1153564760", "confluence:TeamCore:1282539740"], "expected_keywords": ["deactivated", "batch"], "expected_answer": "If the user's account is deactivated the delegation token immediately ceases to be valid (all delegations are invalidated, the job fails and generates an alert). If only some permissions are removed, the following night job executes only the operations for which the user still has rights: the no-longer-authorized operations are rejected individually without blocking the entire batch.", "notes": "Delegation Token Light 'Requirement Attention Point' and requirements analysis RP-09/RP-12, CU-04/CU-05", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-b-011", "question": "What is the difference between delegation and impersonation in OAuth 2.0 token exchange?", "lang": "en", "category": "comparison", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1318027400"], "expected_keywords": ["impersonation", "RFC 8693"], "expected_answer": "With impersonation a system completely assumes the identity of another subject: the actor is invisible and A and B are indistinguishable to the resource server. With delegation the system acts on behalf of the user while keeping its own identity: the token includes the subject (user) and the actor (service) via the act claim, so the resource server can distinguish them.", "notes": "Section 3. Delegation and impersonation (RFC 8693)", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-b-012", "question": "Quali parametri sono obbligatori in una richiesta di token exchange e quando serve actor_token?", "lang": "it", "category": "list", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1318027400"], "expected_keywords": ["subject_token", "subject_token_type", "actor_token"], "expected_answer": "Sono obbligatori subject_token (il token che rappresenta l'identità per cui si richiede il nuovo token) e subject_token_type. actor_token (con actor_token_type) è opzionale e serve solo nei casi di delegation per rappresentare chi agisce; requested_token_type, resource/audience e scope sono ulteriori parametri opzionali.", "notes": "Section 4. Token Exchange Request - Parameters of the call", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-b-013", "question": "What is step-up authentication, and is there a TeamSystem product where MFA is required at login rather than per operation?", "lang": "en", "category": "definition", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1297678356"], "expected_keywords": ["TS-Pay", "OTP"], "expected_answer": "Step-up authentication requires a higher level of security only when the user is about to perform a sensitive action: the user is already authenticated but must confirm identity with a stronger factor (OTP, app, biometrics). Some business capabilities instead require the second factor mandatorily at login, e.g. TS-Pay.", "notes": "Sections 'What is Step-Up Authentication?' and 'Typical use cases'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-b-014", "question": "In our microfrontend shell with Module Federation, can each microfrontend keep its own access token in localStorage and refresh it on its own?", "lang": "en", "category": "yes-no", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1335197772"], "expected_keywords": ["localStorage", "Module Federation", "PKCE"], "expected_answer": "No. Session, access token and refresh token management must be centralized in the shell (or a BFF): microfrontends must not keep or manage tokens, must not talk to the IdP and must not perform refreshes; they use only the shared Auth SDK exposed by the shell. Tokens go in JS memory (not localStorage/sessionStorage) and the public-client variant uses Authorization Code Flow with PKCE.", "notes": "Intro, 'Architectural principles' and 'Solution A: SPA Public Client'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-b-015", "question": "Nell'architettura di autenticazione per SPA, che differenza c'è tra la soluzione SPA+BFF e la soluzione BFF Proxy riguardo a dove vengono conservati i token?", "lang": "it", "category": "comparison", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1335197772"], "expected_keywords": ["HttpOnly", "CSRF", "Redis"], "expected_answer": "Nella soluzione B (SPA + BFF) l'access token resta in memoria JS nel browser mentre il refresh token è cifrato in un cookie HttpOnly + Secure + SameSite impostato dal BFF, che lo usa per chiamare la refresh API di TSID. Nella soluzione C (BFF Proxy) sia access che refresh token restano sul server nella sessione del BFF (es. Redis), il browser usa solo un cookie di sessione e i microfrontend non vedono mai i bearer token; in cambio bisogna gestire il CSRF.", "notes": "Sections 'Solution B: SPA + BFF' and 'Solution C: BFF Proxy'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-b-016", "question": "A customer wants to federate their corporate IdP with TSID using OpenID Connect. What configuration data do they have to give us, and what do we give back?", "lang": "en", "category": "procedural", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1294893122"], "expected_keywords": ["Authority", ".well-known/openid-configuration", "/federation/{schema}/signin"], "expected_answer": "The customer provides the email Domain to federate, Client ID, Secret, Scope, the Authority (issuer URL), Response Type code and whether PKCE is required; the authorization, token and JWKS endpoints are derived automatically from the discovery document at https://<authority>/.well-known/openid-configuration. The platform returns the Redirect URI https://<platform-domain>/federation/{schema}/signin.", "notes": "Section 7. OIDC configuration parameters", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-b-017", "question": "Quali dati utente deve inviare obbligatoriamente l'Identity Provider esterno per il SSO con la piattaforma, e quale campo viene usato come identificativo univoco?", "lang": "it", "category": "list", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1294893122"], "expected_keywords": ["First name", "Last name", "Email"], "expected_answer": "I dati obbligatori sono nome (First name), cognome (Last name) ed Email; l'email è usata come identificativo univoco dell'utente nella piattaforma. Con SAML 2.0 viaggiano come elementi Attribute della SAML Assertion, con OIDC come claim standard nell'ID Token.", "notes": "Section 4. Required user attributes", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-b-018", "question": "What's the difference between the Owner and an Admin of an Item in terms of what they can manage?", "lang": "en", "category": "comparison", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1105068039"], "expected_keywords": ["Owner", "Admin", "Policy Manager"], "expected_answer": "The Owner is the unique user who created or claimed the Item; each Item has only one Owner and the role cannot be unassigned or removed. Both Owner and Admin access the Policy Manager and have implicit access to all Item services (including future ones), but the Owner can manage an Admin's permissions while an Admin cannot manage the Owner's. Being Admin does not mean having individual service-level permissions explicitly assigned.", "notes": "Entries 'Admin (of an Item)' and 'Owner (of an Item)'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-b-019", "question": "Which passwordless factors are considered valid for PSD2 Strong Customer Authentication, and which ones are not?", "lang": "en", "category": "list", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1051590759"], "expected_keywords": ["Passkey", "WebAuthn", "Magic Link"], "expected_answer": "Valid PSD2/SCA factors: Passkey/WebAuthn (possession), local biometrics such as FaceID/TouchID (inherence) and Push Authentication via an authenticator app (possession). SMS OTP is only a legacy possession factor acceptable as secondary; OTP via email/Magic Link and social login (Google, Apple, Microsoft) are not PSD2 factors. SCA requires combining two factors from different categories, e.g. Passkey + Biometrics.", "notes": "Table 'Passwordless Factors - Web + Mobile' and note", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-b-020", "question": "Per quanto tempo vanno conservati i log secondo PCI DSS e secondo le linee guida del Garante sugli amministratori di sistema?", "lang": "it", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1027014769"], "expected_keywords": ["PCI DSS", "12 months", "6 months"], "expected_answer": "PCI DSS v4.0 richiede la conservazione dei log per almeno 12 mesi, con almeno i 3 mesi più recenti immediatamente disponibili per analisi e forensics. Le linee guida del Garante sugli amministratori di sistema impongono una conservazione documentata di almeno 6 mesi per i log degli accessi degli operatori privilegiati.", "notes": "Sections 'PCI DSS v4.0' and 'Rulings of the Garante Privacy'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-b-021", "question": "Why does the TSID installer for on-prem products use Authorization Code Flow with PKCE instead of a client secret?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1091371026"], "expected_keywords": ["PKCE", "client secret"], "expected_answer": "Because the installer is distributed on customer machines and cannot guarantee secure storage of a secret; PKCE completely avoids the client secret, is standard and robust. The installer uses a single preconfigured client generated by the back-office and distributed to all customers.", "notes": "Sections 2.1 Solution and 2.2 Rationale for choosing PKCE", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-b-022", "question": "How many PBKDF2 iterations does TSID currently use for password hashing, and what do the directives require?", "lang": "en", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1092059160"], "expected_keywords": ["PBKDF2", "600,000", "100,000"], "expected_answer": "TSID uses PBKDF2 with SHA-256 at 100,000 iterations today, while the directives require 600,000 iterations for SHA-256 (or 210,000 for SHA-512), so the value must be brought into line. The same page also sets password rotation every 90 days, a ban on reusing the last 3 passwords, and deactivation after two years without login.", "notes": "Section 3.1 Algorithm used", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-b-023", "question": "Con la nuova informativa privacy di TSID, il consenso all'AI training è attivo di default? E in che lingua vedono i testi gli utenti non italiani?", "lang": "it", "category": "yes-no", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1235812491"], "expected_keywords": ["AI Training", "opt-out"], "expected_answer": "Sì: la nuova policy sull'AI Training è di tipo opt-out, accettata dall'utente per default, e va implementato il log di questo consenso. I testi sono forniti dal legal in italiano; chi accede con una lingua diversa dall'italiano vede la traduzione inglese, nessun'altra lingua è prevista. Gli utenti esistenti vedono l'aggiornamento al primo login dopo il rilascio.", "notes": "Sections 1 and 2 of 'What we have to do'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-b-024", "question": "When publishing IAM events through Hermes, what are the ordering requirements for record_key and outbox_timestamp, and what does the default EMIT_STRATEGY do?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1150058578"], "expected_keywords": ["SkipOnSameDlqKey", "tsIdSubject", "13 digits"], "expected_answer": "record_key must be the main entity ID (e.g. identityId, policyId, tsIdSubject) so all events for the same entity land on the same partition and are ordered; outbox_timestamp must be a Unix timestamp in milliseconds (13 digits). EMIT_STRATEGY defaults to SkipOnSameDlqKey, which blocks messages with the same key if one ended up in the DLQ, preserving order. Delivery is at-least-once, so consumers must be idempotent.", "notes": "Sections 3.3 Delivery guarantees & ordering and 3.4 Key Relay Parameters", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-b-025", "question": "How many wrong passwords can a user enter on TSID before being blocked, how long do they wait, and does it apply to @teamsystem.com accounts?", "lang": "en", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1023246350"], "expected_keywords": ["10 minutes", "@teamsystem.com", "five"], "expected_answer": "An incorrect password is allowed up to a maximum of five times; after that the user is blocked and must wait at least 10 minutes before trying again. There is no blocking for users with an @teamsystem.com email. From the blocked screen the user can use 'Forgot password?' (not available for own-auth domains and @teamsystem.com).", "notes": "Section 'User Blocked'. Note: the 'TSID log on Grafana' page instead mentions lockout after 3 consecutive wrong passwords - possible inconsistency in the KB", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-b-026", "question": "In Grafana, which service name do I filter on to see TSID login logs, and which key identifies the application that redirected the user?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1188757581"], "expected_keywords": ["tsid_ui", "Request.ClientId", "Request.TrackId"], "expected_answer": "The reference service name is tsid_ui. Request.ClientId identifies the application that redirected the user to TSID and is the primary filter; a specific user can be found via Request.Email or Request.TrackId, while ActionName (e.g. /Account/LoginPassword) identifies the flow step.", "notes": "Sections 'Log' and 'Log keys' / 'User flows'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-b-027", "question": "For the Policy Manager PDP, what are the trade-offs between a centralized deployment and running OPA as a sidecar next to the services?", "lang": "en", "category": "comparison", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1007845441"], "expected_keywords": ["sidecar", "bottleneck", "PDP"], "expected_answer": "A centralized PDP is simpler to operate but adds network latency and can become a bottleneck as calls grow. A PDP/OPA sidecar close to the services gives minimal latency and greater isolation, at the cost of more operational complexity (rollout, policy versioning, distributed observability). In both cases evaluation must stay consistent with the PAP lifecycle, which is why Collector/Distributor components propagate changes.", "notes": "Section 7) Deploy topologies (conceptual) and 6) Propagation", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-b-028", "question": "Nel Policy Manager qual è la tenancy di default e quando ha senso introdurre una sub-tenancy? Fai un esempio.", "lang": "it", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1008042093"], "expected_keywords": ["workspace-id", "project-id", "business-unit-id"], "expected_answer": "La tenancy di piattaforma è il Workspace ID (workspace-id), chiave comune usata dalle Business Capability per operare nello stesso contesto dati. La sub-tenancy è un livello di isolamento opzionale dentro lo stesso workspace, da usare quando serve una separazione più fine del solo workspace-id, ad esempio project-id o business-unit-id; non sostituisce il workspace-id ma lo specializza e va validata con lo stesso rigore.", "notes": "Sections 1) Quick definitions, 2) and 6) Sub-tenancy", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-b-029", "question": "Which roles exist in the Policy Manager, can I create a new one, and what is the Affiliate role for?", "lang": "en", "category": "list", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1008173190"], "expected_keywords": ["Affiliate", "Manager", "predefined"], "expected_answer": "Roles are a fixed, predefined set: Owner, Admin, Manager and Affiliate; new roles cannot be created. Every user linked to a company has at least one role (minimum Owner or Affiliate). Affiliate exists only to maintain the user's membership of the company, even when they have no operational permissions on modules or resources.", "notes": "Sections 1) Rules of the game and 2) Available roles", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-b-030", "question": "Basta nascondere un pulsante nella UI per proteggere un'operazione con il Policy Manager? E come evito una tempesta di chiamate di autorizzazione da una pagina con tanti componenti?", "lang": "it", "category": "yes-no", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1010663490"], "expected_keywords": ["UI-only", "BFF", "PEP"], "expected_answer": "No: l'enforcement UI-only è un anti-pattern aggirabile. La UI può usare le decisioni solo per UX (show/hide/disable), la sicurezza reale deve stare nel backend/servizio (PEP) lato server. Per evitare N chiamate dalla UI si usa il batching via BFF: la UI fa una richiesta al BFF, che costruisce un batch di check verso il Policy Manager e restituisce una mappa di permessi per la pagina, eventualmente con una cache di breve durata.", "notes": "Sections 1.1, 3.2 UI-only enforcement (anti-pattern) and 4) UI pattern: avoiding N calls", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-b-031", "question": "Who is allowed to access the Policy Manager UI? Can a user with the legacy MANAGER or WRITE policy get in?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1057226774"], "expected_keywords": ["core.legacy.v1.admin", "OWNER", "ADMIN"], "expected_answer": "Only OWNER users and ADMIN (legacy) users, i.e. those with the policy core.legacy.v1.admin, can access the Policy Manager. Users holding only legacy MANAGER, WRITE, READ or service-ADMIN policies are base users and can never access it. Neither the OWNER nor an ADMIN can modify their own permissions, and an ADMIN cannot modify the OWNER's permissions.", "notes": "Section 'Who can access the Policy Manager'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-b-032", "question": "If I remove the Admin role from a user who also has some permissions explicitly assigned, do they lose everything?", "lang": "en", "category": "yes-no", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1161429089"], "expected_keywords": ["explicitly assigned", "SDI", "core.legacy.v1.ADMIN"], "expected_answer": "No. Removing the Admin role/attribute (permission core.legacy.v1.ADMIN) removes Policy Manager access and the implicit access to all Item services, but the user keeps access to the services for which they have explicitly assigned permissions (e.g. Luca Verdi keeps SDI). If the user had only the Admin permission, with the current behavior they disappear from the users table because nothing else is assigned.", "notes": "Section 'Remove permissions' use cases", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-b-033", "question": "What are the possible workspace classifier values for the type of organization shown in the Policy Manager, and what counts as a fake company?", "lang": "en", "category": "list", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1158021279"], "expected_keywords": ["CONDOMINIUM", "vatIdentifier", "classifier"], "expected_answer": "The classifier can be COMPANY, CONDOMINIUM, PERSON, SELF_EMPLOYED_WORKER, PUBLIC_ENTITY, SOCIAL_ENTERPRISE, PROFESSIONAL_ACCOUNTING_ASSOCIATION or TRUST, retrieved via GET /api/v2/workspaces?ownerId={ownerId}. A fake company is any classifier whose countryCode, taxIdentifier and vatIdentifier are all null.", "notes": "Sections 'Classifiers list' and 'Fake company'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-b-034", "question": "In the Policy Manager UI, how is a technical service code like domain.subdomain turned into a readable name, and which services are always displayed?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1079902302"], "expected_keywords": ["appDescription", "featureCode", "oneplatform"], "expected_answer": "service = domain.subdomain = appId.featureCode = appDescription.description: domain maps to appId and subdomain to featureCode in the Metering service catalog, so the front-end shows appDescription.description. Platform services (domain 'oneplatform') are always displayed; other services are shown only if active for the Item according to the Metering catalog. Legacy policies translate to ADMIN/MANAGER, new policies use the title from the policy catalog.", "notes": "Sections 'General assumptions' and 'Translation to a human language of the services and policies'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-c-001", "question": "A customer wants their TeamSystem ID account deleted. What should the support operator tell them?", "lang": "en", "category": "procedural", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:907739295"], "expected_keywords": ["privacy@teamsystem.com"], "expected_answer": "The operator informs the customer that a request must be sent to privacy@teamsystem.com indicating the email address to be deleted; the legal office will then request the disabling or deletion of that TS ID.", "notes": "FAQ TSID ticket handling, General requests row 12", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-c-002", "question": "Un utente vede il messaggio 'CAPTCHA Test failed or missing' durante il reset password su TSID senza vedere nessun captcha: quali URL esterni deve verificare che non siano bloccati dalla rete aziendale?", "lang": "it", "category": "list", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:907739295"], "expected_keywords": ["recaptcha", "gstatic"], "expected_answer": "Bisogna verificare che la rete aziendale non blocchi https://www.google.com/recaptcha/api.js, https://www.google.com/recaptcha/api/siteverify e https://www.gstatic.com/recaptcha/api2/*. Se dopo lo sblocco il test CAPTCHA continua a fallire, il ticket va passato a L3.", "notes": "FAQ TSID row 11 (Forgotten password section)", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-c-003", "question": "How long does the TSID account activation email link stay valid, and how long is the passwordless (login without password) email link valid?", "lang": "en", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:907739295"], "expected_keywords": ["24 hours", "15 minutes"], "expected_answer": "The activation link received from identity@email.teamsystem.com is valid for 24 hours, while the link for logging in without a password is valid for 15 minutes.", "notes": "FAQ TSID rows 4 and 9", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-c-004", "question": "In the Policy Manager, what is the difference between 'Remove user' and 'Cancel invitation'?", "lang": "en", "category": "comparison", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1618313409"], "expected_keywords": ["Cancel invitation", "Pending"], "expected_answer": "'Remove user' applies to Active users and removes their permissions and affiliation from the profile, while 'Cancel invitation' applies to Pending users and deletes the invitation together with the saved permissions, since the user did not yet have a profile on the organization.", "notes": "FAQ - Policy Manager", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-c-005", "question": "Nel Policy Manager non vedo i permessi del mio servizio nella tabella di assegnazione: quali controlli devo fare, in ordine?", "lang": "it", "category": "list", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1618313409"], "expected_keywords": ["Metering", "Policy Catalog", "Identity Profile"], "expected_answer": "Verificare in ordine: che il servizio sia attivo su Metering per l'organizzazione; se il servizio è item-based o workspace-based (proprietà Metering); che il permesso esista nel Policy Catalog dell'ambiente corretto (tdev/test/demo/prod); che l'utente loggato possieda quel permesso nel proprio Identity Profile; per Admin/Manager che l'utente abbia un TeamSystem ID; per Manager che esista una connessione tra organizzazioni (managed) per il servizio item-based.", "notes": "FAQ - Policy Manager, last Q 'Why do I not see my service in the policy manager?'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-c-006", "question": "Where do I find the Policy Manager in OnePlatform and which roles are currently allowed to use it?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1617952961"], "expected_keywords": ["My Value Center", "Owner"], "expected_answer": "The Policy Manager is accessible from My Value Center (Users section), reachable from the home or from the organization workspace. Today access is reserved to Owner and Admin users; access for other roles via explicit permission is still being defined.", "notes": "PM – Overview, sections Overview / How It Works / Rules", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-c-007", "question": "Quando invito nel Policy Manager una persona che non ha ancora un TeamSystem ID, posso assegnarle subito i ruoli dei servizi legacy?", "lang": "it", "category": "yes-no", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1618378874"], "expected_keywords": ["legacy roles", "TSID"], "expected_answer": "No. I servizi con soli ruoli legacy non sono assegnabili a utenti senza TSID durante l'invito: compaiono tra i permessi assegnabili solo se l'utente ha già un TSID attivo. Per gli utenti senza TSID questi permessi vanno assegnati dopo, dalla schermata di modifica permessi, una volta che l'utente è Active.", "notes": "PM – User Invitation Flow, Step 2 constraint and Scenario 1", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-c-008", "question": "What does 'reconciliation' mean in the Policy Manager invitation process?", "lang": "en", "category": "definition", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1618378874"], "expected_keywords": ["reconciliation", "TSID activation"], "expected_answer": "Reconciliation is the automatic process that, at the moment of the TSID activation, transfers the permissions saved in the invitation to the user's profile. Until then, for a user without TSID, permissions are stored in the invitation and not in the profile.", "notes": "PM – User Invitation Flow, Key Concepts", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-c-009", "question": "How does the Policy Manager invitation wizard change when my organization manages services for client organizations? Which extra steps appear?", "lang": "en", "category": "procedural", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1617756341"], "expected_keywords": ["Choose organizations", "Enabled clients"], "expected_answer": "The flow expands from 3 to 5 steps: after entering the email, a new 'Choose organizations' step lets the admin select the client organizations; then permissions are chosen on the own organization, then a new step 'Choose permissions on the selected clients' (with the 'Enabled clients' drawer per permission), and finally the confirmation with two tabs ('Your organization' and 'Clients').", "notes": "PM – User Invitation Flow – with Client Organizations, 'How the flow changes' table", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-c-010", "question": "Posso invitare un utente dando permessi solo sulle organizzazioni clienti gestite dal mio studio, senza dargli nulla sulla mia organizzazione?", "lang": "it", "category": "yes-no", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1617756341"], "expected_keywords": ["at least one permission", "affiliation"], "expected_answer": "Al momento no: la checkbox 'Set permissions on your organization as well' è obbligatoria ed è necessario assegnare almeno un permesso sulla propria organizzazione per completare l'invito. Il vincolo è temporaneo e verrà rimosso con l'implementazione dell'affiliation.", "notes": "Step 2 'Current constraint' and FAQ", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-c-011", "question": "Se dalla schermata di modifica permessi tolgo tutti i permessi a un utente, viene anche rimosso dall'organizzazione?", "lang": "it", "category": "yes-no", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1649836109"], "expected_keywords": ["Remove user", "affiliation remains"], "expected_answer": "No. Rimuovere tutti i permessi non equivale a rimuovere l'utente: l'affiliazione resta. Per eliminare completamente l'utente dall'organizzazione bisogna usare l'azione 'Remove user'.", "notes": "PM – User Permissions Modification, FAQ", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-c-012", "question": "In the new user-removal logic (OPC-7502), what happens when an Admin removes a user who still holds permissions on managed organizations the Admin cannot see?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1554120757"], "expected_keywords": ["in-app notification", "IdentityProfileWrite"], "expected_answer": "In Step 1 the removal is partial: permissions on the primary org and on the managed orgs visible to the Admin are removed, but the affiliation attribute is not removed (it is removed via IdentityProfileWrite only if all permissions are gone), and the Admin receives an in-app notification about the residual permissions with the indication to involve the Owner to complete the removal.", "notes": "UC002 and general rules R2/R7", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-c-013", "question": "Why is 'role inheritance on workspaces' relevant for the user removal feature in the Policy Manager, and is it considered a permanent solution?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1554120757"], "expected_keywords": ["role inheritance", "UC002"], "expected_answer": "With role inheritance, Owner and Admin automatically inherit their role across all workspaces managed by the organization, so the Admin has full visibility and removal is always total (partial-removal case UC002 does not apply). It is a transitional technical enabler: the definitive behavior depends on the Admin role revision and role management on the Policy Manager (OP-RU-03).", "notes": "Architectural note — Role inheritance on workspaces", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-c-014", "question": "Qual è il bug attuale documentato nella rimozione utente dal Policy Manager per quanto riguarda le organizzazioni gestite?", "lang": "it", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:confluence-teamcore-teamcore-1577975809-pm-remove-user-affiliation-scenarios"], "expected_keywords": ["managed orgs", "Not removed"], "expected_answer": "Oggi la rimozione utente elimina correttamente i permessi sull'organizzazione principale, ma i permessi sulle organizzazioni gestite (managed orgs) non vengono rimossi e restano nel sistema. La soluzione a lungo termine è ridefinire il ruolo Admin con visibilità completa su tutte le managed orgs.", "notes": "as-is behavior (documented bug) and Long-term solution", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-c-015", "question": "During the Policy Manager invitation flow, how does the system know which organization to attach the affiliation attribute to?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:confluence-teamcore-teamcore-1467678966-pm-management-of-affiliation-policy-opc-6904"], "expected_keywords": ["sourceItemId", "IdentityProfile"], "expected_answer": "The invitation request includes sourceItemId, which identifies the Item/organization; the Invitation service calls IdentityProfile (IdentityProfileWrite) to ensure the scope for that Item exists and adds the affiliation attribute in that scope, regardless of whether service permissions are assigned.", "notes": "REQ002 – Affiliation assignment during the invitation flow, UC001/UC002", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-c-016", "question": "What exactly is the 'affiliation attribute' in the IAM/Policy Manager model, and does it give the user any permissions?", "lang": "en", "category": "definition", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1397948484"], "expected_keywords": ["Identity Profile", "scope", "not an authorization policy"], "expected_answer": "Affiliation is the association between a user and an organization, stored as an Identity Profile attribute in the scope of the specific Item. It is not an authorization policy: it grants no operational permissions and is independent from service permissions; it is the basis for the user's visibility in the Policy Manager.", "notes": "Section 'What is the affiliation attribute?'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-c-017", "question": "For existing users (backward compatibility), which signals let the system assign the affiliation attribute without ambiguity, and where is affiliation assigned when a user has permissions on managed organizations?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:confluence-teamcore-teamcore-1509490736-pm-define-user-affiliation-scenarios-for-backward-compatibil"], "expected_keywords": ["Company Owner", "Company Admin", "primary org"], "expected_answer": "Affiliation is assigned only on the user's primary organization; permissions on managed organizations never generate affiliation on those orgs. In the priority hierarchy only Company Owner and Company Admin are always unambiguous; Service Admin, Service Manager and New-Policies-only cases can be ambiguous when permissions span several orgs (open points OP001/OP002/OP003).", "notes": "Core rule + 'Backward Compatibility Assignment Rules' table", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-c-018", "question": "Nell'analisi OPC-7523 sull'unificazione di ruoli legacy e nuove policy, come si ricavano gli stati NOT_MIGRATED, IN_PROGRESS e MIGRATED di una capability?", "lang": "it", "category": "definition", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1529118725"], "expected_keywords": ["integration_status", "MIGRATED"], "expected_answer": "Gli stati non esistono come entità: si derivano da due condizioni. NOT_MIGRATED = policy catalog assente; IN_PROGRESS = policy catalog presente con integration_status = false; MIGRATED = policy catalog presente con integration_status = true. Il flag integration_status è modificabile solo via API.", "notes": "Document conventions mapping table / REQ002", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-c-019", "question": "In the Policy Manager frontend, which legacy role is shown on the 'My organization' page versus the 'Client organizations' page, and are Read/Write roles ever displayed?", "lang": "en", "category": "comparison", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1529118725"], "expected_keywords": ["Manager", "Read and Write"], "expected_answer": "On the 'My organization' page only the Admin (service) legacy role is exposed, while on the 'Client organizations' page only Manager (service) is exposed. Read and Write are never displayed in any context; the change is frontend-only and the underlying assignment rules (e.g. Manager automatically includes Read and Write) do not change.", "notes": "REQ005 / UC009 exposure logic table", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-c-020", "question": "According to the TSID inbound migration assessment questionnaire, which authentication flow is recommended for a backend batch integration with no human user, and which for an interactive web app with a human user?", "lang": "en", "category": "comparison", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:985563249"], "expected_keywords": ["Client Credentials", "PKCE"], "expected_answer": "For machine-to-machine access with no user identity (backend/batch) the guidance is OAuth2 Client Credentials; for interactive access with a human user needing user identity it is OpenID Connect Authorization Code, with PKCE for public apps. SAML 2.0 is suggested for already federated enterprise systems and TSID-IdP federation for full delegation.", "notes": "Section K – Flow Guidance", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-c-021", "question": "Which Auth0 tenants are used in the TeamSystem Auth0 PoC, for the pre-PoC phase and for the PoC itself?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1508638846"], "expected_keywords": ["green-goose-97556", "tsid-dev@eu"], "expected_answer": "The pre-PoC tenant is green-goose-97556 (accessed via the cic-demo-platform dashboard), while the PoC tenant is tsid-dev@eu, with admin credentials managed by the Auth0 Solutions Engineers.", "notes": "Project Logistics > Environment", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-c-022", "question": "From the Auth0 PoC Q&A: can Universal Login be embedded in an iframe, and what is the default limit of client grants per tenant?", "lang": "en", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1508638846"], "expected_keywords": ["clickjacking", "100k", "1M"], "expected_answer": "No, Universal Login in an iframe is blocked for security reasons (clickjacking prevention). Client grants per tenant default to 100k and can be extended to 1M with performance considerations.", "notes": "Q&A Highlights", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-c-023", "question": "What is the difference between the 'TSID mode' and the 'Auth0 mode' for token issuance in the Auth0 integration of TeamSystem ID?", "lang": "en", "category": "comparison", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1579810859"], "expected_keywords": ["TokenMode", "signed by Auth0"], "expected_answer": "In TSID mode (TokenMode = Tsid, the default) Auth0 only authenticates the user and TSID issues and signs the access/ID tokens, keeping full control of claims so clients need no changes. In Auth0 mode Auth0 authenticates and issues the tokens, so the client receives a token signed by Auth0 and can leverage Auth0 native features (RBAC, Actions) at token level.", "notes": "Login flow section + Configuration table", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-c-024", "question": "Con la Lazy Migration verso Auth0, TSID invia ad Auth0 la password o il suo hash degli utenti esistenti? Come funziona la migrazione al primo login?", "lang": "it", "category": "yes-no", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1579810859"], "expected_keywords": ["LazyMigration", "auth0-migration/login", "bcrypt"], "expected_answer": "No: TSID non invia mai né la password né l'hash. L'utente digita la password nella Universal Login di Auth0; al primo login Auth0 non trova l'utente e chiama lo script Login della Custom Database Connection, che invoca POST /api/v1/auth0-migration/login su TSID per validare le credenziali (PBKDF2). Se valide TSID restituisce il profilo, Auth0 ri-hasha in bcrypt la password già in suo possesso e salva l'utente nel proprio DB; dai login successivi non contatta più TSID.", "notes": "User Migration > 2. Lazy Migration", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-c-025", "question": "How can I preview which changes an Auth0 Deploy CLI import would apply to the tenant without actually modifying it?", "lang": "en", "category": "procedural", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:1544486919"], "expected_keywords": ["--dry-run", "AUTH0_ALLOW_DELETE"], "expected_answer": "Run the import with the --dry-run option: it generates a plan of changes (resources to be created, updated, and deleted if AUTH0_ALLOW_DELETE is enabled, plus differences with the remote tenant) without applying anything. Adding --interactive gives a menu to review the plan, apply it, export it to a file or exit.", "notes": "Dry Run section", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-c-026", "question": "Con la step-up authentication OIDC di TSID, come fa il client a capire se il token attesta un'autenticazione forte, e come richiede l'autenticazione forte se manca?", "lang": "it", "category": "procedural", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:974979328"], "expected_keywords": ["amr", "acr_values", "mfa"], "expected_answer": "Il client si basa solo sui claim standard: il token è forte se il claim amr contiene \"mfa\" (nella fase 1 l'autenticazione forte non ha scadenza; auth_time è previsto per evoluzioni future). Se il token non è forte l'accesso deve fallire e il client avvia una nuova authorization request OIDC con acr_values per richiedere esplicitamente la strong authentication; l'IdP richiede la MFA e rilascia un nuovo strong token.", "notes": "Relevant OIDC claims / Requesting the Step-Up Authentication", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-c-027", "question": "How does TSID propagate a logout to the applications using OIDC Back-Channel Logout, and which claim ties the logout to the right session?", "lang": "en", "category": "procedural", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:985497725"], "expected_keywords": ["Back-Channel Logout", "sid", "Logout Token"], "expected_answer": "At login TSID puts a session id (sid) in the ID token, which the application stores with its own session. On logout TSID terminates its session cookie and POSTs a Logout Token (containing sub and sid) to each application's pre-registered Back-Channel Logout URI; the app validates the token, finds the session by sid and terminates it, answering HTTP 200. The URIs must be reachable from the IdP and use TLS.", "notes": "Solutions > OIDC Back-Channel Logout (draft document)", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-c-028", "question": "Which Elasticsearch/HELK indexes should I use to look up TeamSystem ID login and signup logs in test and in production?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:953516193"], "expected_keywords": ["tsid-stage-filebeat", "tsid-filebeat"], "expected_answer": "On the HELK dashboard the reference indexes are tsid-stage-filebeat for the test environment and tsid-filebeat for production.", "notes": "Log section, first paragraph", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-c-029", "question": "In the TSID logs, what happens after a user types a wrong password several times in a row, and which ActionName/Response.Message identifies it?", "lang": "en", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:953516193"], "expected_keywords": ["User locked out", "/Account/LoginPassword", "3 consecutive"], "expected_answer": "After entering an incorrect password 3 consecutive times the user is locked out: the log has ActionName /Account/LoginPassword, Request.Action 'Login button clicked' and Response.Message 'User locked out. Redirect to login locked out page'. A single wrong attempt logs 'Invalid password' instead.", "notes": "Log list table", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-c-030", "question": "For the new GDPR-compliant log application based on MongoDB Atlas, how long are logs kept 'hot', how long are they retained on Azure immutable storage, and what is the estimated yearly cost?", "lang": "en", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:968982587"], "expected_keywords": ["MongoDB Atlas", "2 months", "TTL 2 years", "18K"], "expected_answer": "Hot logs (last 2 months) are kept in MongoDB Atlas accessible via web interface; a copy goes through Atlas Data Federation to Azure Immutable Storage with a TTL of 2 years as per GDPR policy. Estimated cost is about 18,000 credits/year, roughly 18K EUR/year for 3 Atlas clusters (Dev, Test, Prod).", "notes": "Solution and Estimated costs sections", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-c-031", "question": "How do the hot/cold retention periods used in the MongoDB audit-log PoC compare with the retention targeted by the final MongoDB solution?", "lang": "en", "category": "multi-hop", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:988184699", "confluence:TeamCore:968982587"], "expected_keywords": ["1 week", "2 weeks", "2 years"], "expected_answer": "The PoC uses short retentions to validate the mechanism: data deleted from MongoDB after 1 week (hot) and from the immutable Azure storage after 2 weeks (cold), with the previous day's logs copied at 12:01 PM. The target solution keeps hot logs for the last 2 months in MongoDB Atlas and the copy on Azure Immutable Storage with a TTL of 2 years.", "notes": "MongoDB PoC success criteria + MongoDB discovery Solution section", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-c-032", "question": "Why must the Gainsight PX tag be added manually on TeamSystem ID, and at what point in the app should the Identify call be triggered?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:682786872"], "expected_keywords": ["Identify call", "userObject", "not in OnePlatform"], "expected_answer": "Because TSID is not in OnePlatform, the Gainsight JavaScript tag has to be inserted manually in the head of all HTML pages (below any dataLayer). The Identify call must be added where user authentication occurs, i.e. when the user lands on the redirect page after a successful login; it takes a mandatory userObject and an optional accountObject.", "notes": "Gainsight PX tag setup / Identify call", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-c-033", "question": "Il social login (Google, Meta, ecc.) su TSID può essere usato anche per TSPAY?", "lang": "it", "category": "yes-no", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:998735882"], "expected_keywords": ["PSD2", "TSPAY", "SCA"], "expected_answer": "No. I requisiti normativi PSD2/SCA impongono una Strong Customer Authentication controllata dal provider finanziario e non da provider social esterni, quindi per TSPAY non è possibile usare social login o login federato: l'analisi esclude il caso TSPAY, dove è obbligatoria una password 'locale' governata da TeamSystem (il TSID).", "notes": "Opening note of 'Analysis on the introduction of the Social Login in TSID'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "cfl-c-034", "question": "What did the Legal team ask TeamSystem ID to implement regarding privacy consents and AI training, and is the AI training consent opt-in or opt-out?", "lang": "en", "category": "list", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "confluence", "expected_source_ids": ["confluence:TeamCore:637272293"], "expected_keywords": ["opt-out", "AI Act", "EDPB"], "expected_answer": "To comply with the AI Act, GDPR and the EDPB opinion, TSID must add a dedicated section where users consult/update consents (Marketing, Data sharing, AI training), add the AI training consent as opt-out, update the texts of the existing Marketing and Data Sharing policies, and send a bulk communication about the updates; new users get a multi-step consent flow after 'Create a TeamSystem ID' and existing users are re-consented at login.", "notes": "General Context + Main Requirements", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-m3-001", "question": "If I call the agyo-subscription-api subscribe endpoint without passing an expirationDate, what expiry does the package get?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/m3/metering/packages/"], "expected_keywords": ["2099-12-31", "expirationDate"], "expected_answer": "When expirationDate is omitted the package is created with expirationDate set to the conventional value 2099-12-31, which means a package with no effective expiry and auto-renewal active. If a date is given instead, the package expires on that date and is not renewable.", "notes": "Package management > As Is > Management application - agyo-subscription-api > Management of the expiry date", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-m3-002", "question": "Come fa m3-bucket-worker a evitare di processare due volte lo stesso evento di consumo?", "lang": "it", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/m3-bucket-worker/"], "expected_keywords": ["eventId", "redis", "1h"], "expected_answer": "Prima di processare un evento il worker verifica se un evento con lo stesso eventId è già presente nel key-value store Redis. Se non c'è, lo processa e salva l'eventId in Redis con un TTL di 1h: se lo stesso evento arriva di nuovo entro un'ora viene ignorato.", "notes": "m3-bucket-worker > Duplicate events management", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-m3-003", "question": "How long does a metering slot stay in cooldown before it can be reused on another company?", "lang": "en", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "git-md", "expected_source_ids": ["git-md:repo-paas-services-m3-docs-docs-metering-consumptions"], "expected_keywords": ["COOLDOWN", "6 months"], "expected_answer": "A slot put into the COOLDOWN state becomes reusable again after 6 months. The cooldown prevents the company associated with the slot from being removed just to reuse the slot on another company.", "notes": "Consumption management > Introduction", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-m3-004", "question": "Which legacy metering microservice contains the credit logic, and what does the sumEnabled flag control?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "git-md", "expected_source_ids": ["git-md:repo-paas-services-m3-docs-docs-metering-consumptions"], "expected_keywords": ["realtime-usage-collector", "sumEnabled"], "expected_answer": "The only microservice with credit logic is realtime-usage-collector. Its sumEnabled flag (true in all environments) makes Credits calculate the sum of the weights and the count of the consumptions of a package within the credit's startDate and endDate; the billing-cycle check is total consumption amount minus total credit amount against the constraint limit.", "notes": "Consumption management > realtime-usage-collector > Credits Flow", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-m3-005", "question": "Come faccio a lanciare il trasferimento dei pacchetti da una vecchia azienda a una nuova? Quale API devo chiamare e cosa devo passare?", "lang": "it", "category": "procedural", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/m3/m3/core-features/transfer-flow/"], "expected_keywords": ["/api/v1/companies/transfer", "postCompanyTransfer", "metering-service"], "expected_answer": "Si fa una sola chiamata POST /api/v1/companies/transfer al metering-service, con permesso METERING / postCompanyTransfer e header Authorization (Bearer JWT), AppName e X-Request-ID. Nel body si passano oldCompany e newCompany, ciascuna con fiscalCode e vatNumber; tutto il resto (package write, attivazione servizi M1, subscription e slot su M3) avviene in modo asincrono.", "notes": "Transfer Flow > How to Perform a Transfer > Trigger the transfer", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-m3-006", "question": "The company transfer API answered 422 — what does that mean and how do I fix it?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/m3/m3/core-features/transfer-flow/"], "expected_keywords": ["bbsId", "422"], "expected_answer": "A 422 means the destination (new) company has no associated bbsId. Both companies must already exist and the new company must be fully set up with a bbsId before retrying the transfer.", "notes": "Transfer Flow > Responses table and Q&A 'Why did I get a 422 Conflict?'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-m3-007", "question": "What token do I need to send Action events to m3-consumptions-producer and which claims must it carry?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/m3/m3/core-features/consumption-flow/"], "expected_keywords": ["M3-CONSUMPTIONS-PRODUCER:WRITE", "M2M"], "expected_answer": "The API requires an M2M (machine-to-machine) token, requested via a service desk ticket for the release of M2M credentials for m3-consumptions-producer. The token must carry the claims M3-CONSUMPTIONS-PRODUCER:<FEATURE-NAME> and M3-CONSUMPTIONS-PRODUCER:WRITE; write permission is sandboxed to the declared Feature, so cross-feature event generation is blocked.", "notes": "Consumption Flow > How to send an Action Event? > Authentication", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-m3-008", "question": "Da cosa dipende se un'Action inviata a Smartmeter viene instradata nel flusso tecnico oppure in quello monetizzato?", "lang": "it", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/m3/m3/core-features/consumption-flow/"], "expected_keywords": ["Monetization Enabled", "m3-consumptions-producer", "Capability Catalog"], "expected_answer": "Il producer non sceglie nulla a runtime: m3-consumptions-producer consulta la propria replica del Capability Catalog e, se la Feature ha il flag Monetization Enabled a true, instrada l'evento nel Monetized Consumption Flow; se è false lo manda solo al Technical Consumption Flow (bucket). Una configurazione errata del flag causa errori di billing o perdita di dati non monetizzati.", "notes": "Consumption Flow > M3 Internal Processing Flows", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-m3-009", "question": "What is the endpoint to lock a slot in M3 and what does it return?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/m3/m3/core-features/slots-flow/"], "expected_keywords": ["/api/v2/slot", "Producer", "X-Correlation-ID"], "expected_answer": "You call POST /api/v2/slot/{serviceName}/{type}/{keyword}/lock with OnePlatform authentication and the Producer permission, plus the mandatory headers Authorization, X-App-Name, X-App-Version, X-Correlation-ID and X-Request-ID (optional payload map in the body). On 200 OK it returns the slot id, which you must persist and reuse to unlock via POST /api/v2/slot/{slotId}/unlock.", "notes": "Slots Flow > Producer APIs (Write) > Lock a Slot", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-m3-010", "question": "What are the validation rules on the paging and status parameters when listing slots through the read API?", "lang": "en", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/m3/m3/core-features/slots-flow/"], "expected_keywords": ["1..100", "COOLDOWN", "slots"], "expected_answer": "For GET /api/v1/{keyword}/{type}/slots the keyword must be a valid UUID, type non-empty, the optional status must be one of FREE, LOCKED or COOLDOWN, page must be >= 0 and size must be in 1..100. Invalid values give a 400 with type IllegalArgumentException.", "notes": "Slots Flow > Read APIs > List Slots", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-m3-011", "question": "Which actions can arrive on the subscription webhook that a Feature's Config Service must handle?", "lang": "en", "category": "list", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/m3/m3/core-features/feature-activation-flow/"], "expected_keywords": ["ENABLE_READONLY_SUBSCRIPTION", "DISABLE_READONLY_SUBSCRIPTION"], "expected_answer": "The webhook can send ENABLE_SUBSCRIPTION (activate the feature), DISABLE_SUBSCRIPTION (deactivate it), ENABLE_READONLY_SUBSCRIPTION (activate in read-only mode, e.g. consumption exhausted or administrative block) and DISABLE_READONLY_SUBSCRIPTION (sent only when a previously read-only subscription is reactivated). The Feature must return HTTP 200 for success.", "notes": "Feature Activation Flow > Flow", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-m3-012", "question": "Se il mio Config Service risponde con un errore alla POST del webhook di attivazione, quante volte riprova Metering e con quali attese?", "lang": "it", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/m3/m3/core-features/feature-activation-flow/"], "expected_keywords": ["5/10/15/20/25", "SERVICES_SUBSCRIPTION_WEBHOOK:WRITE"], "expected_answer": "Metering considera la chiamata riuscita solo con HTTP 200; qualsiasi altra risposta è un fallimento. Non c'è altra gestione dell'errore oltre a 5 retry con attese incrementali di 5/10/15/20/25 minuti. Il webhook deve essere protetto con un Bearer token M2M che include il permesso SERVICES_SUBSCRIPTION_WEBHOOK:WRITE; in caso di errore si può restituire un JSON con chiave message per il logging.", "notes": "Feature Activation Flow > Feature Implementation > Webhook Configuration", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-m3-013", "question": "What are the three core domains that make up the M3 monetization platform?", "lang": "en", "category": "list", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/m3/m3/getting-started/architecture/"], "expected_keywords": ["Service Manager", "Subscription Manager", "Smartmeter"], "expected_answer": "M3 consists of three domains: the Service Manager (Capability Catalog, Feature Activation Flow, Feature Monitoring), the Subscription Manager (subscription lifecycle and consumption assignment) and the Smartmeter (collection of Actions and Slots, conversion into Consumptions and bucketization).", "notes": "M3 Architecture Overview > Topology of Core Components", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-m3-014", "question": "Nel glossario M3 cosa si intende per Tier e a quale concetto del vecchio metering corrisponde?", "lang": "it", "category": "definition", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/m3/m3/getting-started/glossary/"], "expected_keywords": ["Tier", "Family", "Commercial Offer"], "expected_answer": "Un Tier è una specifica configurazione di una Commercial Offer che definisce l'elenco di Features e Constraints inclusi nell'offerta. Nel vecchio M1/Metering corrisponde al concetto di Family.", "notes": "Glossary table, row Tier", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-m3-015", "question": "In the Smartmeter architecture, what is the tombstone strategy of the relay component?", "lang": "en", "category": "definition", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/m3/m3/getting-started/smartmeter/"], "expected_keywords": ["Tombstone", "m3-consumptions-relay"], "expected_answer": "When m3-consumptions-relay finds anomalous events during dequeuing (e.g. erroneously processed identifiers reaching the storage) or hits idempotency exceptions, it turns those incongruities into Tombstone events: they are blocked (not sent to the broker) and archived in separate tables for audit or manual resolution.", "notes": "Smartmeter Architecture > Main Components > 2. M3 Consumptions Relay", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-m3-016", "question": "How does the release procedure differ between the legacy metering services and the new M3 services (branches, Maven command, tag format)?", "lang": "en", "category": "multi-hop", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "git-md", "expected_source_ids": ["git-md:repo-paas-services-m3-docs-docs-metering-guides", "git-md:repo-paas-services-m3-docs-dev-0-legacy-start-up"], "expected_keywords": ["release:prepare", "metering-package-write-1.3.6", "v1.1"], "expected_answer": "Legacy metering services use three environment branches (dev, test, master): after merging to dev you run mvn release:clean release:prepare, which creates a tag like metering-package-write-1.3.6, then you rebase the test/master branch on that tag and push. New M3 services work from main: mvn release:prepare creates a tag such as v1.1, the CI pipeline builds and generates deploy commands for TEST and PROD, and major version bumps require team approval.", "notes": "guides.md 'Release of a service > New development' vs start-up.md '4. Release Flow'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-m3-017", "question": "Does the M3 database keep consumption data older than the last two billing cycles, and which database engine was chosen?", "lang": "en", "category": "yes-no", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/m3/adrs/ADR00001_data_store/"], "expected_keywords": ["two billing cycles", "PostgreSQL", "CockroachDB"], "expected_answer": "No. ADR00001 decided to use a clean version of PostgreSQL (not tools like CockroachDB) and to move the heavy reporting, analytics and archive operations to the Data Lake, keeping only write operations for the last two billing cycles; the implication is that M3 contains no data older than the last two billing cycles. The status is to be re-evaluated after analyzing production consumption.", "notes": "ADR00001 > Summary and Implications", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-m3-018", "question": "Quale rule engine è stato scelto nell'ADR00002 del metering e qual è lo stato della decisione?", "lang": "it", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/m3/adrs/ADR00002_rule_engine/"], "expected_keywords": ["Drools", "Permanent"], "expected_answer": "È stato scelto il rule engine Drools per gestire dinamicamente le configurazioni di subscription e consumi dei pacchetti senza scrivere codice e senza deploy del servizio a ogni nuova configurazione. Lo stato della decisione è Permanent.", "notes": "ADR00002 > Summary > Decision / Status", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-m3-019", "question": "What are the production timeout values of the data-retention-scheduler between the retention states?", "lang": "en", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "git-md", "expected_source_ids": ["git-md:repo-paas-services-m3-docs-docs-metering-data-retention"], "expected_keywords": ["ARCHIVING_TIMEOUT_IN_SECONDS", "10368000", "3888000"], "expected_answer": "In production ALERT_TIMEOUT_BEFORE_ARCHIVING_IN_SECONDS is 3888000 (45 days, STARTED to ARCHIVE_INIT), ARCHIVING_TIMEOUT_IN_SECONDS is 5184000 (60 days, to ARCHIVED), ALERT_TIMEOUT_BEFORE_DELETION_IN_SECONDS is 9072000 (105 days, to DELETE_INIT) and DELETION_TIMEOUT_IN_SECONDS is 10368000 (120 days, to DELETED). SCHEDULER_PERIOD is 3600 seconds (1 hour).", "notes": "Data retention > Data retention scheduler", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-m3-020", "question": "Can I scale the digital-data-retention service to several replicas?", "lang": "en", "category": "yes-no", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "git-md", "expected_source_ids": ["git-md:repo-paas-services-m3-docs-docs-metering-data-retention"], "expected_keywords": ["digital-data-retention", "SINGLE instance"], "expected_answer": "No. digital-data-retention must run as ONE SINGLE instance: with several instances there is a risk of executing the data retention process more than once. It dequeues the activation/readonly/deactivation events and calls postRetention on data-retention-write only when all services of the same App Id are readonly or deactivated (for readonly, only if the package is READONLY_EXPIRE_DATE_REACHED).", "notes": "Data retention > Digital data retention", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-m3-021", "question": "Come posso simulare il purge della tabella archived_invoice prima di cancellare davvero i record?", "lang": "it", "category": "procedural", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "git-md", "expected_source_ids": ["git-md:repo-paas-services-m3-docs-dev-procedures-purge-archived-invoices"], "expected_keywords": ["-simulate", "purge-archived-invoices", "PURGE_BEFORE_DATE"], "expected_answer": "Dopo aver configurato il .env (DB_*, PURGE_BEFORE_DATE che deve essere almeno 2 anni nel passato, BATCH_SIZE, BATCH_DELAY_MS, MAX_ROWS_PER_RUN) si lancia node src/index.js -scope=purge-archived-invoices -simulate: esegue solo una COUNT_BIG(*) senza cancellare righe. Verificato il conteggio, si esegue il purge vero, prima con un cap (MAX_ROWS_PER_RUN=500000) e poi senza.", "notes": "Procedure: Purge Archived Invoices > Step 3 and Step 4", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-m3-022", "question": "How much disk space do I need to build the temporary timestamp index on archived_invoice before a purge, and how big is the finished index?", "lang": "en", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "git-md", "expected_source_ids": ["git-md:repo-paas-services-m3-docs-dev-procedures-purge-archived-invoices"], "expected_keywords": ["IX_archived_invoice_timestamp", "80 GB", "RESUMABLE"], "expected_answer": "Creating IX_archived_invoice_timestamp (ONLINE = ON, RESUMABLE = ON, MAXDOP = 4) needs about 80 GB of free space in the user DB for the in-DB sort peak; the finished index takes about 31-41 GB and can be reclaimed (~40 GB) by dropping it afterwards. Check free space with EXEC sp_spaceused first; without the index each 50k-row batch does a full heap scan (~200 s).", "notes": "Procedure: Purge Archived Invoices > Step 2 and Step 8", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-m3-023", "question": "I need to add an optional attribute to the Subscriptions Data Product without breaking existing consumers. What's the correct way to declare and roll it out?", "lang": "en", "category": "procedural", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "git-md", "expected_source_ids": ["git-md:repo-paas-services-m3-docs-dev-procedures-evolve-data-product"], "expected_keywords": ["Witboost", "Databricks", "null"], "expected_answer": "Model the field as nullable with a default on every producer layer (in m3-subscriptions-worker for the Subscriptions DP), declare it in the DP JSON Schema as type [\"<type>\", \"null\"] and do not add it to required, always emit it (null when unset, no Jackson NON_NULL), do not backfill historical rows, and update the registered schema in Witboost (Builder, Edit and Test, partial deploy) before emitting non-null values. Then ask the Hermes/Data Product team to add the column to the Databricks table, since the Liquibase Tech Adapter does not manage schema changes.", "notes": "Procedure: Create or Evolve a Data Product > Strategy and Steps 1-5", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-m3-024", "question": "What are the standard Azure Service Bus settings for M3 (delivery count, lock duration, message TTL, queue size)?", "lang": "en", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "git-md", "expected_source_ids": ["git-md:repo-paas-services-m3-docs-dev-0-legacy-service-bus-semantic"], "expected_keywords": ["P14D", "PT1M", "PT5M"], "expected_answer": "Max delivery count 10 before dead-lettering, lock duration PT1M for topics and PT5M for queues, message TTL P14D (14 days), queue max size 5120 MB, minimum TLS 1.2, dead lettering on expiration always enabled, SKU Premium in prod (capacity 1) and Standard in dev/test.", "notes": "M3 Azure Service Bus & Dapr Configuration Reference > 2. Standard Configuration Values", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-m3-025", "question": "Quali endpoint di health deve esporre obbligatoriamente ogni microservizio M3?", "lang": "it", "category": "list", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "git-md", "expected_source_ids": ["git-md:repo-paas-services-m3-docs-dev-0-legacy-monitoring"], "expected_keywords": ["/q/health/ready", "/q/info", "/q/health/live"], "expected_answer": "Ogni servizio M3 deve esporre gli endpoint Quarkus /q/health (health complessivo, 200 con status UP), /q/health/live (liveness), /q/health/ready (readiness: DB connesso, Dapr pronto) e /q/info (versione, build time, commit SHA, environment). Le probe Kubernetes devono puntare a questi endpoint.", "notes": "M3 Monitoring & Observability > 1. Health & Readiness Endpoints", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-m3-026", "question": "What reliability targets do M3 services commit to for availability, latency and error rate?", "lang": "en", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "git-md", "expected_source_ids": ["git-md:repo-paas-services-m3-docs-dev-0-legacy-monitoring"], "expected_keywords": ["99.9%", "500ms", "99.95%"], "expected_answer": "Standard SLOs over a 30-day rolling window: availability >= 99.9%, p50 latency <= 100ms, p99 latency <= 500ms, message processing >= 99.95% and 5xx error rate <= 0.1%. The error budget for 99.9% availability is about 43 minutes per month; when exhausted, feature releases are frozen until reliability is restored.", "notes": "M3 Monitoring & Observability > 9. Service Level Objectives", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-m3-027", "question": "Which application properties must I set to enable the OnePlatform bearer-token authentication mechanism from m3-utils in a Quarkus service?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/m3-utils/features/oneplatform-http-authentication-mechanism/"], "expected_keywords": ["oneplatform.authorized.subdomain", "quarkus.rest-client.http.platform.authentication.uri.url", "5000"], "expected_answer": "You set the app identity (oneplatform.app.name, oneplatform.app.version), the action-building keys oneplatform.authorized.subdomain and oneplatform.authorized.version (e.g. m3:smartmeter:v1:httprequest.get), and the REST client URLs quarkus.rest-client.http.platform.authentication.uri.url and quarkus.rest-client.http.platform.authorizer.uri.url (optionally connection-timeout/read-timeout). The mechanism runs at priority 5000 in the Quarkus authentication chain and returns a 401 challenge on failure.", "notes": "OnePlatform HTTP Authentication Mechanism > Configuration", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-m3-028", "question": "Nel m3-outbox-relay per quanto tempo vengono conservati gli eventi già consegnati e con quale proprietà si cambia?", "lang": "it", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "git-md", "expected_source_ids": ["git-md:repo-paas-services-m3-infrastructure-m3-outbox-relay-docs-index"], "expected_keywords": ["outbox.retention.period.days", "DELIVERED", "DeleteDeliveredEvents"], "expected_answer": "Il use case DeleteDeliveredEvents, eseguito come job schedulato dal modulo cron, cancella periodicamente solo gli eventi in stato DELIVERED più vecchi del periodo di retention, che di default è 7 giorni e si configura con outbox.retention.period.days.", "notes": "M3 Outbox Relay Documentation > Core Concepts > Retention Policy", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-m3-029", "question": "What changed between the V1 and V2 store-consumption APIs of m3-consumptions-producer?", "lang": "en", "category": "comparison", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/m3-consumptions-producer/"], "expected_keywords": ["executionDate", "consumptionDate", "/api/v2/consumptions"], "expected_answer": "V1 (POST /api/v1/consumptions/) uses a JWT issued by the M3 Identity Provider with the Producer role and fields type/consumptionDate, and requires X-App-Name and X-App-Version headers. V2 (POST /api/v2/consumptions/) uses OnePlatform authentication via @HttpAuthenticationMechanism(\"OnePlatformAuthentication\") with the Producer permission, renames type to action and consumptionDate to executionDate, and drops X-App-Name/X-App-Version because appName is derived from the token roles. V2 deprecates V1 while keeping backward compatibility.", "notes": "M3 Consumptions Producer > Consumption Storage vs Consumption Storage V2", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-m3-030", "question": "Which checks does m3-subscriptions-subscriber run before accepting a POST /api/v1/subscription request?", "lang": "en", "category": "list", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/m3-subscriptions-subscriber/"], "expected_keywords": ["subscriberId", "resolveServices", "ServiceCatalogReadClient"], "expected_answer": "SubscriptionCreateUseCase validates that subscriberId is a valid UUID, that packageId and subscriberId are not empty, that endDate is later than startDate, that there are no overlapping subscriptions with the same subscriberId and packageId in the same timespan, and (via resolveServices, calling getServicesByIds on ServiceCatalogReadClient) that all included services exist and are enabled. Only then it sends the create event to m3-subscription-worker.", "notes": "m3-subscription-subscriber > Flow > Subscribing a package to a subscriber > Validation / Execution", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-m3-031", "question": "Quando l'aggregatore dei consumi chiama metering-package-write per mettere un pacchetto in readonly, e come evita chiamate duplicate?", "lang": "it", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/m3-subscriptions-consumptions-aggregate/api/"], "expected_keywords": ["constraintLimitReached", "N_DIPENDENTI", "RedisCommandCache"], "expected_answer": "m3-subscriptions-consumptions-aggregate invoca POST /package/{id}/readonly/constraintLimitReached su metering-package-write quando viene raggiunto il limite del constraint N_DIPENDENTI, così da mettere il pacchetto in readonly. Per non ripetere la chiamata usa una cache Redis (RedisCommandCache) per package ID con TTL configurabile, di default 1 ora; se la chiamata fallisce l'entry non viene scritta e il consumo successivo ritenta.", "notes": "API Reference > Outbound HTTP Calls > constraintLimitReached", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-m3-032", "question": "Which extradata keys does the TSH-PMS feature receive at activation, and which package makes the governingApp flag true?", "lang": "en", "category": "multi-hop", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "git-md", "expected_source_ids": ["git-md:repo-paas-services-m3-docs-dev-core-features-extra-data-management", "devportal:default/component/m3/metering/packages/"], "expected_keywords": ["governingApp", "TSH-PMS", "tsIntegrationHub"], "expected_answer": "TSH-PMS receives seven extradata keys, all false by default: enterprise, guestPortal, governingApp, domotics, HOAU, tsIntegrationHub and externalIntegrationHub. governingApp becomes true when the owner has an active TSH_GOV_APP package (enterprise needs TSH_ENTERPRISE, guestPortal TSH_ENTERPRISE or TSH_PRO, domotics TSH_DOMOTICS, HOAU TSH_HOAU, tsIntegrationHub TSH_ENTERPRISE/TSH_START/TSH_PRO, externalIntegrationHub TSH_ENTERPRISE).", "notes": "extra-data-management.md 'Keys produced > Feature-specific keys' + packages.md 'metering-service-activator > Management of the extradata'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-ai-001", "question": "In Ticket Tinder v4, what happens when BERT associates a ticket with more than one candidate skill?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/ai-services/api/customer_support/customer_support_ticket_tinder/"], "expected_keywords": ["ticket_tinder_agent", "selectedSkill"], "expected_answer": "The ticket_tinder_agent assistant is invoked through LiteLLM with the ticket description and the candidate list and must return one of the candidates, which becomes the selectedSkill. If the LLM returns a skill outside the list, an empty answer, or the call fails, the service falls back to the first candidate skill; the selection never blocks the prediction.", "notes": "Version 4 > Single skill selection (LLM)", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-ai-002", "question": "Dove vengono pubblicati gli eventi di predizione di Ticket Tinder e in quale tabella Delta finiscono in produzione?", "lang": "it", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/ai-services/api/customer_support/customer_support_ticket_tinder/"], "expected_keywords": ["TICKET_TINDER_PREDICTION_TOPIC", "ticket_tinder_prediction"], "expected_answer": "Al termine di ogni predizione il servizio pubblica un evento CloudEvents 'Ticket Tinder Prediction' per ciascun ticket sull'outbox topic configurato con la variabile TICKET_TINDER_PREDICTION_TOPIC; Hermes lo trasferisce su Kafka e un notebook PySpark su Databricks lo scrive nella Silver table. In prod la tabella è aiplatform_prod.ml_predictions_and_feedbacks.ticket_tinder_prediction.", "notes": "Prediction events (outbox) + Data Product section", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-ai-003", "question": "Can I send a partial update of a department's skill matrix to the Ticket Tinder skill-matrix API, only for the operators that changed?", "lang": "en", "category": "yes-no", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/ai-services/api/customer_support/customer_support_ticket_tinder_config_api/"], "expected_keywords": ["skill-matrix", "No partial updates"], "expected_answer": "No. For every modification of a department's skill matrix the complete skill matrix must be re-sent via POST /customer-support/api/v1/skill-matrix; no partial updates are supported. The update is department-specific and is propagated immediately to the assignment models.", "notes": "Skill Matrix > Notes", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-ai-004", "question": "Che differenza c'è tra aggiornare la skill matrix e aggiornare i case type di un dipartimento, in termini di quando Ticket Tinder inizia a usare i nuovi dati?", "lang": "it", "category": "comparison", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/ai-services/api/customer_support/customer_support_ticket_tinder_config_api/"], "expected_keywords": ["re-training", "case-type"], "expected_answer": "L'aggiornamento della skill matrix (POST /customer-support/api/v1/skill-matrix) viene propagato immediatamente ai modelli di assegnazione. L'aggiornamento dei case type (POST /customer-support/api/v1/case-type) invece non è immediato: serve un re-training del modello, e solo i case type coinvolti nell'ultimo training vengono considerati nell'assegnazione.", "notes": "Skill Matrix Notes vs Case Type Notes", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-ai-005", "question": "Which library solves the optimisation problem behind Ticket Tinder's operator assignment, and what constraints does the model enforce?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/ai-services/api/customer_support/customer_support_ticket_tinder_lp_ass/"], "expected_keywords": ["PuLP", "Linear Programming"], "expected_answer": "The assignment is a binary integer linear programming problem solved with PuLP. It maximises the total compatibility score between tickets and operators subject to: each ticket assigned to exactly one operator, a maximum capacity per operator derived from FTE, a minimum skill level, and cluster compatibility.", "notes": "Problem Formalization + final note on PuLP", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-ai-006", "question": "If a caller of the TSDesk ticket gateway omits priority and contact reason, which defaults are applied and how can I change them?", "lang": "en", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/ai-services/docs/tsdesk_ticket_gateway_flow/"], "expected_keywords": ["TSDESK_DEFAULT_PRIORITY_CODE", "Chiarimento funzionale"], "expected_answer": "The default priority is code 3 (Non Bloccante) and the default contact reason is ID 18 (Chiarimento funzionale). They are configurable with the environment variables TSDESK_DEFAULT_PRIORITY_CODE and TSDESK_DEFAULT_CONTACT_REASON_ID.", "notes": "Dynamic Priority & Contact Reason Resolution > Configuration", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-ai-007", "question": "Quanto può pesare al massimo un allegato inviato al tsdesk_ticket_gw e come viene costruito l'AttachmentId nel payload del ticket?", "lang": "it", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/ai-services/docs/tsdesk_ticket_gateway_flow/"], "expected_keywords": ["10 MiB", "AttachmentId"], "expected_answer": "La dimensione decodificata dell'allegato è limitata a 10 MiB (MAX_ATTACHMENT_SIZE_BYTES); oltre si riceve HTTP 422 prima di qualsiasi upload. Dopo l'upload su POST /TicketAttachment TSDesk restituisce un Id numerico e l'executor compone l'AttachmentId come {numeric_id}*\\*{filename}, ad esempio 638961402987299069*\\*670660.jpg.", "notes": "Pre-ticket Attachments > Size limit / How the attachment is linked", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-ai-008", "question": "Can I call the Reconciliation Tinder API with a batch of bank transactions, and what are the requirements to be allowed to use the service?", "lang": "en", "category": "yes-no", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/ai-services/api/reconciliation_service/"], "expected_keywords": ["Banklink", "Hermes", "item-id"], "expected_answer": "No: the input must be a single bank transaction, batch processing is not supported. To use the service you must implement user feedback events sent to Hermes, the invoices to suggest must already be in Datalake, and the item-id header / a TS Digital token are required; the recommended integration is through Banklink via Hermes events rather than calling the API directly.", "notes": "Service notes and requirements", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-ai-009", "question": "How does the NIF Predictor work out the Spanish tax ID of a counterparty from a bank transaction description?", "lang": "en", "category": "list", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/ai-services/api/international/nif_predictor/"], "expected_keywords": ["ai-ner", "TF-IDF", "unresolved"], "expected_answer": "It runs a waterfall of up to three techniques, stopping at the first confident one: (1) exact match of the normalized description against historical data (own company first, then global), (2) similarity match using TF-IDF and cosine similarity, (3) counterparty name extraction via the ai-ner service followed by a fuzzy match against the company's own registry. If none clears the purity gates the result is 'unresolved' with an empty NIFCode instead of a guess.", "notes": "How does it decide? + The matching logic in detail", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-ai-010", "question": "Quali sono le soglie di default (purity e similarity) configurabili via variabili d'ambiente nel NIF Predictor?", "lang": "it", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/ai-services/api/international/nif_predictor/"], "expected_keywords": ["NIF_PREDICTOR_EXACT_MATCH_PURITY_THRESHOLD", "0.75"], "expected_answer": "NIF_PREDICTOR_EXACT_MATCH_PURITY_THRESHOLD = 0.9 (step 1), NIF_PREDICTOR_SIMILARITY_THRESHOLD = 0.75 (cosine similarity, step 2), NIF_PREDICTOR_SIMILARITY_PURITY_THRESHOLD = 0.6 (majority vote tra i vicini, step 2), NIF_PREDICTOR_TEMPLATE_PURITY_THRESHOLD = 0.5 (pre-check che salta la chiamata NER, step 3) e NIF_PREDICTOR_REGISTRY_FUZZY_THRESHOLD = 85.0 (score WRatio di rapidfuzz, step 3).", "notes": "Purity gating table / Configuration reference", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-ai-011", "question": "How do I create a team, a user and a virtual key on the LiteLLM proxy used by ai-services in the dev environment?", "lang": "en", "category": "procedural", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/ai-services/docs/ai-litellm/"], "expected_keywords": ["/key/generate", "/team/new"], "expected_answer": "Against https://ai-litellm-dev.agyo.io send three POST requests with Authorization and x-litellm-key headers: /team/new (with team_alias, organization_id and models, using the master key), then /user/new (username, team_id, user_role such as internal_user_viewer, using the team key), then /key/generate with the models list and the user_id returned earlier. Save the returned sk- key because it is shown only once; for test use ai-litellm-test.agyo.io and for prod contact the project owners.", "notes": "Virtual Key and Permission Hierarchy > 4. Creating Virtual Keys", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-ai-012", "question": "According to the ai-services energy impact study, how much energy and CO2 does a typical 4000-token request cost on GPT-4o compared with GPT-4o-mini?", "lang": "en", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/ai-services/docs/ai_impact/"], "expected_keywords": ["GPT-4o-mini", "1.3 Wh"], "expected_answer": "For a 4000-token request GPT-4o consumes about 1.3 Wh (~6x10^-4 Wh per token), corresponding to ~0.35 g CO2 in Italy, while GPT-4o-mini needs about 0.13 Wh (~6x10^-5 Wh per token) and ~0.035 g CO2, i.e. roughly ten times less. The estimate assumes an Italian grid intensity of 270 g CO2/kWh and an error margin of about ±50%.", "notes": "Results / Table 1", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-ai-013", "question": "Quale modello LLM usa l'endpoint comment_report del pod ai-llm-tasks e come posso cambiarlo senza modificare il codice?", "lang": "it", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/ai-services/api/llm_tasks/comment_report/"], "expected_keywords": ["gemini-2.5-pro", "REPORT_COMMENT_MODEL"], "expected_answer": "L'endpoint POST /llm-tasks/api/v0/comment_report delega a un proxy LiteLLM usando attualmente gemini-2.5-pro. Il modello si cambia con la variabile d'ambiente REPORT_COMMENT_MODEL (default gemini-2.5-pro), senza modifiche al codice.", "notes": "Overview + Configuration (environment variables)", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-ai-014", "question": "In the fintech product-to-clusters API, which cluster fields are always populated in the response and why are the others sometimes missing?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/ai-services/api/fintech/cpmatcher_from_product_to_clusters/"], "expected_keywords": ["ATECODivisionCode", "macroRegionDesc"], "expected_answer": "Only ATECODivisionCode and macroRegionDesc are always valued. The other fields (ATECOClassCode, regionDesc, provinceDesc, cityDesc, postalCode) are filled from coarser to finer grain, because finer clusters may be too small to return meaningful data without privacy risks; e.g. cityDesc is never filled if provinceDesc is not.", "notes": "Version 0 > Response", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-ai-015", "question": "Cosa fa l'API hotel_price_recommender e quali parametri accetta in input?", "lang": "it", "category": "definition", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/ai-services/api/micro_vertical/hotel_price_recommender/"], "expected_keywords": ["pricePred", "occupancyTh"], "expected_answer": "Suggerisce un prezzo per ogni tipologia di camera di una struttura per i prossimi 365 giorni. In input riceve hotelId, occupancyTh (float tra 0 e 1, occupazione richiesta per room type) e opzionalmente startDate/endDate in formato ISO; in output restituisce un uuid e, per ogni room type, una lista di date con pricePred e occupancyPred.", "notes": "micro-vertical/api/v0/hotel_price_recommender", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-ai-016", "question": "When I draw highlights on a PDF from the documents/locate response, what coordinate convention does bbox use and why must I avoid PDF.js convertToViewportPoint?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/ai-shared-api/en/documents-chunk-locate/"], "expected_keywords": ["bbox", "top-left", "convertToViewportPoint"], "expected_answer": "bbox is [x0, top, x1, bottom] in PDF points (1/72 inch) with the origin at the top-left of the page, and page numbers are 1-based. Because the origin is already top-left (same as the HTML canvas) you just multiply by the render scale; convertToViewportPoint must not be used because it expects native PDF coordinates with a bottom-left origin.", "notes": "Response > Field semantics; Frontend integration guide > Drawing highlights on PDF", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-ai-017", "question": "Come va nominata la Service Action di Metering per un tool di un MCP server dell'AI Assistant, e cosa succede se mando eventi prima di registrarla?", "lang": "it", "category": "procedural", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/ai-platform-docs/consumption-and-metering/"], "expected_keywords": ["CalendarTool_CreateEvent", "AI-ASSISTANT"], "expected_answer": "Ogni tool deve avere una Service Action registrata in Metering con il nome nel formato <MCPServerName>_<ToolName>, ad esempio CalendarTool_CreateEvent, sotto il servizio AI-ASSISTANT; la registrazione si richiede via email al product owner di Metering. Se gli eventi arrivano prima della registrazione Metering li accetta senza assegnarli, e una volta registrata l'action gli eventi passati vengono recuperati senza doverli reinviare.", "notes": "AI Assistant > 2. Register the Service Action in Metering", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-ai-018", "question": "Which chunking strategies of the K-Hub ingestion pipeline carry segment metadata such as page_number into the resulting chunks?", "lang": "en", "category": "list", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/ai-platform-docs/documents-and-rag/customer-documents/ingestion/configuration/"], "expected_keywords": ["paginated", "agentic"], "expected_answer": "Only recursive (copies the metadata of the segment with the greatest character overlap) and paginated (direct 1:1 copy, one segment per chunk) propagate segment metadata. semantic, agentic and \"None\" operate on the concatenated text and do not, unless you separately enable use_document_structure with segmentation_method: propagate and propagate_segment_metadata: true.", "notes": "chunk_text > Segment Metadata Propagation into Chunks", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-ai-019", "question": "What is the default min_score of the Semantic Search Service and how is the MongoDB numCandidates value computed?", "lang": "en", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/ai-platform-docs/documents-and-rag/customer-documents/semantic-search-service/details/"], "expected_keywords": ["0.85", "numCandidates"], "expected_answer": "The default min_score is 0.85 (cascading request param → use case config → settings.yaml default) and it is not applied in hybrid mode. numCandidates = min(20 × num_results, 10,000); the 20x multiplier is tunable via vector_search.num_candidates_multiplier in settings.yaml.", "notes": "API Reference > Request Body; Performance & Tuning", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-ai-020", "question": "Se nell'ingestion K-Hub lascio il modello di embedding di default, quante dimensioni devo indicare nel vector_search_index del file usecase.yaml della Semantic Search?", "lang": "it", "category": "multi-hop", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/ai-platform-docs/documents-and-rag/customer-documents/ingestion/configuration/", "devportal:default/component/ai-platform-docs/documents-and-rag/customer-documents/semantic-search-service/details/"], "expected_keywords": ["text-embedding-ada-002", "1536"], "expected_answer": "Il modello di default di create_embeddings.model_name è text-embedding-ada-002, che produce vettori a 1536 dimensioni; quindi vector_search_index.vector_fields[].num_dimensions deve essere 1536 (con similarity_metric cosine e path chunk_vector), altrimenti l'indicizzazione fallisce o la ricerca restituisce risultati errati. Se si cambia modello va ricreato l'indice e reindicizzati tutti i documenti.", "notes": "ingestion-configuration: create_embeddings.model_name; SSS details: Use Case Configuration File", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-ai-021", "question": "On the LLM Gateway, when should I call /v1/models versus /v1/model/info?", "lang": "en", "category": "comparison", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/ai-platform-docs/genai-platform/llm-gateway/models/"], "expected_keywords": ["/v1/model/info", "x-litellm-api-key"], "expected_answer": "/v1/models returns only the model IDs enabled for your key (OpenAI /models shape) and is enough when you just need the value to pass as model. /v1/model/info returns richer per-model metadata (provider, mode, context window, supported features, pricing) useful for routing, UI dropdowns or budgeting. Both are called with the x-litellm-api-key header set to your LLM_GATEWAY_API_KEY.", "notes": "Discover available models / Detailed model info", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-ai-022", "question": "Come devo chiamare l'alias di una API key del LLM Gateway? Ci sono esempi di nomi corretti e sbagliati?", "lang": "it", "category": "procedural", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/ai-platform-docs/genai-platform/llm-gateway/key-aliases/"], "expected_keywords": ["mcp-fatture-in-cloud", "kebab-case"], "expected_answer": "Il formato è <purpose>-<scope> in kebab-case minuscolo, dove purpose è il ruolo funzionale (mcp, chatbot, rag, embeddings, evals, smoke-test, local-dev) e scope è l'applicazione o servizio che usa la chiave, es. mcp-fatture-in-cloud o chatbot-fic-assistant. Non vanno inclusi owner, team o ambiente (già tracciati da LiteLLM) né suffissi di versione o date: le chiavi si ruotano riemettendole con lo stesso alias. Esempi sbagliati: fatture-in-cloud-prod, mcp-server, crm-mcp-v2.", "notes": "Format / Rules of thumb / Examples", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-ai-023", "question": "How do I expose a newly deployed MCP server through the AI Platform request handler so it is reachable under /mcp/<alias>?", "lang": "en", "category": "procedural", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/ai-platform-docs/genai-platform/mcp/publishing-mcp-server/"], "expected_keywords": ["ingress-mcp.yaml", "gateway-mcp.yaml"], "expected_answer": "In the ai-requests-handler project of the k8s-oneplatform-deploy-configs repo add a rule under rules[].http.paths in ingress-mcp.yaml for every environment (dev, test, prod) with path /mcp/<your-mcp-server-alias>(/|$)(.*) pointing to your Kubernetes Service on port 8000. In dev only, also add two rules to gateway-mcp.yaml: an HTTPS redirect rule in the HTTPRoute ending with -http and a backend routing rule with URLRewrite to /$2. This step is not needed if the server is registered with its internal cluster address.", "notes": "Register the MCP Server Route", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-ai-024", "question": "Which MLflow scorers does the MCP blueprint apply in the pre-deploy evaluation of MCP tools?", "lang": "en", "category": "list", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/ai-platform-docs/genai-platform/mcp/evaluating-mcp-tools/"], "expected_keywords": ["RelevanceToQuery", "ExpectationsGuidelines"], "expected_answer": "Three scorers: RelevanceToQuery (built-in LLM judge checking the output is relevant to the request), ExpectationsGuidelines (built-in LLM judge scoring the output against the natural-language guidelines in the dataset expectations) and entity_in_output (a custom code-based scorer that deterministically checks the expected entity appears in the output).", "notes": "MLFlow scorers", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-ai-025", "question": "A cosa serve l'header X-Assistant-ID che l'orchestratore TS AI inoltra ai server MCP a ogni tool call?", "lang": "it", "category": "definition", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/ai-platform-docs/ts-ai-and-orchestrator/headers/"], "expected_keywords": ["X-Assistant-ID"], "expected_answer": "Indica quale assistant ha originato la chiamata (l'assistant nominato nella run). Poiché lo stesso MCP server può essere collegato a molti assistant, permette di applicare comportamenti o contenuti specifici per assistant, di scoprire dati e default al contesto di prodotto giusto e di attribuire uso e osservabilità per assistant; se il tool si comporta allo stesso modo per tutti può ignorarlo.", "notes": "The special header: X-Assistant-ID", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-ai-026", "question": "How long do files attached to a TS AI chat stay available in the Assetstore, and can I extend the retention for my assistant?", "lang": "en", "category": "yes-no", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/ai-platform-docs/ts-ai-and-orchestrator/upload-documents/"], "expected_keywords": ["Assetstore", "2-day", "MAX_ATTACHMENTS"], "expected_answer": "Attachments live in the Assetstore for a hard, global 2-day TTL that cannot be extended per assistant, tenant or file; a GET on day 3 returns 404 NOT_FOUND with no recovery. If the content must outlive the conversation you have to copy the bytes into storage you own within the 2-day window. Runs also accept at most 10 attachments by default (MAX_ATTACHMENTS, clamped to 1..100).", "notes": "Retention and limits", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-ai-027", "question": "Which Databricks workspace hosts the dev TS AI observability MLflow experiment, and which Entra ID group do I need to be nested under to write traces to it?", "lang": "en", "category": "multi-hop", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "git-md", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/ai-platform-docs/ai-platform-internals/ai-platform/mlflow-writer-groups/", "git-md:repo-tsdigital-oneplatform-ai-cowork-docs-ai-platform-docs-docs-ai-platform-internals-ai-platform-mlflow-on-databricks"], "expected_keywords": ["GenAIPlatformMLFlowWritersDev", "dbw-aiplatform-dev"], "expected_answer": "The dev experiment ts_ai_observability lives in the dbw-aiplatform-dev workspace (https://adb-1853051426659347.7.azuredatabricks.net) with Unity Catalog schema aiplatform_dev.ts_ai_observability. Write access is granted only through the GenAIPlatformMLFlowWritersDev meta group: create an Entra ID group and ask the GenAI Platform team to add it as a child, never adding groups directly to experiments or schemas.", "notes": "writer-groups table + mlflow-on-databricks Access to Databricks table", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-ai-028", "question": "Is DocStore still the platform I should use for a new customer document ingestion integration?", "lang": "en", "category": "yes-no", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/ai-platform-docs/documents-and-rag/customer-documents/legacy-docstore/"], "expected_keywords": ["DocStore", "TS Documents", "doc-store.yaml"], "expected_answer": "No. DocStore is a legacy document management platform kept only for existing integrations; new integrations must use TS Documents. DocStore uses the generic doc-store.yaml configuration, has no authorization enforcement (TS Documents uses OPA Policy Manager) and does not support structural segmentation.", "notes": "Legacy Platform warning + Key differences table", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-data-001", "question": "Which JSON Schema draft version should I use when defining a Hermes 2.0 event schema, and why that one?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/module/hermes/record-schema-definition/"], "expected_keywords": ["draft-07"], "expected_answer": "Hermes uses JSON Schema draft-07: it is the most widely used draft, newer drafts only add complex validation options that are not needed, and many code libraries are not updated for the most recent drafts, so draft-07 is the more conservative choice with good validation capabilities.", "notes": "Section 'Json schema > Drafts'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-data-002", "question": "How do I build the CloudEvent type value for a record I want to publish on Hermes? What parts must the name contain and what casing?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/module/hermes/record-schema-definition/"], "expected_keywords": ["kebab-case", "com.teamsystem", "v1"], "expected_answer": "The type follows com.teamsystem.<business>.<domain>.<subdomain>.<record-type>.<record-name>.<version>, e.g. com.teamsystem.fintech.banklink.platform.event.payment-transaction-hint-updated.v1. record-type is entity, event or schema; the record name must be kebab-case with no dots (for EventRecords entity + past-tense verb, like invoice-sent-to-sdi); the version is a lowercase v followed by a number (v1, v2). Sub-domain is 'platform' for once-only platform services.", "notes": "Sections 'Cloud-Event: Type' and 'Give it a name'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-data-003", "question": "Nel definire uno schema JSON per Hermes conviene lasciare additionalProperties al valore di default? E vale anche per gli oggetti annidati?", "lang": "it", "category": "yes-no", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/module/hermes/record-schema-definition/"], "expected_keywords": ["additionalProperties", "Closed Content Model"], "expected_answer": "No: se in dubbio si raccomanda di impostare additionalProperties a false (Closed Content Model), perché il default true (Open Content Model) accetta campi non dichiarati e cambia le regole di compatibilità dello schema. L'impostazione non si eredita: ogni oggetto annidato deve dichiarare esplicitamente il proprio additionalProperties, altrimenti quel livello diventa un Open Content Model.", "notes": "Sections 'AdditionalProperties' and 'Important Reminder: Nested Objects'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-data-004", "question": "What Kubernetes deployment constraints must the Hermes outbox relay respect?", "lang": "en", "category": "list", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/module/hermes/hermes-relay/"], "expected_keywords": ["replicas: 1", "Recreate", "KEDA"], "expected_answer": "Exactly one replica (replicas: 1), deployment strategy type Recreate so the old pod is terminated before the new one starts, and no autoscaling at all: KEDA or any horizontal/vertical autoscaling must not be used. Geo-replication is not supported, so in production the ArgoCD ApplicationSet must contain only one cluster. Suggested resources are 500Mi request / 1500Mi memory limit with JAVA_OPTS set.", "notes": "Section 'How to install'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-data-005", "question": "If the relay already has a poison message in the deadletter table for a given key, what happens to the next record with that same key, and when does the relay stop emitting altogether?", "lang": "en", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/module/hermes/hermes-relay/"], "expected_keywords": ["SkipOnSameDlqKey", "EMIT_STRATEGY_SKIPONSAMEDLQ_MAX_KEYS", "500"], "expected_answer": "With the default emit strategy SkipOnSameDlqKey, a record whose key already has a deadletter is also sent to the DLQ so records are not emitted out of order. Emission stops when EMIT_STRATEGY_SKIPONSAMEDLQ_MAX_KEYS (default 500) distinct keys are reached; to proceed you must fix the DLQ entries or raise the value. The alternative strategy AlwaysEmit ignores the DLQ; the strategy is set via the EMIT_STRATEGY env var.", "notes": "Section 'Emit strategies'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-data-006", "question": "In che unità va scritta la colonna outbox_timestamp della tabella outbox letta dal relay Hermes?", "lang": "it", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/module/hermes/hermes-relay/"], "expected_keywords": ["outbox_timestamp", "milliseconds"], "expected_answer": "outbox_timestamp è un bigint che deve contenere uno Unix timestamp in millisecondi (13 cifre, es. 1715683560123), non in secondi (10 cifre): è usato per ordinamento, filtri e retry e in secondi porta a comportamenti incoerenti. Si ottiene ad esempio con Instant.now().toEpochMilli() in Java, Date.now() in JavaScript o int(datetime.now(timezone.utc).timestamp() * 1000) in Python.", "notes": "Section 'Outbox Tables > Columns'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-data-007", "question": "Which values are accepted for tenantKey when submitting a Hermes backfill, and is consumerParam mandatory?", "lang": "en", "category": "list", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/module/hermes/hermes-backfill/"], "expected_keywords": ["itemId", "workspaceId", "4000"], "expected_answer": "tenantKey must be one of itemId, workspaceId or kind. consumerParam is optional free-form text with a maximum length of 4000 characters, while topicName (the historical topic), tenantValue, idempotencyKey, requester, rangeStart and rangeEnd are required.", "notes": "Section 'Submit a backfill > Request body'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-data-008", "question": "After a backfill finishes, how can my consumer tell apart the records that were produced for its own request on the historical topic?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/module/hermes/hermes-backfill/"], "expected_keywords": ["backfillRequester", "backfillConsumerParam"], "expected_answer": "The DataLake propagates the submit values as Kafka message headers on the historical-topic records: backfillRequester (equal to the submitted requester) and backfillConsumerParam (equal to the submitted consumerParam, empty if not provided). The consumer filters for records whose backfillRequester matches its own identity and reads back its context from backfillConsumerParam; no other backfill-specific headers are guaranteed.", "notes": "Sections 'Consumer-owned parameters' and 'Consume side: backfill Kafka headers'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-data-009", "question": "Che differenza c'è tra un EntityRecord e un EventRecord in Hermes 2.0?", "lang": "it", "category": "comparison", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/module/hermes/hermes-records/"], "expected_keywords": ["EntityRecord", "EventRecord", "tombstone"], "expected_answer": "Un EntityRecord (state-focused) rappresenta lo stato corrente, l'ultimo snapshot, di un'entità del dominio (event-carried state transfer): non dice perché il dato è cambiato e include implicitamente creazione e cancellazione, quest'ultima esposta come tombstone. Un EventRecord (change-focused) notifica che è avvenuta una specifica operazione di business, va nominato con verbi specifici (es. InvoiceReceived e non InvoiceUpdated) e contiene solo l'id dell'entità e i campi rilevanti per l'evento. Hermes non supporta record request-response.", "notes": "Section 'Type of records'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-data-010", "question": "How many records can I send in one Hermes batch emit call, and what is the difference between the two batch endpoints?", "lang": "en", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/module/hermes/emit-records/"], "expected_keywords": ["1000", "fail-fast", "continue-on-error"], "expected_answer": "The maximum is 1000 records per batch request. /records:batch:fail-fast stops at the first validation or emission error and emits nothing after it, preserving strict order; /records:batch:continue-on-error processes every record and reports both successes and failures. Neither endpoint is atomic or transactional, so partial writes can happen.", "notes": "Section 'Batch API'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-data-011", "question": "Is there a test topic I can use to check that my Kafka consumer can reach Hermes, and what consumer group naming does it require?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/module/hermes/dummy-topic/"], "expected_keywords": ["tracked-animal", "ts-dp-hermes-tools-"], "expected_answer": "Yes, the dummy topic public.com.teamsystem.hermes.tools.faker.entity.tracked-animal.v1 is continuously populated with random records in dev and test (demo and prod only hold static records for connectivity checks). The ACLs on the dedicated consumer API key enforce consumer group IDs starting with the prefix ts-dp-hermes-tools-; the API key is requested via a support ticket to the Hermes team.", "notes": "Sections 'Environment-Specific Behavior' and 'Getting Started'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-data-012", "question": "Quale cleanup policy Kafka viene usata per i topic di tipo entity e quale per quelli di tipo event su Hermes?", "lang": "it", "category": "comparison", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/module/hermes/in-depth-delete-compaction/"], "expected_keywords": ["compact and delete", "delete.retention.ms"], "expected_answer": "I topic Entity usano la strategia 'compact and delete' (compact,delete): la compaction mantiene solo l'ultimo record per chiave e la deletion rimuove i record oltre la retention. I topic Event usano la sola strategia 'delete': i record vengono rimossi dopo il periodo di retention. I tombstone (valore NULL) sono conservati almeno delete.retention.ms per dare ai consumer il tempo di osservare la cancellazione; la compaction è asincrona e non deterministica nei tempi.", "notes": "Section 'Kafka Topic Strategy'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-data-013", "question": "How should I size the partition count of a new Hermes topic for production, and what minimums apply in the test environment?", "lang": "en", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/module/hermes/topic-sizing/"], "expected_keywords": ["4 partitions", "10 MB/s"], "expected_answer": "Compute the desired throughput as AverageRecordSize x RetentionRecordMaxCount / 86400 seconds, divide by the Kafka partition speed of 10 MB/s and round to an even number (invoice example: ~50 MB/s -> 5 -> 6 partitions). If unsure, start from 4 partitions as a production baseline since changing partitions later is hard. In test use half the production partitions but never fewer than 2; for infinite-retention topics used in GlobalKTable joins add about 50% more partitions.", "notes": "Section 'Partitions'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-data-014", "question": "Why did Hermes introduce a custom serializer that strips Confluent's magic bytes, and what is the trade-off of that decision?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "gitlab", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:tsdigital/oneplatform/hermes-2.0/docs:adr/magic-bytes.md"], "expected_keywords": ["DAPR", "AbstractKafkaJsonSchemaSerializer", "Avro"], "expected_answer": "Confluent's JSON Schema SerDe prepends a magic byte plus a 4-byte schemaId that DAPR's Kafka PubSub binding (and e.g. the MongoDB Kafka Connector) cannot handle, crashing consumers. The ADR (status Proposed) chose Option 1: extend AbstractKafkaJsonSchemaSerializer to skip the magic bytes in the body and put the schemaId in Kafka headers, keeping producer-side schema validation. It is an intermediate 'OOP hack' with technical debt and risk of divergence from Confluent; migrating to Avro (Option 2) is the long-term option to evaluate.", "notes": "ADR 'Solving the magic bytes issue'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-data-015", "question": "Quale modalità di compatibilità degli schemi ha scelto il team Hermes per i topic, e perché ha scartato FORWARD e FULL?", "lang": "it", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "gitlab", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:tsdigital/oneplatform/hermes-2.0/docs:adr/suggest-schema-compatibility-mode.md"], "expected_keywords": ["BACKWARD", "FORWARD", "Kafka Streams"], "expected_answer": "È stata scelta la BACKWARD compatibility, abbinata al Closed Content Model (additionalProperties: false) come linea guida di default. FORWARD è stata esclusa perché non permette di consumare i messaggi più vecchi, requisito irrinunciabile per riprocessare dati storici; FULL è impraticabile con JSON Schema (nei test pratici nessuna modifica risulta ammessa) e Confluent indica che per Kafka Streams sono supportate solo FULL e BACKWARD. L'approccio scelto per le linee guida è 'Experimental', l'ADR è in stato Proposed e la strategia di rollout è ancora in discussione.", "notes": "ADR 'Suggest Schema Compatibility Mode' > Decision Outcome", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-data-016", "question": "What is Girino and how does it relate to Hermes?", "lang": "en", "category": "definition", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/module/hermes/hermes-vs-integration-hub/"], "expected_keywords": ["Girino", "Integration Hub", "point-to-point"], "expected_answer": "Girino is the proxy component of Integration Hub, installed on-premises next to TeamSystem management software: it handles acquisition, encryption, signing and secure transfer of files over the internet and talks to the application through a locally exposed REST API. It is not part of Hermes: Hermes is a cloud-native store of business events in an application-agnostic format with an event catalog, whereas Integration Hub (created in 2018) is a bus for bidirectional point-to-point exchange of messages, often large files, between on-prem applications and cloud components.", "notes": "Section 'Feature Comparison'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-data-017", "question": "Come sono distinti i domini dati in TeamSystem e in quale dominio finiscono i dati provenienti da TS Studio?", "lang": "it", "category": "definition", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "git-md", "expected_source_ids": ["git-md:repo-oneplatform-tsdataplatform-data-governance-ts-dataplatform-datagovernance-documentation-docs-domains"], "expected_keywords": ["Finance - Accounting", "City Map"], "expected_answer": "I domini sono contesti ispirati al Domain-Driven Design allineati alle business capability della TS City Map, non ai singoli prodotti, per resistere a rinomine, acquisizioni e riorganizzazioni. Si distinguono domini interni (dati da sistemi corporate o processi interni, es. HR, Sales, FinOps, Biosphere, Data Platform) e domini esterni (dati generati e usati dai clienti tramite i prodotti, es. Finance-Accounting, Tax, HRS, Hospitality, Trust & Cyber). Non esiste un dominio 'TS Studio' o 'Commercialisti in Cloud': quei dati rientrano in 'Finance - Accounting'. I domini sono definiti centralmente dal team Data Governance.", "notes": "Intro and 'List of domains currently mapped'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-data-018", "question": "Which tools does the MCP Text2SQL server expose, and what kind of SQL is off limits?", "lang": "en", "category": "list", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "git-md", "expected_source_ids": ["git-md:repo-oneplatform-tsdataplatform-data-governance-ts-dataplatform-datagovernance-documentation-docs-intelligence-system-intelsys-text2agent-mcp"], "expected_keywords": ["query_data", "poll_data"], "expected_answer": "Two tools: query_data (async submit of a natural-language question, returns a signed query_id bound to the caller) and poll_data (polls until completion and returns status, data, error). Only read-only single-statement analytical queries are supported (aggregations, filters, GROUP BY, joins, window functions); DML (INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE/MERGE), DDL (CREATE/DROP/ALTER), arbitrary user-provided SQL and multi-statement execution are out of scope. Hallucinated table or column names are rejected before execution.", "notes": "Section '2. MCP surface'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-data-019", "question": "Che convenzione di naming devono seguire i campi di un Data Product e come si riconoscono i campi tecnici?", "lang": "it", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "git-md", "expected_source_ids": ["git-md:repo-oneplatform-tsdataplatform-data-governance-ts-dataplatform-datagovernance-documentation-docs-dev-journey-12a-dp-policy"], "expected_keywords": ["camelCase", "(METADATA)"], "expected_answer": "I nomi dei campi sono in inglese, in camelCase, con il solo set di caratteri ^[0-9a-zA-Z]+$, e seguono la struttura Prime [+ Qualifier] + Class (es. customerId, orderDate, taxAmountTotal); gli acronimi come ID, GUID, ERP fanno eccezione e le abbreviazioni criptiche vanno evitate. I campi tecnici (system metadata) iniziano con l'underscore '_', per il resto seguono il camelCase e la loro descrizione è prefissata con '(METADATA)', es. _silverUpdateTimestamp o _deletedFlag.", "notes": "Sections 'Field Name' and 'Technical Fields'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-data-020", "question": "What naming conventions does the Witboost Hermes Producer component enforce for the service account and the topic prefix ACL?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "git-md", "expected_source_ids": ["git-md:repo-oneplatform-tsdataplatform-data-governance-ts-dataplatform-datagovernance-documentation-docs-solution-witboost-hermes-producer"], "expected_keywords": ["ts-dp-<domain>-<solution>-w", "public.com.teamsystem.streaming", "wb-user-hermes-name"], "expected_answer": "The service account (producer/write type) is named ts-dp-<domain>-<solution>-w and the target topic prefix ACL is public.com.teamsystem.streaming.<domain>.<solution>., covering all topics of that solution in the domain; domain and solution are lowercase alphanumeric with no spaces. There can be only one Hermes Producer per Solution in a domain, secret names must differ across dev/test/prod, and before deploying the Witboost user header wb-user-hermes-name must be set to name.surname in profile settings.", "notes": "Sections 4, 5 and 9", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-data-021", "question": "Devo far pubblicare la mia applicazione su Hermes: che convenzione ha il nome del topic e quale permesso devo chiedere nel token M2M?", "lang": "it", "category": "procedural", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "git-md", "expected_source_ids": ["git-md:repo-oneplatform-tsdataplatform-data-governance-ts-dataplatform-datagovernance-documentation-docs-hermes-on-boarding"], "expected_keywords": ["audience", "HERMES:WRITE", "M2M"], "expected_answer": "Il topic segue <audience>.com.teamsystem.streaming.<domain>.<solution>.<message-type>.<message-name>.<version>, con audience 'internal' o 'public', message-type 'entity' o 'event' e versione v1, v2... Il token M2M si richiede via ticket sul portale di supporto, uno per ciascun ambiente (DEV, TEST, PROD), indicando il claim HERMES:WRITE; l'identificativo generato va comunicato al team Hermes tramite il team Enablement, insieme a service account, ACL, retention, partizioni e JSON Schema. Le applicazioni on-premises devono passare da Integration Hub e in quel caso il ticket lo apre direttamente il team Hermes.", "notes": "Section 'On boarding process'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-data-022", "question": "My Hermes Output Port deployment fails on the partition count policy: what is the limit and how do I fix a topic that is already deployed?", "lang": "en", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "git-md", "expected_source_ids": ["git-md:repo-oneplatform-tsdataplatform-data-governance-ts-dataplatform-datagovernance-documentation-docs-hermes-op"], "expected_keywords": ["ERROR", "parameters.yaml"], "expected_answer": "The deploy-time 'Partitions number cap' policy (severity ERROR, blocking) requires the partition count to be equal or lower than 2 in both the dev and test Hermes environments. To fix an existing topic: consume and migrate any data you need first (reducing partitions deletes and recreates the topic, unconsumed messages are lost), undeploy the non-compliant component from the Witboost Development environment via Advanced Provisioning, open the component's source view (<> icon) and edit parameters.yaml in the git repository, then redeploy.", "notes": "Sections 'Topic partitions number cap' and 'Lowering partitions number' migration guide", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-data-023", "question": "At what similarity score does the Witboost glossary check flag a field, and does it block the publication of the Data Product?", "lang": "en", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "git-md", "expected_source_ids": ["git-md:repo-oneplatform-tsdataplatform-data-governance-ts-dataplatform-datagovernance-documentation-docs-glossary-similarity-policy"], "expected_keywords": ["0.8", "non-blocking"], "expected_answer": "The Glossary Similarity Policy computes a 0-1 similarity score for each field of the SQL output ports against the enterprise glossary; a score greater than or equal to 0.8 means the field is highly similar to a glossary attribute and should be renamed (e.g. VATId -> VATIdentifierId, score 0.95). The policy is non-blocking: it raises a WARNING but does not prevent publication. It runs only at publication/update time (not retroactive) and returns an error if the Data Product has no SQL output ports.", "notes": "Sections 'Scoring Interpretation' and 'Policy Outcome'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-data-024", "question": "Come devo creare il gruppo Entra ID del mio team perché venga sincronizzato nel Marketplace Witboost, e che nomi devono avere i gruppi?", "lang": "it", "category": "procedural", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "git-md", "expected_source_ids": ["git-md:repo-oneplatform-tsdataplatform-data-governance-ts-dataplatform-datagovernance-documentation-docs-groups"], "expected_keywords": ["#witboost", "Security", "DataEngineersDev"], "expected_answer": "Dal portale Azure crea un gruppo di tipo Security con membership Assigned; la descrizione deve contenere '#witboost', altrimenti non viene sincronizzato nel Marketplace. Il nome indica team e ruolo/dominio: per chi produce dati 4 gruppi [Team][Domain]DataEngineersDev/Demo/Test/Prod (owner: il Data Product Owner), per chi consuma [Team][Role]Dev/Demo/Test/Prod, es. SalesAnalyticsBIEngineersProd. Solo i membri (non gli owner) ricevono i permessi, i gruppi sono sincronizzati automaticamente su Databricks e il gruppo Databricks va attivato con un primo utilizzo.", "notes": "Section 'Create your EntraID group'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-data-025", "question": "How do I get a Hermes topic ingested into Databricks using the centralized ingestion tool, and where does the data land?", "lang": "en", "category": "procedural", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "git-md", "expected_source_ids": ["git-md:repo-oneplatform-tsdataplatform-data-governance-ts-dataplatform-datagovernance-documentation-docs-dev-journey-17-centralized-hermes-data-ingestion"], "expected_keywords": ["provisioning/flow_configs", "PAUSED", "raw_"], "expected_answer": "Create a branch from MAIN in the ts-dataplatform-shared-databricks-ingestion-hermes repository and add a YAML under provisioning/flow_configs/<domain>/<solution>.yaml (all topics of a solution in one file), open a Merge Request to MAIN assigning a Data Platform Team reviewer, and hand over the Hermes API key/secret referenced in the YAML for the platform key vault; the platform engineer merges and runs the Terraform deploy. Data lands in the dataplatform_raw_ENV catalog, in a domain_solution schema with one raw_<entity_name> table and a dedicated Spark streaming pipeline per topic. All four environments (DEV, TEST, DEMO, PROD) are mandatory: topics not yet active in an environment are configured as PAUSED.", "notes": "Sections 'Repository', 'Highlights' and 'Workflow'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-data-026", "question": "Can I attach more than one row-level security function to a Databricks output port in Witboost?", "lang": "en", "category": "yes-no", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "git-md", "expected_source_ids": ["git-md:repo-oneplatform-tsdataplatform-data-governance-ts-dataplatform-datagovernance-documentation-docs-resource-witboost-witboost-databricks-security-function"], "expected_keywords": ["at most one", "SET ROW FILTER", "SET MASK"], "expected_answer": "No: an Output Port can be associated with at most one RLS function (row filter), applied in the Liquibase SQL with ALTER TABLE <table> SET ROW FILTER <function> ON (...), whereas it can have multiple CLS/column-masking functions, one per column, applied with ALTER TABLE ... ALTER COLUMN <col> SET MASK <function>. The functions are created with the 'Databricks Workload - Function' component, and a security function cannot reference tables that are themselves protected by a row filter or column mask (nested security is not supported).", "notes": "Intro and 'Usage > Steps', 'Limitations'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-data-027", "question": "Which domains does FP&A treat as core domains under strict metric monitoring?", "lang": "en", "category": "list", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "git-md", "expected_source_ids": ["git-md:repo-oneplatform-tsdataplatform-data-governance-ts-dataplatform-datagovernance-documentation-docs-metrics"], "expected_keywords": ["FP&A", "Contract & Licence Management", "Procurement"], "expected_answer": "Contract & Licence Management, Customer Relationship, Finance Administration, HR, Marketing, Procurement and Sales. Each core domain has a dedicated FP&A representative supporting metric definition, and strategically important metrics are jointly monitored by FP&A and Data Governance, who periodically review dashboards and metrics published in the Marketplace.", "notes": "Section 'Strictly monitored core domains'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-data-028", "question": "Per un nuovo caso d'uso di interrogazione dati in linguaggio naturale devo usare Genie o il server MCP Text-to-SQL? E il vecchio Data Agent è ancora supportato?", "lang": "it", "category": "comparison", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "git-md", "expected_source_ids": ["git-md:repo-oneplatform-tsdataplatform-data-governance-ts-dataplatform-datagovernance-documentation-docs-intelligence-system-intelsys-guidelines-dataagent"], "expected_keywords": ["Genie", "MCP Text-to-SQL", "Deprecated"], "expected_answer": "Genie va usato per utenti corporate interni (email @teamsystem.com) con esigenze semplici di data querying, autorizzazione via RLS di Unity Catalog, senza multi-agente né metering. Il server MCP Text-to-SQL sull'AI Assistant Orchestrator è lo standard per prodotti rivolti ai clienti (utenti autenticati TSID), casi con policy OPA per la row-level security (boolean o fragment), orchestrazione multi-agente e query/join su tabelle di più Data Product. Il Data Agent v1 (DatabricksLLMTool con Security Columns) è deprecato e non più supportato: i nuovi casi d'uso devono usare l'approccio MCP Text-to-SQL.", "notes": "Guidelines - Data Querying Tools", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-data-029", "question": "ADR0008 says Hermes does not keep the full history in Kafka and relies on the data lake for reprocessing. Which component do I actually call today to get expired records back, and where do they end up?", "lang": "en", "category": "multi-hop", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0008_hermes_architecture.md", "devportal:default/module/hermes/hermes-backfill/"], "expected_keywords": ["Kappa", "Hermes Backfill Orchestrator", "historical topic"], "expected_answer": "ADR0008 (Kappa Architecture, accepted) states that Hermes keeps only a sufficiently large persistence window in Kafka and data is reloaded from the data lake, without transformation, when reprocessing is needed. The component that implements this is the Hermes Backfill Orchestrator: you POST to /api/v1/backfills with the historical topic name (not the live topic), tenantKey/tenantValue, a rangeStart/rangeEnd window, requester and idempotencyKey; it authorizes the caller (hermes:backfill:v1:job.trigger), starts the DataLake (Databricks) run that reconstructs the records onto the DataProduct historical topic, and returns a trackingToken to poll with GET /api/v1/backfills/{trackingToken} until SUCCESS or FAILED.", "notes": "ADR0008 'Data reprocessing and backfill' + Hermes Backfill 'Where Hermes Backfill fits' and 'Submit a backfill'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-data-030", "question": "Our transactional service needs data from a consumer-aligned data product. Which output port should we consume, and what do we need to do to get onboarded as a consumer?", "lang": "en", "category": "multi-hop", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "adr", "expected_source_ids": ["gitlab:oneplatform/adrs:Platform/ADR0022_data_product_consumption_guidelines.md", "devportal:default/module/hermes/getting-started-consumers/"], "expected_keywords": ["support ticket", "consumer group prefix", "escapeHeaders"], "expected_answer": "Per ADR0022, applications/services with transactional, near-real-time needs should prefer the Hermes output port (decoupling through platform-enforced schema evolution, push semantics, minimal latency, reusability), while analytical workloads use Databricks; the criteria of decoupling, integration complexity, read performance and reusability must be weighed, and a Databricks choice for an application must be justified. To consume from Hermes, open a support ticket describing the use case and the topics you need; the Hermes team provides an API key/secret and a consumer group prefix to which you append a unique identifier. If the consumer uses DAPR, the subscription component must set escapeHeaders to \"true\" so the __value_schema_id header is not dropped.", "notes": "ADR0022 'Decision' + Getting started consumers 'Prerequisites' and 'Consumer onboarding request'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-core-001", "question": "When TSID issues a token after multi-factor login, which values can appear in the amr claim to show that a second factor was actually used?", "lang": "en", "category": "list", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/ts-id/developer_guide/mfa/"], "expected_keywords": ["amr", "otp", "sms"], "expected_answer": "The amr claim is an array of strings; the MFA-related values are otp (One-Time Password via the TeamSystem Authenticator app), sms (SMS-based MFA) and mfa (MFA performed with a recovery code). Other values are pwd (password) and external (external IdP such as SPID). If MFA is required the application must check that amr includes otp, sms or mfa.", "notes": "Section 'Accepted Formats for amr Claim' and 'Validating the amr Claim'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-core-002", "question": "Se avvio la rotazione del client secret su TSID, quanti secret validi possono coesistere e quali sono le scadenze del secret vecchio e di quello nuovo?", "lang": "it", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/ts-id/developer_guide/client_secret_rotation/"], "expected_keywords": ["RotateSecret", "180 days", "5 days"], "expected_answer": "La rotazione avviene tramite l'API RotateSecret. Possono coesistere al massimo 3 secret validi; il secret corrente scade 5 giorni dopo la richiesta (solo la prima volta che si avvia la rotazione) e il nuovo secret scade dopo 180 giorni. L'API e' protetta da un rate limiter: massimo 5 richieste in 12 ore.", "notes": "Sections 'Rotation Details' and 'API Call Protection'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-core-003", "question": "In the TSID token exchange with exchange_style=delegation, what extra request parameters can I pass and which additional claims end up in the delegated access token?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/ts-id/developer_guide/token_exchange_flow/"], "expected_keywords": ["delegation_payload", "authorization_details", "act"], "expected_answer": "Besides the base parameters (grant_type urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:token-exchange, subject_token, subject_token_type, scope, client credentials), a delegation request can include delegation_payload (a JSON string with the result of the delegation manager API) and duration (lifetime in seconds, must be positive and lower than the client's configured limits, otherwise the client default is used). The delegated token contains an act claim with the requesting client_id, and, only when delegation_payload is supplied, an authorization_details claim with that JSON and a token_type claim set to delegation.", "notes": "Section 'Delegation Token' (marked as draft)", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-core-004", "question": "Can I revoke a JWT access token through the TSID revocation endpoint, and what does the server answer if the token I send is already invalid?", "lang": "en", "category": "yes-no", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/ts-id/developer_guide/revocation_endpoint/"], "expected_keywords": ["/connect/revocation", "reference type", "200"], "expected_answer": "No: the /connect/revocation endpoint only revokes reference-type access tokens and refresh tokens, sent via POST with application/x-www-form-urlencoded (parameters token and optional token_type_hint = access_token or refresh_token). If the token is invalid or already revoked the server still replies HTTP 200, as required by RFC 7009. The request must carry a valid client_id (public client) or client credentials (confidential client).", "notes": "Sections 'Parameters', 'Example', 'Security Considerations'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-core-005", "question": "How do I call the TSID health check, and how long is the database timeout it uses internally?", "lang": "en", "category": "procedural", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/ts-id/developer_guide/healthcheck_enpoint/"], "expected_keywords": ["/health/ready", "X-API-KEY", "3 seconds"], "expected_answer": "Make a GET call to /health/ready (e.g. https://identity-stage.teamsystem.com/health/ready) passing an environment-specific X-API-KEY header, otherwise you get 401. A healthy response is HTTP 200 with status Healthy and a Database component check; an unhealthy one is 503 Service Unavailable. The timeout on the database connection and queries is set to 3 seconds, and the caller should also manage its own HTTP timeout.", "notes": "Whole document; keys per environment DEV/STAGE/PROD are listed", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-core-006", "question": "Quanto dura la sessione utente (cookie) su TeamSystem ID v3 e quali sono i casi in cui viene terminata?", "lang": "it", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/ts-id/developer_guide/user_session/"], "expected_keywords": ["12 hours", "/connect/endsession"], "expected_answer": "Il cookie di sessione di TSID v3 dura 12 ore. La sessione termina quando un client chiama l'endpoint /connect/endsession (RP-Initiated Logout) oppure quando i cookie scadono naturalmente in base alla loro durata configurata.", "notes": "Section 'Session Lifetime and Termination'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-core-007", "question": "In a resource server protected by TSID scopes, when should I return 401 versus 403, and what scope naming pattern does the guide recommend?", "lang": "en", "category": "comparison", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/ts-id/developer_guide/api_resources_and_scopes/"], "expected_keywords": ["403 Forbidden", "401 Unauthorized", "CompanyRegistry.Read"], "expected_answer": "Return 401 Unauthorized when the token is missing or invalid (bad signature, expired) and 403 Forbidden when the token is valid but lacks the required scope or has the wrong audience (aud). The recommended naming pattern is action-based, <Resource>.<Action> in PascalCase, e.g. CompanyRegistry.Read, CompanyRegistry.Write, CompanyRegistry.Admin; start with medium-grained scopes and always validate both scope and audience server-side.", "notes": "Sections 'Scope Naming Patterns', 'Scope Validation in APIs', 'Error Handling'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-core-008", "question": "Which classifier values are allowed when creating a layer in the Item Registry, and which fields become mandatory for each one?", "lang": "en", "category": "list", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/module/item-registry/layer/"], "expected_keywords": ["INTERMEDIARY", "OFFICE", "/api/v3/layers"], "expected_answer": "A layer (POST /api/v3/layers, body with layer.base.identifier/details and parentUuid) must have classifier INTERMEDIARY or OFFICE. For INTERMEDIARY firstName and lastName are mandatory; for OFFICE description is mandatory. The govCode must be unique within the item and valid for the tax region, the parent item cannot be of type PERSON, and success is signalled only by HTTP 202 with the created layer id.", "notes": "Section 'Creating a layer' > Validations", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-core-009", "question": "Come si carica il logo di un'azienda nel registry e che dimensione massima e' consigliata per il file?", "lang": "it", "category": "procedural", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/module/item-registry/logo/"], "expected_keywords": ["/api/v3/items/{id}/logo", "base64", "1 MB"], "expected_answer": "Si fa una POST su /api/v3/items/{id}/logo (registry-write) con Content-Type application/json e body { \"base64\": \"...\" }; il file deve essere un'immagine, la dimensione massima consigliata e' 1 MB e un nuovo upload sostituisce il logo esistente. L'operazione puo' essere eseguita dall'owner dell'azienda o da un utente BACKOFFICE e viene accettata con HTTP 202; il logo si legge poi dal campo logoUrl nella sezione details dell'item.", "notes": "Section 'Writing the company logo'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-core-010", "question": "What happens when the Registry Updater fails to process an event from the Service Bus: how many retries are there and which errors are deliberately not retried?", "lang": "en", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/module/item-registry/developers/registry-updater/"], "expected_keywords": ["DeadLetter", "IllegalArgumentException", "EventParseException"], "expected_answer": "The Registry Updater has no custom retry logic and relies on Azure Service Bus defaults: an exception marks the event as failed and triggers an immediate retry, with a maximum of 10 retries before the event goes to the DeadLetter Queue. IllegalArgumentException (invalid data) and EventParseException (JSON could not be deserialized) are ignored and the event is marked successful, since retrying would not help.", "notes": "Section 'Retry Logic' and 'Ignored Exception'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-core-011", "question": "I'm implementing the claim-ownership flow for an unowned company in the Item Registry: which endpoint finalises the claim with the code the user received, and what does its response contain?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/module/item-registry/developers/write-flows/ownership-management/"], "expected_keywords": ["/ownership/request/complete", "remainingAttempts", "409"], "expected_answer": "The claim is finalised with POST /api/v3/items/{id}/ownership/request/complete, sending { \"code\": \"...\" } in the body. On success it returns HTTP 200 with success (boolean) and remainingAttempts (0 if completed); HTTP 409 means the code is wrong or the attempts are exhausted. The request itself is started with POST /api/v3/items/{id}/ownership/request, which returns 202 with an expiresAt timestamp (409 if the item has no certified contacts).", "notes": "Section 'APIs' and 'Complete an ownership request'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-core-012", "question": "Why does the registry team insist that changes to the events emitted by the Item Registry stay backwards compatible, and which Service Bus topic is involved?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/module/item-registry/developers/technical-overview/"], "expected_keywords": ["b2btopic", "backwards compatible"], "expected_answer": "All registry services publish on a shared Azure Service Bus topic called b2btopic, used by many core services (connections, user, fatturazione, ...), so it is not really possible to know who is listening to which event, including the command events sent by registry-write. Therefore output events must stay as backwards compatible as possible: avoid renaming events, drastically changing a field's type or removing fields; adding new fields should be fine.", "notes": "Section 'Who is processing my Events?'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-core-013", "question": "Quando un item del registry si considera completamente certificato? Quali valori devono avere i campi status e certificationStatus?", "lang": "it", "category": "definition", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/module/item-registry/developers/write-flows/item-validation/"], "expected_keywords": ["certificationStatus", "VALIDATED", "CERTIFIED"], "expected_answer": "Un item e' pienamente validato/certificato solo quando status vale VALIDATED e certificationStatus vale CERTIFIED. I due campi esistono per ragioni storiche: status era il campo originale (flusso a senso unico verso VALIDATED), mentre certificationStatus fu introdotto per richiedere gradualmente la ri-validazione senza invalidare in massa gli item; permette stati come AWAITING_UPLOAD, AWAITING_APPROVAL e CERTIFIED e la de-certificazione.", "notes": "Section 'Status vs CertificationStatus'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-core-014", "question": "Which external data provider does the Item Registry use to find companies that are not yet in the system, and what format check is applied to VAT numbers?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/module/item-registry/item-registry/"], "expected_keywords": ["Cerved", "11 numeric"], "expected_answer": "Search can be extended beyond the internal registry through integrations with external providers such as Cerved. During validation the formats of fiscal codes and VAT numbers are checked (e.g. 11 numeric characters for VAT numbers) plus their compatibility, and conflict detection verifies the identifiers are not already linked to another item.", "notes": "Section 'Main Flow'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-core-015", "question": "What is the difference between the two endpoints exposed by the OnePlatform Authorizer, and what does the second one return?", "lang": "en", "category": "comparison", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/module/policy-manager/user-guide/call-authorizer/"], "expected_keywords": ["/api/v1/authorized", "/api/v1/filters", "UCAST"], "expected_answer": "Both are POST endpoints. /api/v1/authorized is a boolean check: given an action URN (<domain>:<subdomain>:<version>:<rule>), an identity id and a list of resources, it returns a map keyed by resource id with result (true/false) and violations. /api/v1/filters evaluates a fragment policy and returns UCAST filter conditions (e.g. compound and/field lt/gt) that the caller applies as query predicates to fetch only the resources the identity may access. Enforcement of the decision remains the responsibility of the calling service.", "notes": "Section 'Endpoints' and 'Response'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-core-016", "question": "I need a Rego policy that produces a query filter rather than a true/false answer for the Policy Manager. Which package prefix and metadata must it declare?", "lang": "en", "category": "procedural", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/module/policy-manager/user-guide/partial-evaluation/"], "expected_keywords": ["fragments", "compile.unknowns"], "expected_answer": "Policies meant for partial evaluation are fragment policies: the package name must start with the fragments. prefix (e.g. package fragments.example.items.v1.read) and the METADATA block must list the unknown input paths under compile.unknowns (typically [input.resource]). The structure is the same as boolean policies: default authorized := false, authorized if some allow in allows, with allows rules expressing conditions on input.resource attributes; OPA then returns the residual condition on the unknown fields.", "notes": "Sections 'Naming convention' and 'Required metadata: compile.unknowns'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-core-017", "question": "Do I have to ask for a particular scope when requesting a new M2M client for Policy Manager checks, and whose job is it to give that client its permissions?", "lang": "en", "category": "yes-no", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/module/policy-manager/user-guide/client-credentials-flow/"], "expected_keywords": ["Platform.M2M", "Identity Profiles Write", "client_id"], "expected_answer": "Yes: when opening the service desk ticket to create the client you must explicitly request the Platform.M2M scope (digital-m2m-key are deprecated in favour of the client credentials flow). In authorization calls identity.id must be the client_id of the M2M token. Profiling the client (assigning permissions via the Identity Profiles Write service, with scope workspaceId or itemId) is the responsibility of the reference person of the target service, not of the IAM team nor of the team that registered the client.", "notes": "Sections '1. Register a new client' and '3. Profile the client'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-core-018", "question": "Quali sono i ruoli predefiniti gestiti dal Policy Manager e a cosa serve il ruolo Affiliated?", "lang": "it", "category": "list", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/module/policy-manager/concepts/role-management/"], "expected_keywords": ["Affiliated", "Owner", "Manager"], "expected_answer": "I ruoli sono un insieme fisso: Owner (proprietario dell'azienda/contesto, riferimento top per gestione e delega), Admin (capacita' amministrative, tipicamente delegato dall'Owner), Manager (capacita' di gestione su uno scope specifico) e Affiliated. Affiliated serve a mantenere l'appartenenza (membership) di un utente a un'azienda e puo' esistere anche senza permessi operativi su moduli o risorse. I ruoli modellano relazioni organizzative e vanno sempre letti nel contesto di scope/tenancy.", "notes": "Section '2) Available roles (fixed set)'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-core-019", "question": "For an async job that must run on behalf of a user, which call do I make first to register the delegation, and what do I do with its response when I call the TSID token endpoint?", "lang": "en", "category": "multi-hop", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/module/policy-manager/user-guide/delegation-flow/", "devportal:default/component/ts-id/developer_guide/token_exchange_flow/"], "expected_keywords": ["/api/v1/delegations", "delegation_payload", "offline_access"], "expected_answer": "First the External Service calls the Delegation Manager with the user's access token: POST /api/v1/delegations with delegated (service client_id), delegator (user sub), delegatedPermissions (each scoped to a tenancy) and delegationDuration in seconds. The response is an opaque delegation payload that must be forwarded verbatim as the delegation_payload parameter of a TSID token exchange (grant_type urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:token-exchange, exchange_style=delegation, optional duration). The client must have offline_access and the token-exchange grant enabled; the resulting token carries act, authorization_details and token_type=delegation claims.", "notes": "delegation-flow 'Phase 1' + token-exchange-flow 'Delegation Token' (both marked draft)", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-core-020", "question": "How is an ICE deep link URL structured, and how can I avoid the user having to pick an organization when opening it?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "easy", "source_type": "git-md", "expected_source_ids": ["git-md:repo-oneplatform-experience-ice-docs-docs-tutorials-deeplink"], "expected_keywords": ["organizationId", "productCode"], "expected_answer": "A deep link has the form https://app-dev.teamsystem.cloud/{productCode}/{moduleCode}/{page}?param=value, e.g. /myproduct/billing/invoices?year=2024. Adding the ?organizationId query parameter makes ICE set the organization directly and skip the organization selector; since the product code is in the path no product selector is shown either. If the user is not logged in, ICE redirects to login preserving the destination.", "notes": "Section 'URL Format'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-core-021", "question": "Which values can the ModuleType field take when registering a module in the Modules Catalog, and what are the default policyName and ruleName?", "lang": "en", "category": "list", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "git-md", "expected_source_ids": ["git-md:repo-oneplatform-experience-ice-docs-docs-services-modules-catalog-docs-index"], "expected_keywords": ["ONEBOX", "WIDGET", "defaults.allow"], "expected_answer": "ModuleType is an enum with ONEBOX (\"onebox\", a 1F app built with OneBox.run/OneFront.run), APPLICATION (multi-page application), DIGITAL (ex Digital application), COMPONENT (self-contained microfrontend component) and WIDGET (self-contained widget for dashboards). The App Route is required only for APPLICATION and ONEBOX. Defaults are policyName = defaults.allow (accessible to all users) and ruleName = defaults.always.", "notes": "Section 'Fields of a Module' > ModuleType, Policy Name, Rule Name", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-core-022", "question": "In Powerboard che differenza c'e' tra una dashboard di sistema e una dashboard utente, e qual e' la lunghezza massima del nome?", "lang": "it", "category": "comparison", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "git-md", "expected_source_ids": ["git-md:repo-oneplatform-experience-ice-docs-docs-services-powerboard-docs-index"], "expected_keywords": ["userId", "isDefault", "254"], "expected_answer": "Le System Dashboard sono create e gestite da dipendenti TeamSystem, disponibili di default a tutti gli utenti e hanno userId = null; le User Dashboard sono create dagli utenti (clienti TS), personalizzabili, devono essere collegate a entita'/risorse specifiche e hanno userId valorizzato (UUID dell'utente). Il campo name e' obbligatorio con lunghezza massima 254 caratteri (anche description max 254); isDefault indica la dashboard predefinita e ne puo' esistere solo una per coppia prodotto-utente.", "notes": "Sections 'Dashboard Types' and 'Fields of a Dashboard'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-core-023", "question": "What are the steps to turn an existing OneFront app built on @1f/react-starter-sdk into an ICE federated module?", "lang": "en", "category": "procedural", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "git-md", "expected_source_ids": ["git-md:repo-oneplatform-experience-ice-docs-docs-tutorials-migration-migrate-onefront-app"], "expected_keywords": ["@ice/compat-onefront", "remoteConfiguration", "appConfig"], "expected_answer": "1) Move the OneBox.run configuration from src/main.tsx into an appConfig.ts file and call OneBox.run(appConfig) in main.tsx. 2) Create src/remote-config.tsx that exports remoteConfiguration({ component: federationConfig }) from @ice/compat-onefront, wrapping appConfig (adding e.g. settings.one.rest.proxy.baseUrl '/proxy'). 3) Add the @ice registry to .npmrc (nexus.ts-paas.com ts-platform-npm with auth token) and install @module-federation/vite, @ice/react and @ice/compat-onefront. 4) In vite.config.ts set base: './' and configure the federation plugin with filename remoteEntry.js exposing './remote-config'. 5) Verify http://localhost:{port}/remoteEntry.js returns the Module Federation manifest.", "notes": "Steps 1-5 of the tutorial", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-core-024", "question": "Which ICE hooks let one microfrontend send messages to another and trigger navigation, and how do I target a specific DOM container when navigating?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "git-md", "expected_source_ids": ["git-md:repo-oneplatform-experience-ice-docs-docs-tutorials-not-exposed-hooks-tutorial-index"], "expected_keywords": ["useEventBus", "navigateTo", "domContainerId"], "expected_answer": "useEventBus (from @ice/react) returns the event bus instance with subscribe(event, handler) returning an unsubscribe function and publish(event, data). useNavigationEvent returns navigateTo({ path, options }), where options.domContainerId names the container to navigate within, e.g. navigateTo({ path: '/widget/analytics', options: { domContainerId: 'widget-container' } }). useWidgetDataEvent provides sendData({ source, target, payload }) for widget-to-widget data, and useIceStore gives access to the global store.", "notes": "Sections 'useEventBus', 'useNavigationEvent'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-core-025", "question": "In production, how long after a company's package expires does the metering data-retention process start archiving and then deleting the data, and how often does the scheduler run?", "lang": "en", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/module/metering/data_retention/"], "expected_keywords": ["ALERT_TIMEOUT_BEFORE_ARCHIVING_IN_SECONDS", "3888000", "120 days"], "expected_answer": "The data-retention-scheduler environment variables define the timings from the STARTED state: ALERT_TIMEOUT_BEFORE_ARCHIVING_IN_SECONDS = 3888000 (45 days, to ARCHIVE_INIT), ARCHIVING_TIMEOUT_IN_SECONDS = 5184000 (60 days, to ARCHIVED), ALERT_TIMEOUT_BEFORE_DELETION_IN_SECONDS = 9072000 (105 days, to DELETE_INIT) and DELETION_TIMEOUT_IN_SECONDS = 10368000 (120 days, to DELETED). SCHEDULER_PERIOD is 3600 seconds (1 hour). The process starts only when all services of the same appId are readonly (READONLY_EXPIRE_DATE_REACHED) or deactivated.", "notes": "Section 'Data retention scheduler'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-core-026", "question": "Nel metering, quali sono gli stati di uno slot (consumo sincrono) e dopo quanto tempo uno slot in cooldown torna riutilizzabile?", "lang": "it", "category": "definition", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/module/metering/consumptions/"], "expected_keywords": ["COOLDOWN", "LOCKED", "6 months"], "expected_answer": "I consumi sincroni sono organizzati in slot. Uno slot viene prima creato in stato LOCKED (lock), poi confermato con il commit in stato USED; puo' essere cancellato tornando FREE. Lo stato COOLDOWN serve a evitare che l'azienda associata allo slot venga rimossa per riutilizzarlo su un'altra azienda: uno slot in COOLDOWN torna riutilizzabile dopo 6 mesi. Le API degli slot sono esposte dal servizio usage-broker.", "notes": "Section 'Introduction' and 'usage-broker'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-core-027", "question": "Which metering database tables do I need to populate to configure a brand-new family of packages with its constraints, services and extradata?", "lang": "en", "category": "procedural", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/module/metering/guides/"], "expected_keywords": ["family_descriptor", "family_service", "service_extra_data"], "expected_answer": "Run a script on the Metering DB inserting: the family in family_descriptor (name, upgrade/downgrade flags, billing cycle start day, multi-purchase, trial, enable_by_user...); constraints in constraint_descriptor (name, synchronous, consumption alert) linked via family_constraint; parent-child links in family_parent (child id, parent id); trial links in family_trial (base id, trial id); services in service_descriptor linked through family_service (extensible, studio/company/building/person enabled), whose generated family_service_id is then used to insert extradata in service_extra_data (name, default value).", "notes": "Section 'Configuration of a new family of packages'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-core-028", "question": "Come funziona il flusso di creazione/attivazione di un'azienda tramite l'Agyo Wrapper? Quante chiamate servono e cosa succede a ogni passo?", "lang": "it", "category": "procedural", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/agyo-wrapper/creazione-attivazione-azienda/"], "expected_keywords": ["create_company", "OTP", "Atoka"], "expected_answer": "L'attivazione e' centralizzata in una sola API (POST /create_company, /create_building o /create_association, con autenticazione software) che va chiamata piu' volte con lo stesso body: la prima chiamata (senza il campo pin) arriva allo step 1 e invia il PIN OTP via SMS; la seconda, con il pin ricevuto, arriva allo step 2 e invia l'email di conferma (solo se l'azienda esiste gia' su Digital); la terza, dopo la validazione dell'email, crea l'azienda sul wrapper e l'item su TS Digital, crea la connessione software-azienda e in modo asincrono la chiave tecnica ADMIN e l'attivazione del pacchetto. Su richiesta del chiamante viene fatta anche la validazione dei dati con Atoka.", "notes": "Section 'Activation company' and sub-sections", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-core-029", "question": "Quando l'Agyo Wrapper deve inviare la mail di conferma per un'azienda gia' presente su Digital, con quale ordine di priorita' sceglie l'indirizzo destinatario e da quale mittente parte?", "lang": "it", "category": "list", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/component/agyo-wrapper/creazione-attivazione-azienda/"], "expected_keywords": ["confirmation_email_overrides", "noreplay@email.teamsystem.com", "user-read"], "expected_answer": "L'ordine e': 1) l'indirizzo nella tabella confirmation_email_overrides se esiste un record per il soggetto; 2) l'email di un OWNER recuperato via API user-read; 3) l'email del soggetto gia' presente sul wrapper con lo stesso CF; 4) l'email di un soggetto con la stessa partita IVA sul wrapper; 5) l'email di un ADMIN via user-read; altrimenti l'invio fallisce. La mail e' inviata tramite NCS con mittente noreplay@email.teamsystem.com e contiene un link che approva o rifiuta la richiesta tramite le API validate_email e reject_email.", "notes": "Section 'Check e-mail confirmation'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-core-030", "question": "According to the Workspace load tests, roughly how many requests per second can a single pod sustain for workspace creation, and what limit was found for the CSL read service?", "lang": "en", "category": "numeric", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/module/workspace/load-tests/LoadTests/"], "expected_keywords": ["K6", "160 requests", "600 request"], "expected_answer": "Tests were run with the K6 framework on a single pod in the Azure test cluster. For workspace creation a single pod handles approximately 160 requests per second with good response times (107 ms median, 43 errors), while at 200 rps the system is beyond capacity (388 ms, 3226 errors). For the CSL service, 600 requests per second is the feasible limit: beyond it the authentication layer causes failures and between 600 and 700 rps response times jump (28 to 485 ms without auth, 35 to 1100 ms with auth). Get workspace scales linearly up to 1000 rps.", "notes": "Sections 'Get CSL auth e no auth' and 'Create workspace'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-core-031", "question": "What are the three types of connection in TS Digital connections v2 and in which status is each created?", "lang": "en", "category": "list", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/module/connections/create-connection/"], "expected_keywords": ["UNVERIFIED", "SYS", "orphan companies"], "expected_answer": "USER connections link two independent items and are created inactive with status UNVERIFIED (PENDING_REQUEST in the validation flow); the managed company accepts or rejects a notification, moving it to VALIDATED or REJECTED. AUTO connections are for managed items without an owner (orphan companies) that never had another manager for the service: they are created already active and VALIDATED (except SDI, which starts UNVERIFIED and needs an Atto d'Affidamento). SYS connections are AUTO-like cases where the orphan item already had a different manager for the same service: created inactive and UNVERIFIED, activated only after the AdA is certified (status VALIDATED, certificationStatus CERTIFIED). Creation is POST /api/v2/connections returning 202; 409 if a manager already exists for that service.", "notes": "Section 'Connection Types'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-core-032", "question": "Come si cancella una connessione in TS Digital e quali conseguenze ha la cancellazione per il gestore e per l'azienda gestita?", "lang": "it", "category": "procedural", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "devportal", "expected_source_ids": ["devportal:default/module/connections/delete-connection/"], "expected_keywords": ["/api/v2/connections/{connectionId}", "202"], "expected_answer": "Si chiama DELETE /api/v2/connections/{connectionId} sul servizio connection-write con gli header standard TS Digital; servono permessi amministrativi sul manager o sul gestito e la risposta positiva e' HTTP 202 con l'id della connessione. La cancellazione e' definitiva e non annullabile: il manager (e gli utenti a cui erano estesi i permessi) perde tutti i ruoli sull'azienda e se non gli resta alcun ruolo non la vede piu'; l'azienda gestita puo' ricevere una richiesta di connessione da un nuovo gestore; un'eventuale estensione di pacchetto viene annullata e, senza altre subscription, il gestito non puo' piu' usare il servizio.", "notes": "Sections 'Deletion request' and 'Consequences of the deletion'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-core-033", "question": "In the new Relations domain, what is the difference between contract-dependent and contract-independent scopes, and when does a scope count as certified?", "lang": "en", "category": "definition", "difficulty": "medium", "source_type": "git-md", "expected_source_ids": ["git-md:repo-tsdigital-core-relations-relations-docs-domain-definition"], "expected_keywords": ["Contract-dependent", "certified", "Univocity"], "expected_answer": "A contract-dependent scope is considered active only while a contract enabling it is active; a contract-independent scope is active from the moment of its creation. Any scope with an associated active contract is a certified scope, and a contract-dependent scope that is not certified must not be considered when evaluating action availability. Scopes can be added at any time; directionality of actions is defined at scope level (A->B, B->A, A<->B) while the relation itself is neutral, and univocity means only one relation can exist between a given pair of entities.", "notes": "Sections '1A. Univocity', '3B. Scope requirements', '5. Directionality'", "should_abstain": false}
{"id": "git-core-034", "question": "When calling the Relations service REST API, how does pagination work and which concurrency header is mandatory on scope updates?", "lang": "en", "category": "factual", "difficulty": "hard", "source_type": "git-md", "expected_source_ids": ["git-md:repo-tsdigital-core-relations-relations-docs-service-specs"], "expected_keywords": ["If-Match", "409 Conflict", "cursor"], "expected_answer": "List endpoints (GET /relations and GET /relations/{relationId}/scopes) use cursor-based pagination per ADR0014: query parameters cursor (opaque token) and limit (default 25, max 100), with a response envelope { data: [...], pagination: { cursor, hasMore } }; GET /scope-types is unpaginated. For optimistic concurrency, GET responses on scope endpoints include an ETag and PATCH/DELETE on scopes MUST send If-Match; a missing or stale value returns 409 Conflict. Relations have no mutating endpoints so they are exempt.", "notes": "Sections '5.3 Common Query Parameters', '5.4 Pagination', '5.5 Concurrency Control'", "should_abstain": false}
